window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 120","paragraphs":["Alloy (3)","Most people knew dwarves as a race that loved alcohol and minerals.","However, that was only half true.","All dwarves were fond of alcohol, but the same could not be said of minerals.","It was simply that their distinctive physiques and innate physical abilities gave them tremendous potential in mineral-related work.","Naturally, this caused dwarven society to develop around the mining industry.","The pace of that development was also unparalleled.","While the other races remained in the Paleolithic or Neolithic eras, the dwarves alone progressed through the Bronze Age and reached the Iron Age.","Some scholars even argued that dwarves had played an enormous role in the development of the other races.","As time passed, the dwarves ceased to be the only race leading civilization.","However, the impact they had made during that era was so great that, even as the times changed, their image as the \"race of alcohol and minerals\" endured.","\"Ooh... Oooooh...!\"","And Gareth, the gallery’s registered user known as Passing Dwarf, perfectly matched that stereotype.","He didn’t merely enjoy alcohol; he loved it, and he possessed extensive knowledge of metallurgy.","That dwarf was currently staring at the sword in his hands and repeatedly exclaiming in admiration.","Shiiimmer!","Blackish-purple stars shone within a green galaxy.","It was a poetic description, but one that perfectly suited the sword Gareth was holding.","The sword had originally been a dull silver, but at some point, it had begun to glow.","’This is the most beautiful sword I’ve ever seen...!’","Gareth was a dwarf who specialized in metallurgy. Naturally, he possessed extensive knowledge of a sword’s quality and performance.","Although his excessive love of alcohol had left him less skilled than other artisans, his discerning eye was as accurate as any master’s.","The mithril-orichalcum alloy Grylls had created—and the sword forged from it—","It unquestionably ranked first among all the swords Gareth had ever seen, far surpassing every other weapon.","\"It still has a few rough edges, but....\"","Honestly, aside from the materials, the sword itself was closer to a mass-produced weapon.","When crafting a delicate tool like a sword, which needed to transmit force efficiently, one generally didn’t use a mold.","Only by forging it directly with a blacksmith’s own hands could one create a sword that was both practical and beautiful.","Therefore, the sword’s craftsmanship couldn’t be described as exceptional.","However, its materials were so absurdly extraordinary that they compensated for every flaw.","Even tools made from solid mithril were nearly impossible to find, yet this sword contained orichalcum as well.","The result resting in Gareth’s hands completely captivated him.","’I didn’t even channel much mana into it. Just how efficient is this thing?’","Mana was the reason the sword displayed such beautiful colors.","Yet despite receiving only a small amount of mana, it shone like a galaxy.","It was the joint creation of mithril, which naturally contained an extremely high concentration of mana, and orichalcum, which possessed a strong affinity for mana.","Gareth had known from the beginning that the experiment was unlikely to fail, but the resulting masterpiece exceeded even his wildest imagination.","’This isn’t the time for that. I need to sharpen the blade.’","After admiring the sword’s brilliant appearance, Gareth came to his senses.","Why had Grylls sent the sword to him?","It certainly wasn’t a gift.","He had sent it so Gareth could assess the alloy’s performance and sharpen the blade.","Gareth had already gained a rough understanding of its performance, so it was time to work on the edge.","’And he can produce a virtually unlimited amount of this....’","As Gareth sharpened the blade, he wondered what would happen if the sword’s existence became known to the world.","Calling it an uproar would be an understatement. Countless people would attempt to steal it.","A solid mithril sword alone would cause chaos, yet this sword contained orichalcum as well.","’Even the legendary masterpieces weren’t this impressive. Not even the Holy Sword.’","The Hero’s Holy Sword, Revolution.","Ares’s blessing had imbued it with divine power, but the material itself was ordinary steel.","’Perhaps the sword the Heavenly Demon gave him might be comparable.’","It was supposedly made from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron, one of the highest-ranked minerals in existence.","It was far rarer than mithril, orichalcum, and adamantium, which were known as the three great rare minerals.","If the Heavenly Demon’s claim wasn’t mere boasting, her sword might be somewhat comparable.","The fact that it was made entirely from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron was already absurd.","’It looks like he plans to give this sword to the Heavenly Demon....’","Gareth abruptly stopped sharpening the blade, his expression clouding with concern.","Was it truly wise to give this sword to someone else so readily?","Of course, the sword unquestionably belonged to Grylls. Gareth had no say in the matter.","He was simply anxious.","How would the world react once this sword’s existence became known?","Was it really safe to give such a sword to the Heavenly Demon, a shut-in who spent all her time fooling around on the gallery?","It was a serious concern.","’She must hold a fairly high position if she possesses a sword made from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron....’","After worrying for a while, Gareth set aside his concerns and finished sharpening the blade.","He also crafted and attached the handle himself.","Thus, the mithril-orichalcum alloy sword, now bearing the touch of a dwarven artisan, was completed.","’What should we call the mithril-orichalcum alloy?’","Since it was an alloy that had never existed before, even deciding on its name was difficult.","Only Grylls could produce it.","Gareth nodded to himself.","It would be better to let Grylls name both the alloy and the sword.","Slice—","To test the sharpness of the blade, Gareth cut through a stack of paper.","Even though he merely touched the blade against it, the stack was sliced apart with ease.","’Since it’s mostly solid mithril, it’s incredibly light too.’","It was lighter than steel while surpassing a steel sword in performance. It also possessed outstanding mana efficiency.","On top of all that, it produced a brilliant glow whenever mana was channeled into it.","’Judging solely by its performance, doesn’t this seem more like a Holy Sword?’","After entertaining that almost blasphemous thought, Gareth immediately sent Grylls a message.","[Passing Dwarf: Hey. I finished sharpening the blade. I attached the handle too, so take it.]","[Wild Grylls: Haha, perfect timing. I just got back from catching the crab.]","[Passing Dwarf: You don’t have to send it immediately. I’m going to eat it for dinner.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay.]","[Passing Dwarf: By the way, are you giving that sword to someone else?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. I’m planning to give it to the Heavenly Demon. She gave me her sword, remember? Of course I should repay her.]","Gareth began typing a message, then stopped.","Grylls had clearly already made up his mind, so Gareth had no place interfering.","Moreover, Grylls was inside the Forest of Four Seasons. Even if the existence of the sword and the identity of its maker became known, he wouldn’t be placed in danger.","Who would dare enter the Forest of Four Seasons merely to obtain that alloy?","Even if someone managed to acquire it, they wouldn’t be able to leave.","Only Grylls could do that.","’I just hope the Heavenly Demon doesn’t make some pointless post about it.’","Although she posted less frequently now that she was busy working as a junior moderator, she used to flood the gallery with pointless posts.","Hoping that the sword’s existence would remain secret for as long as possible, Gareth sent another message.","[Passing Dwarf: This is fucking ridiculous, hahaha.]","It was absurd, but it was undeniably true. Gareth let out a hollow laugh.","Only Grylls could give an answer like that. Whenever Gareth heard such things from him, he experienced a strange feeling.","[Passing Dwarf: Are you planning to give one to anyone else?]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know. Maybe I’ll only make one for myself. Though I might reconsider if someone offers me a suitable trade.]","[Passing Dwarf: Be as careful as possible about who you give one to. That sword is far too good. It could cause a bloodbath.]","[Wild Grylls: It’s that impressive?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah, it’s that impressive. It’s an alloy of mithril and orichalcum, for fuck’s sake ;;]","[Wild Grylls: There’s so much of both here that I practically trip over them, so I don’t really understand how valuable they are.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh, and I’m going to make one more sword and a dagger. Can you sharpen them for me? If that’s too much trouble, just attach the handles.]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah, I can easily do that much. But I have one condition.]","[Wild Grylls: What is it? Another crab?]","[Passing Dwarf: No. I’ll give you an ingot mold, so make an alloy ingot for me. I want to keep it as a souvenir.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay. Got it.]","[Passing Dwarf: Oh, and what are you going to call the alloy and the sword?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll let the Heavenly Demon name the sword herself. I’m not sure about the alloy. Mithrilicon?]","[Passing Dwarf: You put absolutely no thought into that name ;; But it actually sounds decent.]","[Wild Grylls: Heh.]","Mithrilicon.","It was certainly an uninspired name, but it suited the alloy well enough.","It wasn’t an official name anyway, so there was no harm in calling it something simple.","[Wild Grylls: Anyway, thanks for helping me. I’ll send you the crab this evening.]","[Passing Dwarf: Okay. Make sure you make that ingot for me.]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll make it right away. I’ll send it with the sword and dagger. By the way, do I need to quench the ingot too?]","[Passing Dwarf: No. Just leave it to cool.]","The conversation ended there. He had probably returned to work.","As Gareth closed his conversation with Grylls, a thought occurred to him.","’That bastard isn’t going to find adamantium next, is he?’","The frightening part was how likely that seemed.","Wi Seorak, the Demonic Brain of the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult and the gallery’s registered user Smart Demon, led an extremely busy life.","He was responsible for countless duties befitting his title of Demonic Brain.","He had been particularly unable to rest lately, ever since the atrocities committed by the Holy Kingdom of Eldorado had come to light.","The relationship between the Central Plains and Eldorado had never been particularly significant, but things were different for other nations.","Many countries had been affected by the Immortal King incident to varying degrees.","While they were embroiled in conflict, the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult had no choice but to devise plans of its own.","Wi Seorak’s primary responsibility was to strengthen the cult’s influence.","Step. Step. Step.","Even if he had possessed two bodies, he still would have been overwhelmed with work. Yet Wi Seorak was currently following a woman.","She had narrow shoulders and hair tied into a single tail. Her dignified black attire radiated authority.","In her hand was a dull silver sword.","’Why is she going outside?’","Wi Seorak was currently following the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","As usual, she had summoned him while he was in the middle of his daily duties.","He had been deeply worried from the moment he received the summons, and now even their destination seemed unusual.","Moreover, she was holding a sword he had never seen before.","Setting aside its blade, judging solely by its shape, it didn’t seem to be a high-quality weapon.","It looked so crude that even a sword made by an ordinary blacksmith would have been better.","’Who gave her that sword? Don’t tell me it was Grylls.’","There was no other reason for her to suddenly acquire a new sword.","Wi Seorak accessed the gallery.","Grylls had only uploaded two new posts since the one he had made that morning.","’Mithrilicon....’","One of the posts explained how he had used a makeshift furnace to create an alloy by mixing mithril and orichalcum.","Naturally, the responses had been overwhelming.","An alloy of true silver—mithril—and true gold—orichalcum.","It was significant enough to turn the entire world upside down.","’Could that sword have been made from it?’","Using his exceptional intellect, Wi Seorak reached a hypothesis.","The sword Yu Sowol was currently holding had been forged from that alloy.","Ordinarily, he would never have entertained such an absurd idea.","However, he had already read Grylls’s post.","The post explained that a dwarf had provided him with a mold and various tools.","Using them, Grylls had crafted a sword for the Heavenly Demon and planned to keep the remaining weapons for himself.","\"Your Heavenliness.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"May I ask why you brought me with you?\"","If she merely intended to test the sword’s performance, she could have done so alone. Yet Yu Sowol had brought him along.","Surely she didn’t intend to reveal her identity as a registered user. She must have another reason.","Yu Sowol answered in an unconcerned voice.","\"Recently, this lady’s benefactor gifted her a sword. However, he told this lady to name it herself.\"","\"A name... you say?\"","\"Indeed. This lady possesses little talent for naming things. Therefore, this lady summoned thee, believing it would be better for thee to name it.\"","\"....\"","She had summoned an extremely busy man merely to name a sword.","Wi Seorak stared at her in disbelief.","But who was Yu Sowol?","She was a being who looked down upon others not merely with her eyes, but with the gaze of heaven itself.","\"Thy face is filled with discontent.\"","\"It is not.\"","\"Do not speak words thou dost not mean.\"","\"My apologies.\"","\"Thy willingness to apologize swiftly is commendable.\"","Yu Sowol casually overlooked Wi Seorak’s disrespect. She genuinely didn’t seem to care.","Just as Wi Seorak breathed an inward sigh of relief, Yu Sowol stopped walking.","\"Hmm? Your Heavenliness, this place is....\"","\"This should suffice.\"","Yu Sowol had stopped at the edge of a cliff.","It was a strange place where only a single towering tree stood.","Countless mountain ranges stretched beyond the tree, creating a truly magnificent view.","’W-What? We were inside a building just moments ago.’","Wi Seorak couldn’t conceal his bewilderment.","Though he was known as the Demonic Brain, he was still a martial artist.","His cultivation was by no means shallow, so he could sense even the slightest flow of qi. Yet by the time he regained his senses, he was already standing atop a cliff.","It was as if they had teleported.","Yu Sowol slowly raised the sword.","Wi Seorak suppressed his confusion and stared at her back.","Shiiimmer!","\"A green... galaxy?\"","When Yu Sowol infused the sword with qi, it began to glow.","The surface of the blade overflowed with beauty, appearing to contain an entire green galaxy.","Yu Sowol merely glanced at the sword’s magnificent appearance without stopping.","Her arm gradually rose until the sword pointed toward the heavens.","Swoosh—","Then she lowered it with extraordinary gentleness.","She didn’t even slash downward. She merely lowered it.","The movement was so light that only the sound of the blade cutting through the wind could be heard.","It was an elegant motion, almost as though she were painting a picture.","Craaaack—","However, the aftermath was anything but gentle.","The tree that had stood tall and straight split down the middle, its two halves slowly separating.","The intact tree had been severed without the sword ever touching it.","’As expected....’","Wi Seorak swallowed as he watched.","He had anticipated it, but Yu Sowol had grown far stronger than before.","With this level of power, she would have no difficulty spreading the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult’s prestige.","\"Hmm.\"","However, Yu Sowol herself appeared dissatisfied.","She stared at the sword and murmured quietly.","\"This is not a particularly good sword.\"","\"What? What do you mean...?\"","\"A sword can only be called a sword if it cuts what its wielder desires.\"","\"...?\"","As he listened to her incomprehensible words, Wi Seorak suddenly sensed something strange.","The landscape visible beyond the vertically split tree seemed wrong.","The first thing he noticed was the clouds.","The clouds, which should have formed a single continuous mass, had shifted out of alignment.","And it wasn’t merely the clouds.","A thin line had been drawn across the very sky.","Everything on either side of that line was misaligned.","Grylls exclaimed in admiration as he gazed at his newly crafted sword.","\"Is it a glow-in-the-dark sword? That’s cool.\"","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 121","paragraphs":["The Beastman (3)","\"Grrrrr.\"","The beastman glared at Baek So-cheon and let out a low growl.","\"Damn it! Because I saved you, that bastard seems to be furious with me now.\"","\"Be careful! His claws are incredibly sharp!\"","\"What do you mean, be careful? You’re supposed to stop him!\"","Whoosh!","The beastman charged at Baek So-cheon.","Thud!","Just before it could pounce on him, Yeom Hwasin’s kick sent it flying into the distance.","\"You bastard! I’m your opponent.\"","Yeom Hwasin stepped in front of Baek So-cheon.","Once he began displaying his true abilities, the situation changed entirely. It became obvious that he had deliberately allowed himself to be driven onto the defensive earlier.","Of course, the beastman was formidable as well. Its claws had managed to leave wounds on Yeom Hwasin’s skin. The final blow Yeom Hwasin had used to create the illusion of danger had even gouged him deeply enough to draw blood. Granted, it had merely damaged Yeom Hwasin’s thick skin, but drawing blood from someone possessing an Indestructible Vajra Body was an extraordinary feat in itself.","Yet despite all that, the ultimate conclusion remained unchanged.","There was still no one in the Murim capable of defeating Yeom Hwasin.","As though proving that fact, a single blow from Yeom Hwasin sent the beastman flying. In the next instant, Yeom Hwasin’s massive body followed it like a shadow.","Smash!","Another merciless blow from Yeom Hwasin struck it squarely in the face.","Its face caved in, but the beastman did not die.","When it crashed to the ground, Yeom Hwasin brought his foot down upon it.","Boom!","The kick struck its chest, yet the beastman still did not die. It thrashed desperately, raking its claws across Yeom Hwasin’s shin.","The frantic struggle was highly dangerous, forcing Yeom Hwasin to leap backward.","The beastman seized that opening and launched itself from the ground.","Realizing that it was losing against Yeom Hwasin, it chose another target. It hurled itself toward Baek So-cheon, driven by an instinctive desire to kill him before it died.","With half its face crushed and the last of its strength behind its charge, the beastman was terrifying.","Just as Baek So-cheon realized he would be unable to evade without using his internal energy—","Grab!","The creature stopped directly in front of him.","Yeom Hwasin had arrived using Shifting Form and Position and seized the beastman by the back of its head.","Forcing its mouth open from behind, Yeom Hwasin shouted,","\"Kill it!\"","Without hesitation, Baek So-cheon drew the Ghost Shadow Sword and plunged it into the beastman’s mouth.","Stab!","The blade pierced through the back of its neck. Its body might have been as hard as steel, but the inside of its mouth was not.","Yeom Hwasin grabbed the protruding blade and swiftly spun it in a circle.","Rip! Slice!","The beastman’s severed head dropped to the ground.","The two men collapsed onto the ground and sighed in relief. Baek So-cheon belatedly expressed his gratitude. Had Yeom Hwasin not intervened earlier, he would have been forced to use his internal energy or suffer a serious injury.","\"Thank you.\"","\"Not at all. Thanks to you, I killed it easily.\"","Each of them had saved the other once.","\"About what happened earlier—what would you have done if I hadn’t saved you?\"","\"I would have become even more handsome.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Wouldn’t a long scar across my face make me look more impressive? I’m the Leader of the Cheukcheon Alliance, yet my face is far too unblemished. Look closely. Isn’t my skin as smooth as a child’s?\"","\"Your skin looks your age, but your mental age certainly is that of a child!\"","\"Don’t be jealous.\"","Baek So-cheon shook his head with a dumbfounded expression.","His gaze fell upon the beastman’s corpse.","\"To think they unleashed a creature like this! They truly are unforgivable.\"","Had they failed to eliminate it, this bloodthirsty creature would have wandered the world, slaughtering everyone it encountered.","\"You’re right.\"","\"What do you mean, I’m right? You’re going to forgive them anyway, aren’t you?\"","\"I must forgive them. If a blade cuts you, you put it back in its sheath. There’s no need to go so far as to break the blade, is there?\"","\"Do you truly wish to unite the Murim so badly that you’re willing to go this far?\"","\"What else should I do? Play the part of a benevolent leader of the unorthodox factions?\"","Baek So-cheon had no reply to that.","He buried the beastman and the two men who had come before it in the same place. They said that enemies from a previous life were reborn as husband and wife. Perhaps the three of them might be born as spouses in their next lives.","\"Why bother burying them? Just leave them there.\"","\"When you have the opportunity to bury the dead, you should do so.\"","\"And who will ever know?\"","\"I’ll know, and so will you.\"","\"This is a world where being kind only brings you losses.\"","\"Isn’t that why I’m fighting you? I’m trying to prevent the world from becoming such a place. I’m going to sleep first.\"","Baek So-cheon lay down.","\"Aren’t you going to sleep?\"","At Baek So-cheon’s question, Yeom Hwasin added several more pieces of firewood to the fire.","\"As you said, sitting here and staring blankly into the flames isn’t so bad.\"","Baek So-cheon fell into such a deep sleep that it almost seemed reckless, while Yeom Hwasin silently watched over him until the campfire burned out.","At last, they arrived at the Flood Dragon Sect.","The carriage slowly approached its main gate in the distance.","\"How many antidotes do we have left?\"","\"One pill.\"","If the Flood Dragon Sect did not possess an antidote, Jong Mujin would die.","\"What will you do if they don’t have an antidote for the blood poison that afflicted Warrior Jong?\"","The Seven Unorthodox Families were an alliance of seven clans. Another sect rather than the Flood Dragon Sect might have used the poison, or they might have entrusted the task to an outsider. In either case, the Flood Dragon Sect might not possess an antidote.","\"They’ll have one.\"","\"Why are you so certain?\"","\"Don’t they say that if three people gather, one among them can be your teacher? Seven of them gathered together, so surely at least one of them was intelligent enough to make the right decision.\"","Although Yeom Hwasin spoke as though he were merely guessing, he probably knew their personalities and dispositions well. After all, he had known that Jeong Gyun had defected to the Frenzied Demon Blade.","He might even have already guessed what decision they had reached.","Pretending not to notice, Baek So-cheon drove the carriage onward.","\"Then let’s find out whether their clever one was as intelligent as you and whether the other six followed him as innocently and obediently as I did.\"","\"Don’t belittle yourself. You’ll soon return to our path as well.\"","Wondering what he meant, Baek So-cheon glanced back through the small window behind the driver’s seat.","Yeom Hwasin merely stared out the window, apparently having no intention of explaining.","The gates of the Flood Dragon Sect stood wide open.","Its sect leader, Yeoh Jeol-saeng, personally came out to the entrance to welcome Yeom Hwasin.","\"Welcome, Alliance Leader.\"","\"Have you been well?\"","The two warmly exchanged greetings. After offering Baek So-cheon a formal greeting as well, Yeoh Jeol-saeng asked Yeom Hwasin,","\"What brings you to our sect without any prior notice?\"","\"I was passing by and stopped because I needed to ask Sect Leader Yeoh for assistance.\"","The two men behaved as if the previous attack—and the fact that one had attacked while the other had been attacked—had never happened.","\"What assistance do you require?\"","\"One of my subordinates has been poisoned with blood poison. Do you happen to possess an antidote that can treat him?\"","\"Then you’ve come to exactly the right place. Our sect happens to possess an antidote that is highly effective against blood poison.\"","\"Haha, what a relief.\"","\"Someone, hurry and bring the patient inside!\"","At Yeoh Jeol-saeng’s command, the Flood Dragon Sect’s warriors came forward and carried Jong Mujin from the carriage.","\"I’ve prepared drinks for you. Please come inside.\"","\"Let’s do that.\"","Yeoh Jeol-saeng guided Yeom Hwasin and Baek So-cheon to the great hall, where a drinking table had been prepared.","The men caught up with one another as though they shared an entirely ordinary relationship. Cups of wine and laughter passed around the table, but in his heart, Yeoh Jeol-saeng traveled through hell and back several times. He had no way of knowing when Yeom Hwasin might change his mind and kill him with a single blow.","However, their punishment for this incident was not death, but something else.","\"I’m considering establishing an elite unit within the alliance composed of promising young talents.\"","\"Ah, I see.\"","A fleeting look of panic crossed Yeoh Jeol-saeng’s face before disappearing.","\"It seems only proper that the proud heirs of the Seven Unorthodox Families should lead these young talents. What does Sect Leader Yeoh think?\"","In other words, Yeom Hwasin intended to bring their children to the Cheukcheon Alliance and hold them hostage.","They had only two choices: accept his demand or go to war with him.","Yeoh Jeol-saeng chose to innocently and obediently follow the will of their one clever man. They had already made an internal decision to accept any conditions Yeom Hwasin imposed.","\"You are absolutely right. My eldest son possesses considerable leadership ability, so I am confident that he will be of great assistance to you, Alliance Leader.\"","\"As expected. Sect Leader Yeoh’s loyalty brings me immense joy. However, I wonder what the others will think.\"","\"I’m certain they’ll be delighted.\"","Now that they had reached the main subject, the drinking session did not continue for long.","\"You must be tired after traveling so far. You should retire early and rest.\"","\"Let’s do that.\"","A subordinate came forward and guided Yeom Hwasin and Baek So-cheon to their quarters. Baek So-cheon quietly left the hall. Although Yeoh Jeol-saeng’s name was also written in his Book of Death, that did not mean he intended to kill him here.","Only after Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin had left did a secret door finally open, revealing the six other family heads.","They had hidden there intending to join forces if Yeom Hwasin attempted to kill Yeoh Jeol-saeng. Each of them cared only about his own family, but there was at least one truth they all understood.","If they divided, they would all die.","Do Jeonggil, the leader of the Heavenly Society who had accurately discerned Yeom Hwasin’s intentions earlier, had once again predicted the outcome correctly. He had expected that Yeom Hwasin would never kill Yeoh Jeol-saeng.","\"He even knew that we were hiding here.\"","\"It certainly seemed that way. He projected his energy in this direction.\"","\"That’s right. I felt it as well.\"","From the beginning, Yeom Hwasin had come here while considering the possibility that not only these seven leaders, but also numerous other ambushers, might be lying in wait.","\"One certainly has to acknowledge his courage.\"","This time, Yeom Hwasin had decisively demonstrated that his courage stemmed from his overwhelming strength.","Cheol Han spoke with an angry expression.","\"Do we truly have to send our children to him?\"","Yeoh Jeol-saeng replied,","\"Now that he has even killed the beastman, we have no choice but to do as he says.\"","\"Is there truly no other way?\"","\"There’s no need to worry. At the very least, he isn’t the sort of man who would kill our children without reason.\"","In the end, they all nodded. Once their opponent displayed such overwhelming strength, they found themselves feeling more at ease instead.","At that moment, Do Jeonggil presented an unexpected glimmer of hope.","\"There is one variable.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Baek So-cheon. I don’t believe he has changed his convictions. He is a man with the blood of the orthodox factions flowing through his very bones.\"","\"Then why is he traveling with Alliance Leader Yeom?\"","\"I don’t know. However, one thing is certain. If anyone ever succeeds in killing Yeom Hwasin, it will be Baek So-cheon.\"","They all hoped that would happen.","Of course, they did not know that their names were written in Baek So-cheon’s Book of Death, or that as their enemy, Baek So-cheon would prove even more terrifying than Yeom Hwasin.","In any event, the rebellion of the Seven Unorthodox Families ended there. None of them had died, but their heirs had become hostages, and if war erupted, they would have to stand at the forefront against the orthodox factions.","Considering that they had attempted to take Yeom Hwasin’s life, this was a reasonably favorable outcome.","\"For the time being, let us restrain ourselves and observe the situation.\"","The seven family heads cupped their fists to one another before departing.","Jong Mujin regained consciousness the next day. After learning what Yeom Hwasin had done for him, he performed a deep bow.","\"I will never forget this kindness.\"","His already profound loyalty deepened even further at that moment.","Through this incident, Baek So-cheon learned many things from Yeom Hwasin. In particular, restraining one’s anger for the sake of a greater objective was something few people could accomplish, yet it was an essential virtue for anyone who wished to achieve great things.","In addition to gaining insights into martial arts, Baek So-cheon was also learning how to govern and command people.","Yeom Hwasin said to him,","\"Now that the troublemakers are out of the way, our journey should continue, shouldn’t it?\"","Baek So-cheon climbed into the carriage first.","\"Let’s go.\"","Yeom Hwasin burst into hearty laughter at his enthusiasm.","\"Hahaha!\"","Jong Mujin once again took the driver’s seat. Although they had not told him their destination, the carriage headed north once more.","No one could stop the road that even the Seven Unorthodox Families had failed to block.","The carriage continued north.","The scenery around them gradually turned white as a snowy landscape began to unfold.","After traveling endlessly northward, the carriage finally stopped at the foot of a snow-covered mountain.","\"You’ll have to continue on foot from here.\"","\"Wait for us here.\"","\"Understood.\"","Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin began climbing the snowy mountain. The desolate area contained neither people nor even animal tracks.","Crunch. Crunch.","Walking through the pure-white snow felt surprisingly pleasant.","Eventually, Yeom Hwasin stopped before a sheer wall of ice that rose like a cliff.","\"Where are we?\"","\"The Northern Sea Ice Palace.\"","The Northern Sea Ice Palace was the most mysterious sect in the Murim. It never involved itself in the affairs of the martial world, and it possessed enough power that no other sect dared treat it lightly.","Given their relentless journey northward, Baek So-cheon had suspected that the Ice Palace might be their destination.","However, he could never have anticipated Yeom Hwasin’s next words.","\"This is where we will restore your dantian.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 122","paragraphs":["The Absolute Prohibition (1)","\"Did you just say that the Northern Sea Ice Palace can restore my dantian?\"","Baek So-cheon stared at Yeom Hwasin in astonishment. Judging by his expression, he was not joking.","\"That’s right. As far as I know, the Ice Palace is the only place capable of repairing your dantian.\"","Yeom Hwasin had surprised him many times before. At that moment, he surpassed all his previous records.","\"Didn’t you say you would restore it only after your martial arts reached the next stage?\"","\"As repayment for saving my life, I’ll restore your dantian first.\"","Baek So-cheon remembered what Yeom Hwasin had said earlier—that he would soon return to their path. He now realized that Yeom Hwasin had been referring to this.","\"Why are you looking at me like that?\"","\"You truly are an impossible man to understand.\"","\"I’m not such a complicated person. Perhaps I seem complicated precisely because I’m too simple.\"","A sudden thought occurred to Baek So-cheon.","When Yeom Hwasin had been endangered by the beastman, had he truly not expected Baek So-cheon to save him?","Could he have been planning to restore Baek So-cheon’s internal energy from that very moment?","Yeom Hwasin was such an unpredictable man that it was impossible to tell what he was thinking.","Looking up at the ice wall, Baek So-cheon asked,","\"Do we have to climb over this to reach the Ice Palace?\"","\"No. We only need to wait here.\"","Baek So-cheon was puzzled.","The Northern Sea Ice Palace stood between the orthodox and unorthodox factions, but strictly speaking, it was closer to the orthodox side. How could it have a connection with Yeom Hwasin?","\"I didn’t know the Cheukcheon Alliance had dealings with the Northern Sea Ice Palace.\"","\"It doesn’t.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I’m saying that the Ice Palace Master and I know each other personally. Officially, the Cheukcheon Alliance has no relationship with the Northern Sea Ice Palace.\"","\"What sort of relationship do you have with the Ice Palace Master?\"","\"You might say that we are destined to fulfill a long-cherished wish.\"","\"Whose wish do you mean?\"","Yeom Hwasin merely gave him an enigmatic smile and said nothing more about it.","\"I hope it’s my wish.\"","\"So do I. However, you should prepare yourself.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"There’s a possibility that restoring your dantian will fail. Even without knowing the details, it obviously won’t be an easy task, will it? If something goes wrong, you might die.\"","Yeom Hwasin lowered his voice as though attempting to frighten him, but Baek So-cheon remained completely unconcerned.","\"That’s your problem. You have far too little attachment to life. But that’s all right. You’ll soon recover not only your internal energy, but also your hope.\"","If anything, Yeom Hwasin appeared more excited than Baek So-cheon.","Although Baek So-cheon remained outwardly composed, his heart was also pounding with anticipation and excitement.","’How will they restore my dantian? If it is restored, what will happen to the internal energy I already possess? Will the two merge, or will I be able to control them separately?’","Of course, as Yeom Hwasin had said, the process would not be easy. The treatment itself might be extraordinarily dangerous, and his recovery of internal energy might be discovered in the process.","However, Baek So-cheon had realized something with certainty during this journey.","To oppose Yeom Hwasin, he needed to restore his dantian. Furthermore, he needed to use that process as an opportunity to grow even stronger if he wished to defeat him.","\"Let me ask you one honest question.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"Why are you trying to restore my internal energy? Don’t give me any nonsense. I want an honest answer.\"","\"If I tell you, what will you do for me?\"","\"I’ll honestly answer one of your questions as well.\"","\"Very well. Then I’ll tell you. I’ve encountered a wall on my path to the next stage. I realized that I cannot break through it using ordinary methods, so I intend to choose an extraordinary one.\"","\"And that extraordinary method is restoring my internal energy?\"","\"If I fight a battle in which I genuinely feel threatened with death, perhaps I’ll be able to break through that wall.\"","Baek So-cheon nodded. If Yeom Hwasin had encountered a wall, that method was certainly worth attempting. It was also something only those at their level could try.","\"Now, is it my turn to ask a question?\"","\"Go ahead.\"","Yeom Hwasin moved his lips as though about to ask something, but soon backed down.","\"I’ll ask when I think of something later.\"","\"You should ask while you still can. You’re old enough to start becoming forgetful, aren’t you?\"","\"Hahaha!\"","They conversed and waited for a long time, but no one appeared.","\"Putting aside the wall blocking your martial arts, don’t you think we should do something about the wall in front of us first?\"","Yeom Hwasin pounded on the ice wall and shouted,","\"Go and deliver this message! If you don’t open it immediately, I’ll smash my way inside! Consider yourselves warned!\"","He seemed convinced that someone behind the ice wall was listening to their conversation.","\"It doesn’t seem as though you’re welcome here.\"","\"Where in the martial world would anyone welcome me?\"","\"Given the situation, will they really repair my dantian?\"","\"I am me, and you are you.\"","\"But this is my first time here as well.\"","\"Did you think restoring your dantian would be that easy? We might have to lie down in front of their Palace Master’s residence and refuse to move.\"","\"I can’t bring myself to tell them to cut my stomach open if they want me gone, so you’ll have to do that on my behalf.\"","\"Leave it to me. Being unreasonable is my specialty.\"","Baek So-cheon chuckled.","Life truly was unpredictable. Who could have imagined that he would one day stand at the entrance to the Northern Sea Ice Palace, trading jokes with the Leader of the Cheukcheon Alliance?","Even after they waited for a long time, no one appeared.","Perhaps Yeom Hwasin had expected this cold reception from the beginning, for he did not become angry at all.","\"How long have we been waiting?\"","\"I believe it has been half an hour.\"","\"We’ve waited long enough.\"","When Yeom Hwasin walked toward the ice wall, Baek So-cheon quickly asked,","\"Surely you aren’t going to smash it simply because they refuse to open the door?\"","\"Why wouldn’t I?\"","Yeom Hwasin infused his fist with internal energy.","\"I’ll smash it on the count of three. One, two...\"","He raised his fist high, appearing genuinely ready to destroy the wall.","At that very moment—","Rumble.","A door opened in the ice wall. It had been concealed so perfectly that they only realized a door had been there after it opened.","A woman dressed in white politely greeted the two men.","\"I apologize for keeping our honored guests waiting. I will escort you to the Palace Master.\"","The woman led them inside. Judging by her swift and agile steps, her martial arts had reached the peak level.","Following her guidance, the two walked down an extremely long corridor.","The walls on either side looked as though they were made of ice, but closer examination revealed otherwise. The corridor had been constructed from stone that resembled ice, and beautiful paintings decorated it throughout.","There were various scenes: an adorable pair of male and female birds perched upon a snow-covered branch, children laughing and playing as they rode sleds across the ice, and a grandparent walking hand in hand with a grandchild through the snow.","Although every painting depicted things commonly seen in a cold region, each scene was filled with warmth.","Yet precisely because of that warmth, the presence of the hidden mechanisms beyond the paintings felt even more deadly. It was the same chilling presence one might sense from only the highest-grade mechanisms inside the Murim Alliance Leader’s residence.","In truth, these mechanisms were likely even more powerful than those of the Murim Alliance, certainly not weaker.","Throughout the history of the Murim, no martial faction had ever brought down the Northern Sea Ice Palace. In other words, the power and potential hidden within this place surpassed imagination.","Despite possessing such strength, its people had never left the Northern Sea and continued to live here quietly.","\"Do you know why they never leave the Northern Sea?\" Yeom Hwasin asked.","\"I don’t.\"","\"Because they live under an Absolute Prohibition forbidding them from leaving the Northern Sea and entering the Central Plains.\"","\"Whose command was it?\"","\"Whose do you think? The useless old generations of the Ice Palace who have already become bones beneath the earth.\"","The woman walking ahead of them quickened her steps slightly. It was clear that the conversation made her uncomfortable.","\"How did you learn about this?\"","\"I heard it from those who wished to leave this place.\"","\"There are people here who want to leave?\"","\"There were in the past, and there still are today. To them, the Northern Sea is nothing more than a vast prison from which they wish to escape.\"","The woman ahead of them visibly flinched again. Her reaction revealed just how sensitive this subject was within the Northern Sea Ice Palace.","Baek So-cheon guessed that the Ice Palace must have its own complicated internal circumstances. After all, even a group of beggars living beneath a bridge would establish a hierarchy and engage in politics. Why would this place be any different?","Fortunately for their guide, Yeom Hwasin said nothing more about the matter.","At the end of the long corridor, they emerged into a garden.","The scenery was breathtaking enough to draw an involuntary gasp of admiration.","Baek So-cheon was genuinely impressed.","In the distance stood the majestic buildings of the Northern Sea Ice Palace. Designed to appear as though they had been sculpted from ice, they were dazzlingly beautiful.","Trees covered in frost flowers surrounded them, while statues carved from ice decorated the grounds. Each was so intricate and beautiful that they were works of art capable of stopping people in their tracks.","The men and women passing through the garden were all dressed in white, and every one of them was strikingly handsome or beautiful. Some were martial experts, while others knew no martial arts whatsoever.","They greeted the two visitors with bright, radiant smiles as they passed. They all appeared happy, as though they were strolling through the gardens of paradise.","Yeom Hwasin stopped and asked Baek So-cheon,","\"What do you sense from them?\"","Baek So-cheon answered honestly.","\"They feel unnatural.\"","\"Exactly! You noticed it as well.\"","There was something artificial about their apparent happiness. It felt as though this joyous scene had been deliberately staged because the two men were visiting.","Even if that was not the case, their happiness did not feel genuine.","Eventually, the two arrived at the Palace Master’s residence.","Martial experts stood in a line on either side of the hall. Every one of them had reached a level ranging from the peak to the transcendent realm.","At their center sat a woman dressed in a magnificent pure-white robe adorned with elaborate ornaments.","She was Seo Bingbing, the current Palace Master of the Northern Sea Ice Palace.","She was far younger than Baek So-cheon had expected. At the youngest, she appeared to be in her mid-twenties, and at the oldest, in her early thirties. Judging by her age, Baek So-cheon assumed she had not inherited the position of Palace Master very long ago.","By contrast, all the experts standing guard around her were older women.","\"Why have you come to our palace again?\"","Her first words were prickly and openly hostile.","Yeom Hwasin grinned at her.","\"It’s good to see you too.\"","At that moment, Baek So-cheon understood.","’Something happened between these two.’","Judging by how she treated her guest, Yeom Hwasin had undoubtedly done something that infuriated her.","\"Our palace is not a place just anyone can enter whenever they please.\"","\"But I’m not just anyone, am I? The friend who came with me is also someone special.\"","Everyone’s attention turned toward Baek So-cheon.","Baek So-cheon cupped his fists toward Seo Bingbing and spoke calmly.","\"I am Baek So-cheon.\"","\"I know who you are. Great Hero Baek, you are a hero of the orthodox factions. Why are you traveling with a villain like him?\"","She openly called Yeom Hwasin a villain without hesitation.","\"As you may have heard from the rumors, I lost my strength and ended up in this state.\"","\"That is truly unfortunate.\"","At Seo Bingbing’s lament, Yeom Hwasin laughed.","\"There will be no need to pity him any longer.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"This man is going to regain his original strength.\"","\"The entire world knows that Great Hero Baek’s dantian was destroyed. How can he possibly regain his original strength?\"","Yeom Hwasin stared directly at her.","\"Because the Divine Physician of Life and Death will treat him and restore his dantian.\"","Seo Bingbing’s expression instantly hardened at the mention of the Divine Physician of Life and Death.","Baek So-cheon, on the other hand, was astonished.","\"He is still alive?\"","The Divine Physician of Life and Death had once been hailed as the reincarnation of Hua Tuo and was considered the greatest physician of his time.","Even Ban Wol-ryang, the Divine Physician of the Murim Alliance, had acknowledged him as the greatest physician of their generation. That alone demonstrated just how exceptional his medical skills were.","However, he had eventually vanished from the Murim, and no one had seen him since. Everyone had assumed he was dead, but it appeared that he had come to the Northern Sea Ice Palace.","Seo Bingbing spoke in a tone as cold as her expression.","\"The Divine Physician of Life and Death is not here.\"","Yeom Hwasin remained relaxed, as though he had already anticipated that answer.","\"The Divine Physician of Life and Death must be here. And he must treat this man.\"","The corners of Seo Bingbing’s lips curled upward as she asked provocatively,","\"Why?\"","Baek So-cheon was hardly the only person Yeom Hwasin possessed a talent for startling.","Words that shocked everyone present emerged from his mouth.","\"Because in return, I will lift the Absolute Prohibition.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 123","paragraphs":["The Absolute Prohibition (2)","Silence descended over the hall.","Amid the heavy silence created by those forbidden words, the first to react was the old woman standing beside Palace Master Seo Bingbing.","She radiated a frost-like aura. She was Shim Nahu, the Grand Elder of the Ice Palace.","\"The Absolute Prohibition is our palace’s most sacred and supreme principle! How dare you spout such nonsense!\"","Had her opponent not been Yeom Hwasin, she would have immediately charged forward and struck him with her palm.","\"Is there really anything absolute in this world?\"","\"What exactly are you trying to say?\"","\"How long do you intend to remain confined to the Northern Sea?\"","\"Throughout the ages, our palace has distinguished itself as the guardian of the Northern Sea. Why would you say such a thing?\"","\"The guardian of the Northern Sea? What exactly is there to protect here? Are you planning to guard the snowmen beside the road?\"","\"Silence!\"","Shim Nahu openly unleashed her killing intent. Yeom Hwasin, however, remained perfectly relaxed.","\"What I’m saying is simple. Stop limiting yourselves to the Northern Sea and become guardians of the Central Plains.\"","Just as Shim Nahu was about to shout at him, Seo Bingbing stepped in first. She spoke calmly to Yeom Hwasin.","\"Alliance Leader Yeom, that is enough. Although you are the Grandmaster of the Unorthodox Factions, I can no longer tolerate your insane ramblings.\"","\"I’ve been called a madman countless times, so perhaps I truly am insane. However, what I just said wasn’t the rambling of a madman.\"","\"Mad people never believe they are mad.\"","Their exchange was tense, but Baek So-cheon noticed something.","Compared to Shim Nahu, Seo Bingbing was not particularly angry.","When Yeom Hwasin had said that he would lift the Absolute Prohibition, Baek So-cheon had seen the expression that appeared on Seo Bingbing’s face. It had contained surprise, excitement, and intense emotion—but not anger.","Everyone had been staring at Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin, so no one else had noticed her expression.","Perhaps believing that he had adequately delivered his declaration of war, Yeom Hwasin changed the subject.","\"Coming to such a cold place has left me chilled to the bone. I need a drink to warm myself. Let’s continue our discussion tomorrow.\"","Seo Bingbing addressed one of her subordinates.","\"They are honored guests. Take good care of them.\"","Shim Nahu, on the other hand, continued glaring fiercely at the two men until they left the hall.","The gazes following them as they departed fell into two distinct categories: extreme hostility and hopeful anticipation.","Yeom Hwasin had been telling the truth.","There were undoubtedly people among them who wished to leave this place.","After leaving the Palace Master’s residence, Baek So-cheon said to Yeom Hwasin,","\"We need to talk.\"","Yeom Hwasin grinned.","\"Why do you think I had them prepare a drinking table?\"","***","\"What are you thinking about so deeply?\"","Na Sarin’s voice snapped Cheon-geuk back to her senses.","\"Ah, I’m sorry.\"","Cheon-geuk hurriedly reached for the wine bottle to fill Na Sarin’s cup, only to realize that it was already full.","The two women were drinking together for the first time in quite a while. Cheon-geuk had been the one to suggest it, yet she was the one distracted by other thoughts.","\"Are you worried about Warrior Baek?\"","Na Sarin understood her feelings better than anyone.","\"Yes. His opponent is Yeom Hwasin, after all.\"","\"That is certainly understandable.\"","\"I think I may regret falling in love with him.\"","\"Do you regret it?\"","\"To be honest, I thought I could walk away from my relationship with him at any time. I told myself that merely experiencing love with such a wonderful man was enough. Even when I first became intimate with him, I refused to attach too much meaning to it. I kept telling myself it was nothing significant and tried to control my feelings. But...\"","\"It isn’t that easy, is it?\"","\"I never knew I was this weak.\"","\"You aren’t weak. You’re strong.\"","\"Strong?\"","\"Of course. A weak person cannot truly love someone. Alliance Leader, keep loving him. That love will make you even stronger.\"","\"Thank you, Elder.\"","The two women had just raised their cups for a toast when a voice interrupted them.","\"May I join you?\"","An unexpected guest had visited the teahouse.","Astonishingly, it was Ak So-gun, the Murim Alliance Leader.","\"Alliance Leader.\"","Cheon-geuk and Na Sarin rose and greeted him respectfully.","Ak So-gun cupped his fists and returned their greeting. Although Cheon-geuk was young, she was still the leader of an organization, while the older Na Sarin was his senior in the martial world.","\"I was passing by when you suddenly came to mind, so I decided to stop in. I hope I haven’t interrupted a private moment between the two of you.\"","Judging by the bamboo hat pulled low over his head, he appeared to have left with only the bare minimum of guards.","\"What greater honor could there be than sharing a drink with the Murim Alliance Leader? Please, come and join us.\"","\"Thank you for saying that.\"","Ak So-gun joined the two women at their table. He picked up the wine bottle and moved to fill Na Sarin’s cup first.","\"Allow me to pour you a drink.\"","\"Alliance Leader, I should be serving you first.\"","\"This is a private gathering. As your junior in the martial world, allow me to pour you a cup.\"","Ak So-gun poured wine for Na Sarin.","If word spread that the Murim Alliance Leader had personally poured wine for an assassin, it would undoubtedly become the subject of all kinds of gossip.","However, Ak So-gun no longer cared.","Once the conflict with the Cheukcheon Alliance had been resolved, he intended to hand the position of Alliance Leader over to Baek So-cheon and retire from the martial world with On Byeokhwa.","After making that decision, he had finally freed himself from the opinions of others.","Looking back, he realized that he had spent his entire life bound by how the world perceived him.","\"Once again, thank you for saving my life in the past.\"","When Ak So-gun mentioned the time she had retrieved the Heavenly Outer Primordial Salve for him, Na Sarin responded modestly.","\"My insignificant talents merely happened to be useful for the right purpose. There is no need to think too much of it.\"","Na Sarin filled Ak So-gun’s cup in return.","The three of them drank together.","Although they were an unexpected combination, the atmosphere was pleasant. Na Sarin possessed extensive experience in the martial world and exceptional insight, allowing her to converse easily with Ak So-gun.","Cheon-geuk quietly drank while listening to their conversation.","After discussing various matters, Ak So-gun asked her,","\"Alliance Leader Cheon, do you know where Warrior Baek went to train?\"","In truth, Ak So-gun had not stopped by accidentally.","Zhuge Hyeon had reported that the Cheukcheon Alliance’s movements had changed after Baek So-cheon departed for training.","Ak So-gun was worried that Baek So-cheon might have become entangled with Yeom Hwasin. Knowing how close Baek So-cheon and Cheon-geuk were, he had come to ask her directly.","Cheon-geuk hesitated.","When Zhuge Hyeon had visited previously, she had lied and claimed that she did not know Baek So-cheon’s whereabouts. Now that the Alliance Leader had come personally to ask, she found herself in an uncomfortable position.","After a moment’s consideration, Cheon-geuk decided she could not lie twice.","\"When the chief strategist visited me earlier, I was unable to tell him the truth. However, I will be honest with you, Alliance Leader. He is currently with Yeom Hwasin.\"","\"As I suspected!\"","Ak So-gun appeared to have expected it to some extent.","However, his expression soon darkened as worry overwhelmed him.","\"This is all because I’m not capable enough.\"","Cheon-geuk drove the point home.","\"That’s right.\"","Ak So-gun flinched and stared at her in surprise. Na Sarin, who sat beside her, also turned toward Cheon-geuk in shock.","’Alliance Leader, are you drunk?’","However, Cheon-geuk was not drunk at all. She emptied her cup before continuing.","\"This happened because you and I are both weak. If we had been strong, would that bastard Yeom have been able to run rampant like this? Baek So-cheon was taken from us because we were weak. If not for him, war would already have broken out this spring. He is holding Yeom Hwasin back on our behalf—no, on behalf of the entire Murim. In that sense, Alliance Leader, this wine is a toast to our defeat.\"","Ak So-gun stared blankly for a moment before giving a hollow laugh.","\"You are right.\"","Who else in the world could speak to him so bluntly in such a situation?","Moreover, he was the Murim Alliance Leader. No matter what happened, everyone politely assured him that it was not his fault.","But now that he thought about it, how much comfort had those words ever provided? They had been nothing more than empty formalities.","Cheon-geuk’s frank honesty, however, was strangely comforting.","\"But let’s not worry too much.\"","Having already spoken so openly, Cheon-geuk continued.","\"I once read in a book that forty percent of our worries concern things that will never happen. It said that less than ten percent of our worries are about matters that truly require concern, but because we spend our time worrying about the other ninety percent, we fail to address what actually matters.\"","She repeated the same lesson about worrying that she had once shared with Baek So-cheon.","After listening to her, Ak So-gun’s expression brightened.","\"You are right, Alliance Leader Cheon. It seems that I, too, have been ignoring the things I should worry about while wasting my time on pointless concerns.\"","The three resumed drinking.","When they had emptied one bottle, Ak So-gun rose from his seat.","\"I should leave now. Thank you for the drinks.\"","\"Please take good care of yourself.\"","Just as Ak So-gun was about to leave, Cheon-geuk made an honest confession.","\"Actually, I haven’t been able to follow the advice about worrying that I just gave you. I spend the entire day doing nothing but worrying about him.\"","Ak So-gun smiled.","\"Isn’t that precisely why we continue reading books? Because the teachings written in them are not easy to follow, we read them repeatedly in an effort to discipline our hearts. Alliance Leader Cheon, may I visit you from time to time?\"","\"You’re welcome anytime.\"","They cupped their fists to one another before parting.","After leaving the teahouse, Ak So-gun walked along the road and gazed at the Alliance Leader’s residence in the distance.","\"Geukan.\"","\"Yes, Alliance Leader.\"","The voice of Chief Guard Pung Geukan answered from somewhere in the air.","\"When I leave the alliance and look around, I see an entirely new world like this. It seems I spent far too much time trapped inside that place.\"","After a brief pause, Pung Geukan answered,","\"Because you remained there, Alliance Leader, countless people were able to live freely in that new world.\"","A smile appeared on Ak So-gun’s lips.","\"Thank you for saying that. Let’s return.\"","With his bamboo hat pulled low, Ak So-gun began walking toward the Alliance Leader’s residence.","Standing beside the teahouse window, Cheon-geuk and Na Sarin watched him depart.","Meeting Ak So-gun had made Cheon-geuk think about Baek So-cheon even more.","\"What do you think he’s doing right now?\"","Na Sarin answered calmly.","\"Judging by everything we’ve seen from him until now...he is probably becoming stronger even at this very moment. And he is undoubtedly leaving an unforgettable impact on someone.\"","Cheon-geuk turned toward Na Sarin and forced a cheerful expression.","\"Then I’ll work just as hard. I’ll train diligently and try to become a positive influence on others.\"","Na Sarin smiled with satisfaction and nodded.","\"I believe you have already influenced someone.\"","***","Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin were drinking together in their assigned quarters.","Baek So-cheon had many questions for him.","\"What exactly is going on?\"","\"Where should I begin?\"","\"Let’s start with the Divine Physician of Life and Death. Why is he in the Northern Sea Ice Palace?\"","Seo Bingbing had claimed that he was not there, but that could not possibly be true. If he were not here, Yeom Hwasin would never have traveled such a great distance.","That, at least, was something Baek So-cheon could trust him about.","\"He has extremely deep ties to the Ice Palace. When the previous Palace Master was hovering between life and death, the Divine Physician of Life and Death saved her.\"","\"So that is why he is staying here.\"","\"That’s right. To be exact, he has lived here for the past four years.\"","Since Yeom Hwasin had even specified the length of time, it was clear that the Divine Physician of Life and Death was indeed here.","\"What relationship do you have with him?\"","\"The wounds you inflicted upon me in our last battle were more severe than they appeared.\"","\"Ah! So the Divine Physician of Life and Death was the one who treated you.\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"He disappeared from the martial world some time ago. Were you the one who kept him hidden?\"","\"Didn’t he disappear long before I was injured?\"","\"Then did you find him after he entered seclusion?\"","\"No. I don’t know how he learned about my condition, but he came to the Cheukcheon Alliance himself.\"","\"Are you saying he treated you of his own free will?\"","\"That’s right. He treated me voluntarily.\"","\"I can’t believe it.\"","\"I understand. He originally belonged to the orthodox side, after all. However, once you hear why he came to me, you’ll understand why he saved me.\"","\"Tell me.\"","\"In exchange for treating me, he asked me to kill someone.\"","\"...!\"","The Divine Physician of Life and Death, who had devoted his entire life to saving others, had asked Yeom Hwasin to kill someone?","It was difficult to believe, but Baek So-cheon could sense that Yeom Hwasin was not lying.","\"It was someone only I could kill.\"","\"Who was it?\"","An astonishing name emerged from Yeom Hwasin’s mouth.","\"The Murim Alliance Leader, Ak So-gun.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 124","paragraphs":["The Divine Physician of Life and Death (1)","\"The person the Divine Physician of Life and Death asked you to kill was the Alliance Leader?\"","Baek So-cheon was genuinely stunned. He had never imagined that Ak So-gun’s name would be mentioned.","\"That’s right. The man he asked me to kill was Ak So-gun.\"","What kind of grudge could have driven him to ask for the Alliance Leader’s death?","\"Do you know why?\"","\"I don’t. I didn’t bother asking. It was probably for some trivial reason anyway. In any case, Ak So-gun was someone I already intended to kill, so I was secretly delighted.\"","Baek So-cheon could tell that Yeom Hwasin was telling the truth.","\"If you’re that curious about the reason, ask him while you’re receiving treatment.\"","\"If he is the Alliance Leader’s enemy, will he really treat me?\"","\"Aren’t you the friend of the man who will kill Ak So-gun for him?\"","\"We aren’t friends.\"","\"Even if we aren’t, you should pretend that we are. That way, you’ll receive treatment.\"","\"To go that far...\"","Yeom Hwasin cut him off firmly.","\"You need the treatment.\"","Their gazes met in the air.","\"Very well. Since we’ve come this far, let’s find some way to get me treated.\"","\"Good. That’s more like you.\"","They emptied their cups and refilled each other’s. With one unexpected secret after another being revealed, Baek So-cheon found himself drinking without restraint.","\"Then how can the Absolute Prohibition be lifted?\"","\"There are two methods: an easy method and a difficult one.\"","\"What is the easy method?\"","\"Eliminate everyone who opposes lifting it. We send those trapped by the laws of the dead to join the ancestors they love so much.\"","\"That certainly sounds like your kind of solution. Why haven’t you used it?\"","Baek So-cheon believed Yeom Hwasin was entirely capable of killing them all. He could not allow the friendliness Yeom Hwasin showed him to make him forget the man’s true nature. If necessary, Yeom Hwasin was someone who could eradicate every last blade of grass in the Ice Palace.","\"Unfortunately, that would only make me feel better. It wouldn’t actually lift the restriction.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","Instead of answering, Yeom Hwasin asked a new question.","\"Do you know why the experts of the Northern Sea Ice Palace have been unable to enter the Central Plains?\"","When Baek So-cheon shook his head, Yeom Hwasin revealed another hidden truth.","\"Because a restriction was placed upon them that allows their internal energy to function properly only in cold environments.\"","\"Ah!\"","It was a secret of the martial world that Baek So-cheon had never heard before.","\"Then how can the restriction be lifted?\"","\"One must enter the forbidden grounds of the Ice Palace and retrieve a secret treasure capable of lifting it. I’ve heard that with the treasure, the restriction can be removed permanently, allowing them to use their internal energy even outside cold regions.\"","\"Naturally, that must be difficult.\"","\"They say that not a single person has ever succeeded.\"","\"What happens if someone fails?\"","\"I don’t know. No one who failed ever emerged from that place. Unless they decided to settle down and start a family inside, they probably all died.\"","\"So you intend to enter and retrieve the treasure?\"","Yeom Hwasin did not answer.","When he merely stared at Baek So-cheon with a peculiar smile, Baek So-cheon immediately realized what he was plotting.","\"Surely you aren’t planning to send me inside.\"","\"Why wouldn’t I?\"","\"You...truly are unbelievable!\"","\"Once your internal energy is restored, I believe you’ll be better suited to handling it than I am. To be honest, breaking through forbidden grounds like that isn’t easy for a man my age. My judgment isn’t what it used to be, and my mind no longer works as quickly.\"","\"Is that really the only reason?\"","\"If you insist on another reason, haven’t I already told you? If you encounter a fortuitous opportunity or gain enlightenment while lifting the Absolute Prohibition, you will become even stronger than you are now.\"","\"You plan to fight a stronger version of me and use that battle to reach the next realm?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"What will you do if I become stronger than you?\"","\"Then I’ll die.\"","\"And you’re all right with that?\"","\"If I remain trapped at my current level for the rest of my life, I will live a life worse than death. Can you understand that feeling?\"","\"...I can.\"","Baek So-cheon truly understood him.","He would have felt the same way in Yeom Hwasin’s position.","At present, Baek So-cheon’s heart was entirely focused on leaving the Murim Alliance and living freely. But what if all that desire had instead been focused on martial arts? What if the next stage seemed almost within reach, yet he remained unable to cross the threshold?","What if that continued for the rest of his life?","\"It would be truly agonizing.\"","\"Ordinary people would say that martial arts of such a level should already be enough. They would say that excessive ambition only brings misery. Because that is the reality we live in, you are my one and only true confidant.\"","So that was it.","That was why Yeom Hwasin had allowed him to live.","Baek So-cheon understood that feeling better than anyone.","He raised his cup first.","\"Let’s drink.\"","Yeom Hwasin drank with him.","\"Very well. Let’s assume I agree to enter. Earlier, the opposition to lifting the Absolute Prohibition seemed intense. The elderly expert beside the Palace Master appeared especially furious.\"","\"That old woman is Shim Nahu. She is the Grand Elder of the Ice Palace and holds its real authority.\"","\"Will Elder Shim simply allow me to enter? No, before that, I doubt she’ll even allow them to treat my dantian.\"","Yeom Hwasin then revealed another fact.","\"I received my treatment here at the Ice Palace. Stabilizing my extreme yang internal energy required the Ice Palace’s Yin-Cold Ice Bed.\"","The Yin-Cold Ice Bed was an artifact of the Northern Sea Ice Palace that radiated a freezing chill. It was said that someone practicing extreme yin internal energy could gain far more power than usual by sitting upon it and circulating their energy.","It served a similar function to the Dragon Spring within the Murim Alliance’s Heavenly Dragon Secret Grounds.","\"Ah, so that is how you came to know the Palace Master.\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"Then why do they treat you so poorly?\"","\"Near the end of my treatment, I accidentally broke the Yin-Cold Ice Bed.\"","\"Good heavens! No wonder they’re angry!\"","\"However, they couldn’t hold me directly responsible. I hadn’t broken it intentionally.\"","Yeom Hwasin had probably experienced changes in his body while unconscious. Even if that had not been the case, they would have been unable to punish him because of his connection to the Divine Physician of Life and Death, who had saved the previous Palace Master’s life.","The moment Baek So-cheon heard that, a thought suddenly occurred to him.","\"Did you attain the Indestructible Vajra Body here?\"","\"That’s right. Around the time my treatment was completed, the extreme yin and extreme yang energies collided, causing a tremendous transformation in my body. The Yin-Cold Ice Bed shattered during the process through which I attained the Indestructible Vajra Body.\"","While Baek So-cheon had been wandering in despair after losing his internal energy, unimaginable events had been taking place here.","\"In any case, while I was receiving treatment, I had several opportunities to speak with Palace Master Seo. That was when I learned that she desperately wished to lift the Absolute Prohibition. Shim Nahu and the other elderly experts want to preserve it, while the younger experts wish to abolish it. Palace Master Seo only treated me coldly at first because she was mindful of them. In truth, she desperately hopes I’ll lift the Absolute Prohibition.\"","\"Is an outsider permitted to lift it?\"","\"I asked Palace Master Seo the same question last time. She told me that if the people of the Ice Palace had failed to lift it for so long, perhaps it had always been meant for an outsider to overcome. She said that believing an Ice Palace martial artist had to be the one to lift it was itself an outdated way of thinking. I told her she was clever.\"","Baek So-cheon chuckled.","In a sense, Seo Bingbing had also been drawn into Yeom Hwasin’s plans.","\"Until now, they couldn’t accept outsiders because of those old people. Outsiders weren’t even allowed to enter this place in the first place.\"","\"But that rule was broken because of you.\"","\"Change is necessary for progress.\"","Baek So-cheon finally had a rough understanding of the situation.","What would happen if the Northern Sea Ice Palace lifted its restriction and entered the Central Plains?","What role would it play in the Central Plains’ martial world?","Baek So-cheon asked honestly,","\"If their restriction is lifted and they enter the Central Plains, wouldn’t that disadvantage your side?\"","\"Why do you think it would?\"","\"Isn’t the Northern Sea Ice Palace closer to an orthodox faction?\"","\"That’s your misconception. Don’t assume people are righteous simply because they wear white clothes and smile. They are an organization that cares only about its own interests.\"","Baek So-cheon thought he had a point.","The people of the Ice Palace had been bound by the restriction for generations. Once it was lifted, they were hardly likely to submit themselves to a different form of restraint.","\"The situation in the Murim will become even more complicated.\"","Yeom Hwasin smiled and emptied his cup.","\"That benefits us. Don’t you orthodox factions always make mistakes whenever circumstances become complicated?\"","\"That is prejudice.\"","Baek So-cheon answered firmly, but he could not deny it entirely.","At the very least, the word \"turmoil\" was generally favorable to the Cheukcheon Alliance.","\"Although the Palace Master wishes to lift the prohibition, she didn’t seem able to express it openly.\"","\"Even as Palace Master, she cannot disregard Shim Nahu and her faction.\"","\"What do you plan to do?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"You don’t know?\"","\"From now on, you’ll have to handle it yourself.\"","\"Are you serious?\"","\"Of course. I can’t think of any method other than smashing everything to pieces.\"","\"You understood the situation and still brought me here without any plan?\"","\"You are the plan. Hahaha!\"","Yeom Hwasin heartily drank his wine, and Baek So-cheon emptied his cup alongside him.","Indeed, this was the moment when he needed to rely on his own methods instead of Yeom Hwasin’s.","\"Let me confirm one thing.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Are you certain that the Divine Physician of Life and Death is here?\"","\"I’m certain!\"","In that case, there was one method Baek So-cheon could attempt.","He did not know whether it would work.","***","The following day, Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin were summoned to the Palace Master’s residence again.","The elderly experts, including Shim Nahu, stood closest to Seo Bingbing, while the experts became progressively younger the farther they stood from her.","Now that Baek So-cheon understood the palace’s internal circumstances, he realized the arrangement was less about protection and more about surveillance.","Shim Nahu stepped forward in Seo Bingbing’s place.","\"You two must leave immediately.\"","Her tone was utterly cold.","Yeom Hwasin looked at Baek So-cheon with an expression that seemed to ask what he intended to do now.","Baek So-cheon addressed Seo Bingbing.","\"There is something I must convey before we leave.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"The Murim Alliance Leader said he had a message for the Divine Physician of Life and Death.\"","At the mention of the Murim Alliance Leader, everyone present flinched in surprise.","A smile appeared on Yeom Hwasin’s lips. He appeared to have guessed what method Baek So-cheon intended to use.","\"Tell us the message. I’ll deliver it to him later.\"","\"I must deliver it personally.\"","A brief silence followed.","Baek So-cheon spoke as though the matter were of no particular concern to him.","\"Understood. If the Divine Physician of Life and Death isn’t here, I’ll deliver it on another occasion. We should leave.\"","\"Let’s go.\"","Baek So-cheon cupped his fists in farewell and turned around without hesitation. Yeom Hwasin followed him.","They had taken a little over ten steps when a voice came from behind them.","\"Stop.\"","Baek So-cheon turned around.","A secret door in the rear wall stood open, and an old man was standing before it.","He was Won Gyeongdan, the Divine Physician of Life and Death.","He had been hiding behind the secret door and listening to their conversation.","Won Gyeongdan loudly asked Baek So-cheon,","\"What did that Ak fellow say to me?\"","Ordinarily, he should have shown proper respect by referring to him as Alliance Leader Ak. However, his urgency caused his true feelings to emerge.","\"Do you wish to hear the message here?\"","Baek So-cheon’s question startled the Divine Physician of Life and Death. In his urgency, he had rushed outside without considering the situation.","\"Let us speak privately.\"","Before Shim Nahu could interfere, Seo Bingbing addressed Won Gyeongdan first.","\"I will immediately arrange a private meeting between you and Great Hero Baek.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Seo Bingbing then turned to Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin.","\"Please go ahead and wait. The Divine Physician will join you shortly.\"","\"Understood.\"","Following an Ice Palace warrior’s guidance, Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin left the hall.","When they reached the guest reception room and were alone, Yeom Hwasin burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! That was truly an excellent method.\"","\"It was nothing more than a petty deception.\"","If someone hated another person enough to want him dead, how could he not be curious about a message that person had supposedly sent?","Baek So-cheon had simply taken advantage of human nature.","\"Still, you lied without so much as blinking.\"","\"After spending time with a certain person, I’ve become like ink from staying too close to it.\"","\"I hope the ink stains you even blacker.\"","Indeed, Yeom Hwasin might have started this affair, but it had now become Baek So-cheon’s concern as well.","\"I’ll handle everything from this point onward. You can sit quietly beside me and eat.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 125","paragraphs":["The Divine Physician of Life and Death (2)","Grand Elder Shim Nahu blocked Won Gyeongdan, the Divine Physician of Life and Death, as he was on his way to meet Baek So-cheon.","\"Physician Won, I have something I wish to discuss with you.\"","\"Please speak, Grand Elder.\"","Until now, the two had always treated each other with the utmost courtesy. One was the Ice Palace’s benefactor and honored guest, while the other was the true authority who held its power firmly in her grasp.","\"I know you are busy, so I shall come straight to the point. What happened between you and the Murim Alliance Leader?\"","Won Gyeongdan’s expression stiffened slightly at her question. Even coming from the Grand Elder, it was exceedingly rude to ask him something like that.","\"It is a personal matter, so I cannot tell you.\"","\"This concerns the safety of our palace.\"","\"My personal affairs will not endanger your palace.\"","\"You must make absolutely certain that they do not.\"","\"I am busy, so I shall take my leave. We will speak again another time.\"","Neither of them looked pleased as they walked away.","Shim Nahu was displeased with Won Gyeongdan for appearing out of nowhere and causing trouble, while Won Gyeongdan could hardly have been pleased by her discourteous attitude.","Someone had been watching the exchange from afar.","It was the Ice Palace Lord, Seo Bingbing, accompanied by her bodyguard and most trusted subordinate, Lee Dan, also known as Chutae. Lee Dan was a remarkably handsome young man.","\"We must find a way to lift the Absolute Golden Decree this time.\"","Lee Dan answered her.","\"Everything depends on the meeting between Baek So-cheon and the Divine Physician.\"","Seo Bingbing turned to him.","\"Make sure Elder Shim’s people cannot approach the place where those two meet. She may try to ruin this.\"","\"Yes, understood.\"","Seo Bingbing looked up at the Ice Palace buildings, which glittered like jewels beneath the reflected sunlight.","\"Yes, they’re beautiful. So beautiful that I’m utterly sick of them.\"","***","Baek So-cheon and Won Gyeongdan sat facing each other alone.","Yeom Hwasin had excused himself, claiming that he needed to grind some ink, though he was probably secretly eavesdropping on their conversation.","\"Allow me to introduce myself properly. I am Baek So-cheon.\"","\"I am Won Gyeongdan.\"","\"I have long heard of your great reputation, Divine Physician.\"","\"What reputation could someone like me possibly have? You are the one known throughout the world.\"","After exchanging formal greetings, Won Gyeongdan got straight to the point.","\"What exactly did Alliance Leader Ak ask you to tell me?\"","\"That was a lie.\"","\"What?\"","\"I lied to lure you here. The Alliance Leader never said anything of the sort.\"","Won Gyeongdan rose from his seat with a displeased expression.","\"Then we have nothing more to discuss. I have no intention of restoring your internal energy, either, so you would do well to leave the palace at once.\"","As he turned to leave, Baek So-cheon spoke.","\"If you refuse to treat me, Alliance Leader Yeom will never grant your wish.\"","\"What?\"","Won Gyeongdan spun around in shock.","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"I know what you demanded of Alliance Leader Yeom in exchange for treating him.\"","Won Gyeongdan’s face hardened. He had specifically asked Yeom Hwasin to keep it an absolute secret, yet the man had revealed it to Baek So-cheon.","\"He promised me that he would kill him.\"","\"If he intended to keep that promise, the Murim Alliance Leader would already be dead.\"","\"We are talking about killing the Murim Alliance Leader. How could such a thing be easily accomplished?\"","\"Is that the excuse he gave you? With Alliance Leader Yeom’s current abilities, killing the Alliance Leader is far from impossible. He has simply chosen not to kill him.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Because he still needs the Alliance Leader.\"","\"Why does he need him?\"","\"Because he believes he can control me as long as the Alliance Leader remains alive.\"","\"You?\"","Baek So-cheon knew he would never change Won Gyeongdan’s mind without revealing at least part of the truth.","\"Do you still not understand? To Alliance Leader Yeom, you are merely someone to be used. And not only you. That is how he sees everyone around him.\"","Won Gyeongdan stared at Baek So-cheon before asking suspiciously,","\"Why are you telling me this? Do you think this will persuade me to treat you?\"","\"Would you tell me what happened between you and the Alliance Leader?\"","\"Why should I tell you such a thing?\"","\"For the sake of true revenge.\"","Until now, Baek So-cheon had been cooking with truth as his main ingredient. It was time to add a little falsehood as seasoning.","\"True revenge?\"","\"The fact that you wanted the Divine Physician to kill the Alliance Leader must mean your grudge against him runs extremely deep.\"","\"And?\"","\"There is a way to make him suffer even more than killing him would.\"","\"What way?\"","\"By letting me learn the truth. You know that the Alliance Leader treasures me more than anyone else.\"","Baek So-cheon explained how Ak Sogun had still refused to kill him even after being struck by the Heaven-Beyond Origin Drum.","\"That is the kind of relationship the Alliance Leader and I share. But if a shameful secret that left him unable to hold his head high were exposed to me, nothing could cause him greater anguish. He might even take his own life.\"","After saying this, Baek So-cheon apologized inwardly.","’Alliance Leader, I’m sorry. Given the circumstances, I hope you will understand.’","But what he truly needed to apologize for was what came next.","Still deeply suspicious, Won Gyeongdan asked,","\"If the two of you are so close, why would you do this to your Alliance Leader?\"","\"Because we are not as close as the world believes.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I discovered that the Alliance Leader has two faces.\"","Won Gyeongdan’s eyes gleamed.","\"You discovered it too? How?\"","As expected.","It was exactly as Baek So-cheon had predicted. Won Gyeongdan clearly saw Ak Sogun that way.","Baek So-cheon was taking a gamble. Part of him feared that Ak Sogun truly might have committed some unforgivable act.","Yet deep in his heart, he trusted Ak Sogun. Without that trust, he could never have attempted something like this.","\"After spending so many years with the Alliance Leader, I discovered his duplicitous nature. He is a cowardly man whose outward appearance is completely different from what lies within.\"","\"He is a thoroughly despicable bastard!\"","\"He even took back the sword he had bestowed upon me.\"","\"Exactly! That is how petty the bastard is.\"","When considered calmly, the story did not add up. Ak Sogun had only reclaimed the sword because he was trying to avoid taking Baek So-cheon’s life. Moreover, Baek So-cheon was currently wearing that very Ghost Shadow Sword at his waist.","However, Won Gyeongdan’s heart was already overflowing with resentment toward Ak Sogun, so he focused only on what appeared on the surface.","\"Very well. I will tell you the truth.\"","The suspicion in Won Gyeongdan’s eyes was replaced by hatred.","\"Ak Sogun stole the woman I loved. He even denied me the position of Divine Physician of the Murim Alliance so that he could take her away from me.\"","Baek So-cheon was so shocked and bewildered that he could not speak for a moment. It was a reason he had never imagined.","Won Gyeongdan glared at him venomously.","\"Why? You do not believe me?\"","\"That is not it. Would you explain exactly what happened?\"","\"There was a woman I loved. We shared a profound emotional bond. But then Ak Sogun stole her from me.\"","\"Who was she?\"","\"Someone you know.\"","\"Could you be referring to Senior On Byeokhwa, the former Secret Pavilion Lord?\"","\"Yes. It was her.\"","\"Ak Sogun truly committed a shameless act!\"","Until now, Baek So-cheon had referred to him as the Alliance Leader, but this time, he deliberately called him Ak Sogun.","Inside, however, he was relieved.","Had it been another woman, he might have remained uncertain. But Baek So-cheon knew On Byeokhwa well. He knew how deeply she and Ak Sogun loved each other and, more importantly, he knew her personality. She was absolutely not the kind of woman who would fall for another man without first properly ending things with the man she already loved.","\"How did you first meet Senior On?\"","\"I treated her father.\"","Perhaps remembering that time, Won Gyeongdan’s expression brightened.","\"You must have grown close to her because of that.\"","\"That is right.\"","\"Which of you confessed first?\"","\"Neither of us ever confessed. No, there was no need. We both knew how deeply we loved each other.\"","The moment he heard this, Baek So-cheon understood.","This old, pitiful physician had mistaken her gratitude toward the physician who saved her father for romantic affection.","\"Was she your first love?\"","\"She was also my last. I still love her even now.\"","Won Gyeongdan had never told anyone this before, and speaking it aloud left him feeling as though ten years of pent-up frustration had finally been washed away.","\"That bastard intended to ruin me completely. Is that not obvious from how he appointed that incompetent Ban Wollyang as the Murim Alliance’s Divine Physician instead of me?\"","Once his heart had become twisted, it caused him to see everything in a distorted light.","Ak Sogun and On Byeokhwa probably had no idea that Won Gyeongdan harbored such hatred. Most acts of vengeance born from hatred were like that. On Byeokhwa would likely be astonished to learn that he believed himself to be in love with her.","Won Gyeongdan’s sudden disappearance from the murim must also have coincided with the time Ak Sogun and On Byeokhwa fell in love.","\"Ah!\"","A sigh escaped Baek So-cheon.","When he had asked Yeom Hwasin why the Divine Physician of Life and Death bore such a grudge, the man had answered,","\"I don’t know. I saw no reason to pry. It would surely be something trivial anyway.\"","If Yeom Hwasin heard this reason, he would undoubtedly burst out laughing and declare that he had been right.","But Baek So-cheon did not think it was trivial.","To this old physician, who had never experienced love even once in his life, On Byeokhwa’s smile must have represented the love of a lifetime.","It had nothing to do with the intelligence that had allowed him to master the greatest medical arts under heaven.","Even the supreme masters of martial arts had gaping holes in their hearts. Yeom Hwasin, who kept a woman resembling his first love at his side, was the same. So was Baek So-cheon himself, who sought to complete his life by leaving everyone behind.","Won Gyeongdan smiled happily at Baek So-cheon’s sigh, mistaking it for disappointment in Ak Sogun.","\"Did he say that Alliance Leader Yeom would keep his promise only if I healed you?\"","\"He will.\"","\"Why does he want you healed?\"","At times like this, Won Gyeongdan displayed perfectly sound judgment. It was only when it came to that love affair that his mind became abnormal and warped by hatred.","\"He intends to make me his successor.\"","Just then, Yeom Hwasin’s voice transmission reached him.","—Hahahaha! Isn’t that what you truly want? Become my successor from now on! Hahahaha!","Baek So-cheon pretended not to hear and continued.","\"Otherwise, why would Alliance Leader Yeom spare the man who drove a sword through his chest? You treated him, so you should know better than anyone.\"","\"If I restore your martial arts, will you kill that Ak bastard?\"","Baek So-cheon knew that this was the most crucial moment.","His answer blended truth and lies.","\"Because of the affection we once shared, I cannot do that. But I will ensure that Alliance Leader Yeom keeps his promise to you.\"","\"Truly?\"","\"I mean it.\"","Won Gyeongdan smiled brightly.","\"Good. I will repair your dantian. Hahaha!\"","He was a man willing to do anything if killing Ak Sogun meant he could reclaim On Byeokhwa.","After Won Gyeongdan left, Yeom Hwasin entered the room.","\"Hahaha! Congratulations, my lying successor!\"","\"Stop joking. I’m not in the mood.\"","\"Why? Do you feel guilty for deceiving that old man so thoroughly?\"","\"That too. But more than anything, it leaves a bitter taste in my mouth. What exactly is affection between a man and a woman? Can it truly leave behind hatred this deep?\"","\"That is not affection. It is obsession. Obsession is like a snowball. Once it starts rolling, it grows without end.\"","Baek So-cheon nodded.","The snowball in Won Gyeongdan’s heart had probably grown so large that it could grow no further.","Had Baek So-cheon still been in his twenties, he would have been furious with Won Gyeongdan. He would have wanted to shout, You stupid old fool! If you’re going to lose your mind, at least do it quietly! What the hell do you think you’re doing?","But now, at the age of thirty-nine, he felt more pity than anger toward the man.","Then again, traveling together with Yeom Hwasin like this would have been unthinkable for his younger self.","\"You have broken through one obstacle, but another remains.\"","\"You mean Elder Shim?\"","\"You truly are clever. That’s right. That old woman will never permit the treatment. How do you intend to deal with Shim Nahu? No, don’t spoil the fun by telling me in advance. I’ll watch it myself.\"","Yeom Hwasin looked positively thrilled, as though he were about to watch a troupe perform in the marketplace.","\"This is the most important moment of your life. If you cannot overcome this hurdle, you will never recover your dantian. You will have to do everything within your power.\"","Baek So-cheon recalled how he had lied without the slightest change in expression and murmured,","\"Sometimes, even I wonder how far I am capable of going to achieve my goals...\"","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 126","paragraphs":["This Hellish Place (3)","The Mythricon sword that Passing Dwarf had told me to give away with as much caution as possible.","Originally, I had planned to give it away only after someone provided proof that they had reached the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","But then some middle-aged man verified his identity in a bizarre way.","Apparently, he was fairly famous, because several people recognized him.","He was the teacher of the Hero who was currently on the run after being branded a traitor.","The revelation that such a man had been assigned to the investigation team caused an uproar in the Gallery.","’The manager seemed to know him too.’","More than anything, I couldn’t stop thinking about how shocked the manager had seemed.","They were so stunned that they even stopped adding exclamation marks to the end of every sentence.","Not only that, but they also sent me a private request.","[DontAbandonTheHero: Um... Mr. Grylls! May I ask you for a favor?!]","[Wild Grylls: What kind of favor?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: The gift you said you’d give to someone who proves they’re part of the investigation team! Could you give it to Mr. Ludwig, who just made that post?! I can vouch for him!]","[Wild Grylls: Do you know him?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: Yes! I know him very well!]","[Wild Grylls: Well, if the manager is asking...]","[DontAbandonTheHero: Thank you! The next time you do something that deserves a ban, I’ll grant you immunity!]","And thus, a transaction that wasn’t quite a transaction took place.","I could simply make another sword, so it wasn’t as though I was losing anything.","More importantly, the investigation team needed to survive after entering the forest and reach my location.","One might ask why I didn’t give them an elixir as well, but that was a different matter.","The elixir was something Starlight Princess had painstakingly created.","I might have obtained it through a trade, but it still contained her goodwill.","If I casually gave that goodwill away to someone else, Starlight Princess might feel uncomfortable.","That was simply how people’s feelings worked.","’Since they’re an investigation team, they should have brought various medicines with them.’","They would surely have prepared excellent medicines, even if none were as effective as an elixir.","All that remained was to wait for them to arrive.","No one knew how long it would take.","This was a region where space shifted unpredictably.","Moreover, the land itself was comparable in size to a small country. If we were unlucky, we might never encounter one another.","’They might settle down somewhere suitable, just like I did.’","If they could use the Gallery, locating them would be dozens of times easier.","However, it was common knowledge that the Gallery could not be accessed from within the Forest of Four Seasons.","Eldorado was convinced that it could be used here, but there was no way to know for certain.","Perhaps I was simply special.","’Would they have entered by now?’","I checked for posts written by the middle-aged man who had introduced himself as Ludwig.","He had not posted anything since receiving the sword.","It almost looked as though he had taken the gift and run.","I wished he had at least posted proof when he entered the Forest of Four Seasons, but there was nothing of the sort.","Perhaps he really was just an old-fashioned middle-aged man who had accepted the gift and immediately entered the forest.","’If the Gallery worked inside, he would’ve written something... What a shame.’","It had been not five minutes, but an entire hour.","Yet no new post appeared.","The Gallery users also seemed curious about Ludwig’s whereabouts, but there was no obvious way to find out.","Still, there was one indirect method.","I could ask the manager.","The manager could see the real-time locations of not only fixed-nickname users but anonymous users as well.","It was a privilege and authority unique to the manager.","That should allow us to figure out his general location.","’I should ask.’","The manager seemed to know him, and the matter was important to me as well.","I immediately sent the manager a message, hoping they were still browsing the Gallery.","[Wild Grylls: Manager, do you happen to know where the fixed-nickname user LudwigVanerold is? Is he still outside the Forest of Four Seasons?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: He’s still in front of the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons! I sent him a message, but he isn’t replying!]","[Wild Grylls: Do you think something happened?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: I don’t know either! I think we’ll have to wait and see!]","’Did something happen?’","That thought occurred to me after hearing the manager’s explanation.","The Gallery users had said that while they called it an investigation team, it was effectively a purge.","After all, anyone sent into the Forest of Four Seasons was highly likely to be officially declared \"missing.\"","\"Or maybe he’s too old-fashioned to know how to send messages?\"","It wasn’t entirely impossible.","However, there was no way to be certain of that either.","I could begin forming a proper plan only after the investigation team entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","’No. What plan?’","Space changed however it pleased in this place.","What could I possibly rely on besides luck?","If they were lucky, they might land in the same forest as me.","If they were unlucky, they could appear on the opposite side.","According to the manager, my current location was near the center of the Forest of Four Seasons.","The chances of encountering them were abysmal, but I had no choice except to believe it would happen.","’For now, let’s make some charcoal.’","There was almost nothing I could do until they entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","I had my own work to do, so I planned to focus on it for the time being.","’Let’s see. The charcoal kiln...’","The campfires I had lit until now had produced only a tiny amount of charcoal.","It wasn’t even enough to fill a single small container.","I consumed large quantities of charcoal whenever I forged swords or made other tools.","One way or another, I needed to obtain charcoal in bulk.","I knew nothing about this sort of thing, but I knew someone who did.","[Starlight Princess: The most important part of making charcoal is cutting off the oxygen supply.]","[Wild Grylls: Cutting off the oxygen supply?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. Charcoal is produced through incomplete combustion, and depriving the fire of oxygen creates the necessary conditions. Would you like me to explain it in detail?]","[Wild Grylls: No, it’s fine. Thank you very much, though.]","[Starlight Princess: No problem. Feel free to ask me whenever you have a question related to alchemy.]","That person was Starlight Princess, a genius in the field of alchemy.","She was also the fixed-nickname user who had previously taught me about smoking food.","One might ask why I hadn’t consulted Allfather instead, but his area of expertise seemed different, so I asked Starlight Princess.","Passing Dwarf specialized in metallurgy—in other words, metals—so I had not even considered asking him.","’I need to cut off the oxygen supply...’","Cutting off the oxygen supply would cause incomplete combustion, thereby producing charcoal.","As I slowly pondered her advice, my eyes landed on the oven.","More precisely, I noticed the clay plastered into the gaps in the oven.","It had hardened by now and served as an adhesive.","’That’s it!’","Inspiration struck.","I immediately began gathering wood.","There was a path the leader gorilla had previously created with a single punch.","Since the fallen trees lay across the ground and formed the path, gathering wood was easy.","’I’ll follow that path later.’","After gathering the wood, I arranged it upright as though building a campfire.","Now I needed to light it—","Except I didn’t.","I first had to cover it with clay to cut off the oxygen supply.","If I applied clay directly to the wood, it would neither adhere properly nor remain in place.","’I’ll make a rough frame with branches.’","So I wrapped branches around the pile, particularly those that still had dried leaves attached.","Once they were all in place, I slathered clay over everything until it took the form of a kiln.","But I was not finished yet.","The wood needed to burn fiercely at first, so I made several ventilation holes throughout the kiln.","I also made an opening at the very top.","That was where I planned to insert the flame.","Fwoosh!","Finally, I placed a burning branch into the opening at the top and checked whether the wood had caught fire.","The upper section naturally burned well, but the bottom was what mattered.","That was why I had made the ventilation holes.","Once I was certain the lower section was burning properly, I sealed every vent and cut off the oxygen supply.","\"Cough! Cough! Ugh, that’s strong. Maybe I shouldn’t have checked.\"","I had opened one of the holes to see whether the wood was burning properly, only to inhale a lungful of smoke.","In any case, now that I had confirmed it was burning well, I could move on to something else.","’What’s the situation now?’","I accessed the Gallery and checked whether anything had changed.","However, Ludwig had not written any new posts. Instead, unverified rumors about the investigation team were circulating.","There had been internal strife within the investigation team. The gift Grylls had given Ludwig was so powerful that it had caused an incident.","All kinds of speculative posts were running rampant, but their credibility was virtually nonexistent.","’Why would they start fighting among themselves? Their chances of survival are already low enough.’","Please don’t fight.","Just enter peacefully and come meet me.","Well, honestly, there was no guarantee they would even be able to enter.","It would be better to treat it as nothing more than a faint hope.","After browsing the Gallery for a while, I closed it. Nothing in particular stood out.","’Wait. Even if they enter the forest, will they be able to reach me?’","Smoke occasionally rose high into the sky, but that would not be nearly enough.","Compasses did not work in this damned forest, and its terrain was difficult to comprehend, making it extremely easy to get lost.","I was fine because I had accumulated some experience and generally stuck to familiar routes, but newcomers could not possibly possess that kind of knowledge.","’I should at least make some signposts.’","I would place signposts around the forest so they could find my location.","It might seem a little ridiculous, but it was an effective method.","I immediately prepared my tools.","There were no signposts listed in the Auction House, so I had no choice but to make them myself.","Scrape! Scrape! Scrape!","There were trees everywhere nearby.","I fashioned a signpost from a suitably sized piece of dry wood.","I made a grooved board and a post separately, then fitted them together.","’It would be better to paint it white so it stands out, right?’","I bought paint from the Auction House.","Even that was expensive.","In the center of the arrow-shaped board, I drew a house.","A trapezoid atop a square, with a window drawn inside the square.","It was meant to indicate that someone lived there.","It looked presentable enough.","Its height reached somewhere between my chest and neck, so it should be easy to notice.","Title: Made a Signpost","Wild Grylls","I made a signpost just in case the investigation team passes nearby. I’m about to go set it up.","Members of the investigation team! If you see this, just follow the arrow! It points to where I am!","└ Heavenly Demon) You made it quite neatly. Between this and the sword, you appear to be exceptionally skilled with your hands.","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you, haha.","└ Aren’t you getting your hopes up too much? Kekekeke.","└ I thought this bastard was joking, but he’s actually serious. Kekekeke.","└ What are you going to do if no one ever enters the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll hug Wonmo and sob.","└ Wild Grylls) Really?","└ Of course that was a lie. Ke.","└ Wild Grylls) You bastard. Keke.","└ DontAbandonTheHero) If you really do meet him, please welcome him warmly! Mr. Ludwig is a genuinely kind person.","└ Wild Grylls) Won’t that only matter if he actually enters the forest? There still hasn’t been any news about him coming in.","└ DontAbandonTheHero) That’s true! Honestly, I hope he doesn’t enter!","└ Wild Grylls) You’re crushing my hopes.","└ DontAbandonTheHero) I’m sorry, but I think it’s better for your hopes to be crushed than for someone’s life to be sacrificed meaninglessly!","└ Wild Grylls) Damn it. TT Now I have nothing to say.","└ That’s sad, Grylls... But the manager is right.","└ You’re the strange one. Normally, anyone who enters the Forest of Four Seasons dies within a few days.","└ Wild Grylls) If someone is reasonably skilled, their chances of survival should be higher. My senior survived here too.","└ Your senior? Don’t tell me you mean that skeleton.","└ Have you finally acknowledged him as your senior? Keke.","└ That’s strangely adorable. Kekekeke.","└ What did Wonmo do to deserve that? Kekekekeke.","└ Wild Grylls) He’s my only means of emotional healing.","└ Are you that lonely? Want me to come visit you?","Even the manager had indirectly told me to abandon hope, but I refused to give up!","Of course, that did not mean I wanted Ludwig to risk his life just to enter the forest.","I was simply... preparing for the possibility that the investigation team would become \"castaways.\"","’Are they still waiting outside the entrance?’","With that thought in mind, I made even more signposts.","I planned to install them along every route I had traveled thus far.","’I want to talk to another person too.’","After two weeks, loneliness was slowly beginning to creep in.","While Grylls was kindly making and installing signposts—","Bam!","\"Aaaaaaargh!\"","A holy knight went flying toward the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","He flailed his arms as though desperately protesting that he did not want to enter.","The holy knight remained visible for only a brief moment.","The instant he passed through the \"entrance\" to the Forest of Four Seasons, he vanished without a trace.","\"Whew...\"","The holy knight who had kicked him in the back—Ludwig—exhaled heavily.","Then he slowly turned and faced the hostile watchdogs.","Swoosh—","Ludwig leveled the sword that appeared to contain a flowing emerald galaxy.","Then, radiating a dazzling aura, he spoke.","\"Does anyone else wish to enter?\"","Just as Grylls had hoped, Ludwig was kindly \"procuring\" survivors for him."]},{"title":"Chapter 127","paragraphs":["This Hellish Place (4)","Ludwig was rigid and frustratingly inflexible, but he was also a man who understood honor.","As a believer in Ares, as Ares’s shield, and as the teacher of the holy knights.","Everyone acknowledged Ludwig’s honor, and he himself took great pride in it.","Naturally, he could not help but become angry when that honor was tarnished—especially through underhanded means.","But perhaps the previous incident had been the last one that could still be contained.","No matter how fiercely he resisted, he would eventually be forced into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Now that he had been driven to the edge of a cliff, his actions seemed like nothing more than a desperate final struggle.","Even so, he stepped forward to preserve his honor until the very end.","And not merely his own honor, but the lives of others as well.","’They all escaped safely.’","Ludwig looked around.","Reis and the other members of the investigation team had already scattered in every direction.","Before long, they would become the \"seeds\" of a revolution.","All of this had been made possible by the sword—the one he had received as a gift immediately before entering the Forest of Four Seasons.","Even Ludwig himself regarded the power of the sword that gleamed like an emerald galaxy with awe.","He had fought countless battles as the Sword of Ares, yet he had never encountered a weapon this terrifying.","’If mishandled, this could easily become a demonic sword.’","Unlike the Holy Sword Revolution, it amplified its wielder’s abilities.","However, even the wielder struggled to control it, and a single mistake could result in the user cutting himself down.","It was fortunate that Ludwig had restrained himself while fighting.","Otherwise, he might have placed himself in grave danger.","’What manner of being could have created this sword?’","Its power was astonishingly great.","The problem was that it was excessively powerful.","It was so difficult to control that he could not focus solely on the battle. The slightest misstep caused his aura to run rampant.","Breathing heavily, Ludwig stared ahead.","The watchdogs were still glaring at him.","They all wore helmets, so he could not see their faces, but he could sense it clearly.","They were afraid.","\"What are you afraid of?\"","\"Come. Your enemy stands before you.\"","Ludwig spoke in his usual blunt voice.","If the Hero was the Sword of Ares, then Ludwig was the Shield of Ares.","For the watchdogs to break through him was practically unthinkable.","Moreover, Ludwig now held a terrifyingly powerful sword.","With the rest of the investigation team having escaped, the watchdogs had no options left.","They could attack Ludwig and die by his hand, or they could return and be purged by the Pope.","With the Forest of Four Seasons behind him, Ludwig had nowhere to flee either.","But neither did he possess the strength to break through the watchdogs.","He had pushed himself too hard while scattering the seeds of revolution.","He was managing to hold his ground only because of the sword.","Both sides were trapped in a complete deadlock.","There seemed to be no way out.","’What should we do?’","’What do you mean, what should we do? Why aren’t we attacking him already?!’","’Didn’t you see what just happened? The last people who tried were thrown into the Forest of Four Seasons!’","’Damn it. I wish there were a cliff behind him instead.’","The watchdogs whispered among themselves.","Ludwig was not the only thing they feared.","There was also the Forest of Four Seasons behind him.","The moment they entered that place, they would never emerge again.","Beginning with Archbishop Odon, several watchdogs had already been forced inside.","They had witnessed those people vanish without a trace the instant they crossed the entrance.","Naturally, they could not help hesitating.","’They are wavering.’","With the wisdom accumulated throughout his long life, Ludwig immediately sensed the atmosphere among the watchdogs.","They, too, were hesitating because they had been trapped with nowhere to go.","’Not that my own situation is any better.’","Ludwig’s prospects were far from bright.","In fact, they were bleak.","Even if he broke through the watchdogs and survived, his honor would be dragged through the mud.","As long as the Pope maintained an iron grip over Eldorado, manipulating the media would be a trivial matter.","Furthermore, Ludwig had been the Hero’s teacher.","That made him the perfect scapegoat.","They would claim that the Hero had fallen because Ludwig had corrupted her with his beliefs.","The outcome was so obvious that Ludwig could only chuckle bitterly.","Because he understood honor, he wished above all else to prevent his own from being disgraced.","’It was wise to deal with that pig first.’","With Archbishop Odon gone, there was no one left to issue orders.","Every senior member had either been killed by Ludwig or forcibly thrown into the Forest of Four Seasons.","No one knew whose orders to follow.","Confusion was the natural result.","\"It seems you understand your predicament. If you return like this, you will be purged. If you attack me, you will die.\"","\"I have a proposal.\"","At Ludwig’s words, the watchdogs looked at one another.","Their gazes silently asked whether they should hear him out.","But since they had no better solution, they decided to listen.","\"Even if you return now, the Pope will have you killed. The same will be true even if you kill me.\"","\"What? What are you talking about...?\"","\"No one desires to destroy my honor more than the Pope. Do you know why he arranged for me to disappear?\"","Ludwig was stubborn.","But he was not stupid.","His personality resembled that of a certain Gallery manager, tempered by many years of experience.","\"It is to prevent me from becoming a martyr.\"","\"Even if you bring him my head, the Pope will make every one of you disappear. He will fabricate some pretext and place the blame upon you. I will be declared missing, and you will be executed. Everyone who remembers what happened here will vanish.\"","It was not an absurd claim.","In fact, it was a highly plausible assumption.","The Pope had built his reputation by purging those he branded \"subversives.\"","To preserve that reputation, he would not care if dozens—or even hundreds—of innocent people became casualties.","The watchdogs were part of that scheme.","No matter what happened, their fate remained the same.","They were destined to die.","\"H-How are we supposed to believe that...?\"","\"Because he must have done the same thing to the Immortal King.\"","\"...\"","\"If he could drive an entire kingdom to ruin, destroying a single person would be easy. Countless people will die in the process.\"","The moment Ludwig mentioned the Immortal King, the watchdogs who had been about to object fell silent.","Eldorado had gone so far as to commit a massacre merely to ruin the king of a small nation.","There was no guarantee that the same cruelty would not be directed at them.","The reasoning fit too perfectly for the watchdogs not to waver.","The instant Ludwig sensed cracks forming in their faith, he made his proposal.","\"Therefore, flee.\"","\"Choose whether to escape beyond the Holy Kingdom’s borders or wait until I recover.\"","\"...Will you kill us once you recover?\"","A watchdog with a deep voice spoke.","Tension filled his words.","Ludwig stared silently at him before giving an unexpected answer.","\"No.\"","\"Then what will you do?\"","\"I will enter the Forest of Four Seasons.\"","\"What?\"","The unexpected answer left every member of the watchdog unit visibly bewildered.","That was only natural.","They had assumed that Ludwig had been struggling so desperately because he did not want to enter the Forest of Four Seasons.","But that was not the case.","In truth, Ludwig had resolved to enter the forest long ago.","He explained his reasoning so they could understand.","\"If I sacrifice my honor, I may preserve the honor of others. They can claim that I instilled corrupt beliefs in the Hero and turned her into a traitor.\"","\"...\"","The Pope had erected human shields to protect his own honor.","Ludwig, however, had chosen to become a shield himself.","It was an action befitting the Shield of Ares.","Perhaps Ludwig’s words and actions had stirred something within them.","One by one, the watchdogs hesitantly began lowering their weapons.","Their instinctive desire to survive.","The sincerity contained in Ludwig’s words.","Everything fit together perfectly, breaking their will to fight.","\"A wise decision.\"","\"...When will you enter?\"","\"In one hour.\"","The moment Ludwig answered, he sat cross-legged.","It was a posture for practicing his mana cultivation technique.","The watchdogs could not help but find it absurd.","The man who had threatened their lives moments earlier was now cultivating mana right in front of them?","His actions defied common sense, and murmurs naturally spread among them.","’Should we attack?’","’Are you insane? What if it’s a trap?’","’If he fully recovers, he might turn on us.’","’Ludwig would never do that. Trust him.’","In the end, the watchdogs trusted Ludwig.","They knew how upright he was.","Even without their earlier conversation, his character was anything but corrupt.","On the contrary, he was every bit as noble as the Hero.","While Ludwig practiced his cultivation technique, the watchdogs gradually withdrew.","Eventually, most of them retreated, leaving only a few behind to confirm that he entered the forest.","An hour passed, and Ludwig finished cultivating his mana.","He slowly opened his eyes and looked ahead.","Only two watchdogs remained in sight.","’It seems most of them have left.’","Even after sensing his surroundings, he detected no one else.","Ludwig slowly rose to his feet.","The watchdogs flinched when he stood, seemingly frightened before he had even done anything.","Ludwig stared at them before speaking in his characteristically blunt voice.","\"You two.\"","\"Y-Yes?\"","Ludwig’s tone was gentler than before, causing the watchdog to answer respectfully without even realizing it.","\"Are you the newest recruits?\"","\"Y-Yes?\"","\"I asked whether you are the newest recruits.\"","The unexpected question made the watchdogs glance at each other.","After hesitating, they answered in considerably timid voices.","\"Y-Yes, sir! That’s correct! I only recently completed my apprenticeship!\"","\"I joined one year before this fellow!\"","They answered with rigid military discipline.","Ludwig chuckled.","At the same time, he felt sorry for them.","Even such fresh-faced recruits had been dragged into this filthy business.","’What will become of the Holy Kingdom’s future?’","He had fulfilled his duty as the Shield of Ares, yet he had failed to protect the kingdom from within.","For the Holy Kingdom to regain its true form, its rotten parts would have to be carved away.","That role could not be fulfilled by a shield.","Only a \"sword\" could accomplish it.","Ludwig turned and looked toward the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","The entrance rippled like an aurora, revealing all manner of environments beyond it.","Ludwig feared little, but he was still human.","He, too, felt fear of the unknown.","’What kind of place... lies beyond this?’","Fear of the unknown.","And curiosity.","After a brief hesitation, Ludwig slowly extended his hand.","His hand passed through the aurora.","He felt nothing.","Having taken the first step, it was time to enter with his entire body.","He slowly closed his eyes and murmured.","’Ares, please protect me.’","Step. Step.","Moving both legs, Ludwig entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","A strange sensation enveloped his body.","He slowly opened his eyes.","\"...\"","The first thing he saw was an expansive grassland.","The entire plain was covered in green.","It looked nothing like a forest.","After staring blankly at the grassland, he turned around.","He should have been able to see the place where he had stood moments earlier.","Instead, as if it had all been a lie, there was nothing behind him but verdant grassland.","’Is this where the man called Wild Grylls lives?’","Ludwig immediately attempted to access the Gallery.","He was still unfamiliar with it, but accessing it itself was not difficult.","[The Gallery cannot be accessed in this region.]","Although it was easy enough to attempt, accessing it had become impossible.","Ludwig stared at the message before silently closing it.","The Gallery was inaccessible.","That could mean only one thing.","’This is undoubtedly the Forest of Four Seasons.’","The Gallery could not be used within the Forest of Four Seasons.","That fact had not changed.","Then how was Grylls able to use it?","The question suddenly occurred to him.","’I can ask him when I meet him.’","Ludwig slowly began walking.","The grassland might be vast, but he would surely encounter Grylls eventually.","He did not know when that would happen, but moving was far better than remaining still.","Of course—","Munch. Munch. Munch.","\"...\"","Searching for Grylls and the welcome he received were two entirely separate matters.","Ludwig tilted his head upward and stared at a certain animal.","Its body was predominantly yellow and covered in brown patterns.","Its long legs towered over Ludwig, and powerful muscles stood out beneath them.","But one feature drew his attention more than anything else.","It went beyond unusual and entered the realm of grotesque.","’Its neck...’","Its neck was absurdly long.","It was so long that the animal could effortlessly eat leaves from the tops of towering trees.","Its head, neck, and torso seemed almost entirely disconnected, giving it a bizarre appearance.","Even Ludwig, who possessed a wealth of worldly experience, had never seen such an animal before.","’...What kind of ridiculous animal is that?’","Had Grylls seen it, he would have called it a \"giraffe.\"","Ludwig watched the giraffe eat for a long while before shaking his head.","’This truly is hell.’","There was no other explanation for the existence of such a creature.","With that thought, Ludwig walked past the giraffe.","Munch, munch. Munch, munch.","The giraffe paid him no attention and continued happily eating leaves."]},{"title":"Chapter 128","paragraphs":["This Hellish Place (5)","The Forest of Four Seasons did not place everyone at the same starting point upon entry.","Unless people entered while holding hands, each person would inevitably begin in a different location.","Even if they did hold hands, there was no guarantee they would arrive in the same place.","People had been seen entering, but not a single one had ever come back out.","Still, after countless years of accumulated research, a few things had finally been learned about it.","One of them was that anyone entering the Forest of Four Seasons would be dropped into one of its regions at random.","Only someone truly fortunate would arrive near a person who had entered before them.","\"Ugh...\"","A paladin groaned as he rose to his feet.","His helmet concealed his face, but his attire made his affiliation obvious.","He was the senior surveillance officer whom Ludwig had kicked into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Ordinary paladins typically wore pure white armor, whereas the surveillance officers wore armor so dark it was nearly black.","It was originally armor worn by \"inquisitors,\" but those men had now become the Pope’s private soldiers.","\"Damn it. Where the hell am I now?\"","The surveillance officer looked around and cursed.","He already knew where he was, of course, but desperately wanted to deny it.","He vividly remembered Ludwig kicking him in the back and sending him into the Forest of Four Seasons.","’Damn it...’","He surveyed the scenery, which was completely different from how the Forest of Four Seasons had appeared from outside.","Instead of a lush green forest, the area was filled with dry, skeletal trees.","Whether it had been covered in volcanic ash or ravaged by a wildfire, everything was gray.","And that was not all. The ground was just as bad.","There was at least solid earth where the surveillance officer had fallen, but everything beyond it was a swamp.","’Was I lucky?’","If he had fallen directly into the swamp, he might have died the moment he entered.","That did not mean he was safe, however.","What kind of place was this?","It was the Forest of Four Seasons, known as hell on earth.","A demonic realm from which not a single survivor had ever returned.","The surveillance officer swallowed hard.","’It’s not over yet. That bastard Grylls was living here just fine.’","Even if no one had managed to escape, there was at least one survivor.","That fact gave the surveillance officer hope.","He then checked himself for injuries and inspected his weapon to ensure it was undamaged.","Aside from the spot where he had been kicked in the back, nothing particularly hurt.","[The Gallery cannot be accessed in this region.]","However, he could not access the Gallery.","He was also one of its users.","Having seen it in action, he knew just how useful the Gallery could be in an environment like this.","When a message appeared informing him that it was unavailable, he could only click his tongue.","’So much for it being accessible.’","Using Wild Grylls as evidence, the Pope had proclaimed that the Gallery could now be accessed from within the Forest of Four Seasons.","That propaganda had worked well enough to provide the impetus for dispatching the investigation team.","Only after entering the Forest of Four Seasons did the surveillance officer realize that the Pope had told a blatant lie.","There was a saying that everything leaving the Pope’s mouth—aside from carbon dioxide—was a lie.","The surveillance officer now wholeheartedly agreed.","His mistake had been falling for the Pope’s honeyed words.","’I’ll get out of here no matter what. I’m way stronger than that bastard. There’s no way I can’t escape.’","The surveillance officer ground his teeth.","He would escape within a few days and cut off Ludwig’s head.","The Pope was the true cause of all this, but he was far too powerful. So the surveillance officer directed his resentment toward the comparatively weaker Ludwig instead.","It was the typical behavior of one who bullied the weak and submitted to the strong—a blatant display of selfishness.","’First, I should check my mana.’","Before setting off, the surveillance officer examined the mana within his body.","His fierce battle with Ludwig had consumed a considerable amount of it.","Since he only needed to inspect it, there was no reason to perform the mana cultivation method.","\"...Hmm?\"","Then he noticed something strange.","The surveillance officer’s eyes widened slightly.","Normally, his mana should have been circulating, however faintly, yet it was not moving at all.","No.","It was circulating.","It was merely doing so at an absurdly slow pace.","Alarmed by this inexplicable phenomenon, he hurriedly tried to activate his mana.","’Wh-What’s wrong with my mana?’","It still refused to budge.","Only when he forced it to move could he barely sense it.","Fearing the worst, he even tried to manifest his aura, but it was useless.","His aura would not emerge either.","He had effectively been dropped here with nothing but his bare body.","His chances of survival had plummeted far lower than anticipated.","Suspecting that he might have suffered an injury without realizing it, the surveillance officer carefully examined himself.","Yet he found nothing unusual.","In the end, he risked the danger and began performing the mana cultivation method.","’Wh-What is this...?!’","The moment he began cultivating, he understood the cause.","It was the mana.","More precisely, it was not the mana inside his body, but the mana outside it.","The ambient mana was far too dense.","The mana outside his body was suppressing the mana within him.","It was the same principle by which water pressure in the deep sea crushed objects.","’That’s impossible! That bastard Grylls clearly...!’","The surveillance officer could not believe it.","This was entirely unexpected.","Grylls threw mana around at every opportunity, yet he himself could not use it at all.","He found it impossible to accept.","’No. If I have enough time...’","It was still too early to despair.","The surveillance officer steadied his shaken resolve.","If the external mana prevented him from using the mana inside his body, then he simply had to fill himself with the mana outside.","He did not know how long that would take, but it was not impossible.","’I need to find somewhere safe.’","The surveillance officer quickly assessed the situation.","This swamp was dangerous.","He had no idea what sort of monster might suddenly emerge from it.","The forest where Grylls lived would undoubtedly be much safer.","Having reached that conclusion, he began walking to escape the swamp.","Shing—","He also drew his sword so that he could respond at a moment’s notice.","Although he could not use mana, he still possessed considerable physical prowess and should be able to survive.","’Archbishop Odon should have entered before me... Where could he be?’","The surveillance officer thought of Odon, who had entered the Forest of Four Seasons ahead of him.","Like him, the clergyman had been forcibly sent inside by Ludwig.","He wondered whether he should search for Odon.","Unlike the surveillance officer, Odon specialized in support and possessed virtually no combat ability.","Furthermore, they had just discovered that mana could not be used in this region.","The longer Odon remained alone, the lower his chances of survival would become.","’There’s nothing I can do about the Archbishop. I should find the others first. There must be more people Ludwig sent in here like me.’","Unless something unexpected happened, the surveillance officer decided to abandon Odon without hesitation.","His own combat ability had already been cut in half.","He could not afford to protect someone who possessed no combat ability whatsoever.","Clergymen normally exercised healing abilities through divine power, but that was only possible when they actually possessed divine power.","It would not have been an exaggeration to say that Archbishop Odon had \"none,\" so the surveillance officer expected nothing from him.","After all, Odon had risen to the position of archbishop by attaching himself to the right faction.","If the surveillance officer wanted to escape this hellish forest, he needed to join forces with the strong—not with people who would become liabilities.","’Still... if I happen to run into him, I can’t exactly pretend I didn’t see him...’","The surveillance officer had just finished sorting out his thoughts when it happened.","[...please.]","A voice reached the surveillance officer’s ears.","At first, he thought he had misheard it.","He stopped walking and focused on the sound.","[...save me, please.]","This time, he heard it again, faint though it was. The surveillance officer hurriedly looked around.","He needed to determine exactly where the voice was coming from.","\"Is someone there?! If you are, speak louder!\"","Shouting in a swamp was not a wise thing to do.","A beast might hear him and approach. Given the circumstances, however, he had little choice.","The surveillance officer shouted at the top of his lungs, praying that his voice would reach whoever was out there.","[I’m here! Over here! I’m right here!]","This time, he heard it clearly. The surveillance officer turned toward the source of the voice.","It sounded slightly echoey, but he paid it no mind because of the language being spoken.","It was not the language of some foreign nation, but the language of Eldorado itself.","’And this voice... Archbishop Odon?’","The surveillance officer hurried toward the voice.","Perhaps fortune had favored him, and the Archbishop had regained consciousness close to where he had fallen.","He had just been calling the man useless, but another person was still another person.","’If worse comes to worst, I can use him as a human shield.’","What a shameless change of heart.","It perfectly demonstrated what desperation could reduce a person to.","[I’m right here! Is anyone there?!]","The voice grew closer and closer. Both of the surveillance officer’s feet sank into the water.","It only reached his ankles for now, so he ignored it. Confirming the source of the voice came first.","At last, he reached the place it was coming from.","\"A-Archbishop?! You’re alive?\"","[Oh! You came...!]","The surveillance officer found the Archbishop.","Surprisingly, he appeared completely unharmed.","The strange quality of his voice was suspicious, but otherwise, he looked far too healthy.","[Come this way. I believe the exit is over here.]","\"What? The exit...?\"","[Yes. Someone else helped me as well.]","Archbishop Odon pointed toward the exit with a benevolent expression. The surveillance officer’s suspicions deepened.","The direction he was pointing in led toward the deepest part of the swamp.","The water was already slightly above his ankles here, and anyone could tell that it was far deeper over there.","’Before that...’","There was something even stranger.","It was something he had only just noticed.","Archbishop Odon was short, while the water here was deep enough to cover one’s ankles.","So why was Archbishop Odon standing on top of the water?","Powerful individuals might be capable of walking across water, but Odon was not one of them.","It was strange.","More than merely strange, it was ominous.","\"Wh-Who the hell are you?!\"","[What? Whatever do you mean...?]","\"You vile monster! Reveal yourself!\"","The surveillance officer retreated and pointed his sword at the figure, his voice trembling with fear.","Perhaps it sensed the terror in his voice, because Odon—or rather, the creature disguised as Odon—stopped hiding itself.","Ssssh—","Odon’s form faded like a mirage.","What appeared in its place was, shockingly, a corpse.","It was a shriveled, emaciated corpse. A tentacle was tightly coiled around its neck as though it had been strangled.","The surveillance officer immediately recognized the corpse.","Anyone could tell that it was Odon.","’Wh-What the hell is this?!’","Rrrrrumble!","Whether or not he was horrified, an ominous phenomenon began within the swamp.","The ground started to shake as though an earthquake had struck.","Had Grylls been there, he would have fled the region without even looking back.","However, the surveillance officer had only just entered the Forest of Four Seasons for the first time.","He could do nothing but stand there dumbfounded until the monster made its move.","Splash!","A hand suddenly emerged from the deep pool.","It resembled a human hand, but its skin was smooth like that of an amphibian.","Perhaps as camouflage, the hand possessed a dull, musty color resembling tree bark.","SPLAAAASH!","The monster planted its hand against the ground and heaved itself fully into view.","The surveillance officer could only stare in horror at the creature, which was several times larger than he was.","It had hideous teeth, a long body, and an antenna protruding from its head.","Odon’s corpse had been dangling from that antenna.","Whoosh!","The hand-bearing anglerfish that had emerged from the depths of the swamp reached toward the surveillance officer.","The instant he saw it move, the surveillance officer hurriedly stepped backward in an attempt to escape.","But that very action led him to his death.","As had already been stated, this was a swamp.","Squelch!","\"Urgh!\"","If he had merely remained still, it would have taken longer for the swamp to swallow him.","The surveillance officer lost his balance and fell, and the swamp anglerfish did not miss its chance.","Grab!","\"Aaargh!\"","The swamp anglerfish seized the surveillance officer violently with its humanlike hand.","He struggled against the crushing pressure closing around his body, but it was useless.","He could not use mana in his current state.","He was destined to be devoured.","Crunch. Crunch.","Meanwhile, the swamp anglerfish placed Odon’s corpse, which it had caught with its antenna, into its mouth.","It chewed the corpse into pieces with its razor-sharp teeth.","The anglerfish then wrapped its tentacle-like antenna around the surveillance officer’s neck.","Squeeeze!","\"Ghhhhh...\"","A deflating wheeze escaped his throat, and it was not long before the strength began draining from his body.","Clunk!","His violent struggles had loosened his helmet, causing it to slip off and fall into the swamp.","Inside the armor was nothing but a shriveled mummy, just like Odon’s corpse.","Limp—","The swamp anglerfish released its grip, leaving the surveillance officer dangling from its antenna.","Having drained all his life force, the anglerfish descended into the deep water once more.","Only the antenna holding the surveillance officer remained above the surface.","[A-Archbishop?!]","Amazingly, the mouth of the surveillance officer’s mummified corpse moved, producing his voice.","It was an utterly grotesque sight, as though the antenna were controlling his body.","[You vile monster! Reveal yourself!]","It went beyond simply imitating his voice.","[Is anyone there?! There’s someone here! I need help!]","Its imitation was as perfect as if it had extracted all his memories.","[Please! Anyone—help me!]","The Forest of Four Seasons was a hellish place.","Thwack! Thwack! Thwack!","\"Phew. This should be enough, right?\"","I muttered in satisfaction as I hammered the signpost into the ground.","I had spent quite a lot of time making this signpost.","Still, seeing it firmly planted there filled me with pride.","’I hope they manage to survive.’"]},{"title":"Chapter 129","paragraphs":["Click (1)","After perfectly installing the signpost, I returned to the shelter.","It felt a little strange to say this when I was the one who had made it, but I had designed it so that anyone could easily tell people lived nearby.","Moreover, I had already advertised(?) it on the Gallery, so everyone should recognize it.","’Not that I expect to meet them anytime soon.’","I had taken every measure available to me, but I did not get my hopes up.","The Forest of Four Seasons covered an area comparable to a small country.","Above all, it was a place where space constantly shifted, so no one knew how we might encounter each other.","If we were lucky, we could meet soon. If we were unlucky, we might never meet for the rest of our lives.","’Or they might settle somewhere else...’","In the worst-case scenario, they might already be dead.","That was what worried me most.","Would the investigation team really be able to reach this place safely?","I had no way of knowing.","At least the admin’s location-tracking ability could give me some idea of their chances of survival.","’I just need to keep a close eye on Ludwig’s location.’","He was the registered user who had announced that he would enter the Forest of Four Seasons.","I planned to keep track of his movements.","The admin seemed worried about him as well, so I could simply ask for updates frequently.","If even the admin could no longer locate him, it would be genuinely heartbreaking.","’It’s not as if I’m safe either, though.’","I had plenty of problems of my own, but at least I had dependable allies.","There was Namu-Ppareumbo, who I suspected had fought the leader gorilla.","Then there was Wonmo, the owlbear cub whose presence was remarkably effective at soothing the mind.","The investigation team had nothing.","The presence or absence of a companion with overwhelming combat power like Namu-Ppareumbo would make an enormous difference.","’I really did well to survive back when I was so weak.’","I now had enough strength to endure even if a crisis arose, but that had not been true on my first day.","When the Mad Dog bit me, I thought I was screwed, and I had nearly died for real when I encountered the saber-toothed tiger.","Feeling grateful that I had survived until now, I arrived at the shelter.","’Still, I have work to do.’","I had given Ludwig my sword, so I no longer had a spare.","I needed to make a new one.","Fortunately, I had just produced a large amount of charcoal, so forging one would not be difficult.","I also had spare materials, allowing me to use them without hesitation.","’I should keep collecting mithril and orichalcum.’","I never knew when, where, or to whom I might end up giving another sword.","I should make two in total, including one I could give to someone else.","However, I intended to discuss it with the dwarf first.","Sending one off without consulting him would be rude.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. I’m going to send you another sword in a little while. Can you sharpen it for me?]","[Passing Dwarf: I don’t mind, but did you seriously give him that sword?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. He was entering the Forest of Four Seasons, so I figured I should give him something. It benefits me if they manage to survive somehow.]","[Passing Dwarf: You naïve fool. What are you going to do if that registered user killed everyone else and ran off? That sword is already terrifying enough.]","I understood what the dwarf was worried about.","He was concerned that Ludwig might take the sword and run.","It was a sword whose performance was so exceptional that even the Heavenly Demon had called it a bad thing.","The dwarf was suggesting that Ludwig might have become greedy and deserted the investigation team.","[Passing Dwarf: What is?]","[Wild Grylls: Honestly, it doesn’t really matter to me lol]","[Passing Dwarf: You bastard lololol You’re enjoying all the pleasure with none of the responsibility lololol]","[Wild Grylls: Everyone said he was a good person, though. The admin said he knew him too.]","[Passing Dwarf: Good grief. You did that just because you trusted what other people said? Hah... The milk’s already spilled, so you can’t take it back now.]","[Wild Grylls: But you know what?]","That was what I said, but the admin’s request had actually played a large part in my decision.","I would have hesitated if he had not asked me.","I had already learned through the Gallery that someone named Ludwig was part of the investigation team.","However, after seeing verification like the old man’s and receiving the admin’s request, I somehow felt that it would be fine to give him the sword.","’This should increase their chances of escaping, even if only slightly.’","The more attention the outside world paid to the Forest of Four Seasons, the higher my own chances of survival would become.","I also intended to try(?) my hardest to attract people’s attention.","The easiest way to do that was to spread mithrilcon.","However, if I mishandled it, a war could break out just as the dwarf had warned.","It was a metal everyone desperately wanted but could not obtain.","People were already frantic to get their hands on it.","If too much of it circulated, tragedy would inevitably follow.","Fortunately, it could not even be processed without a specialized furnace.","I intended to exploit the fact that I was the only person capable of making things from it.","Strange people might begin clinging to me, but I planned to ignore them whenever possible and create a deterrent.","[Wild Grylls: I finished making it. Sharpen it for me.]","[Passing Dwarf: The more I think about it, the more ridiculous it gets. Some people might never touch that metal once in their entire lives, while someone else has it spread all over his house and front yard lolol]","[Wild Grylls: You know what they say if you’re jealous, right? Hehe.]","[Passing Dwarf: Piss off lol]","From the dwarf’s perspective, I supposed it really was as easy as a single click.","In reality, it practically was.","The tremendous heat made it difficult, but the process itself was not particularly complicated.","Even if I failed, I had unlimited opportunities to try again, so I could work without feeling pressured.","I examined the newly returned sword from various angles before leaning it against the cave wall.","[Wild Grylls: I made another one. Sharpen this too.]","[Passing Dwarf: How long has it even been since you made the last one?]","[Wild Grylls: You just put them in together, melt them, and pour the metal into the mold. That’s it.]","[Passing Dwarf: Hahahaha, this is seriously ridiculous. Hey, do you even realize that’s also an insanely difficult process?]","[Wild Grylls: Not really? It worked because I did exactly what you told me. Hammering is the hardest part, isn’t it?]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s true, but... Haah. I don’t even know anymore. I’ll take the sword for now.]","Then I made one more sword.","It was a spare for my spare.","I would have liked to make yet another one, but it was already getting late, and I was running low on materials.","Besides, I now wanted to make something other than a sword.","A pickaxe, for example.","I already had the pickaxe the dwarf had given me, but I wanted to mine mithril more easily.","Since I had gone to the trouble of creating a new metal, I also wanted a new tool made from it.","’I should forge the pickaxe myself instead of casting it.’","This was how I would gradually improve my skills.","At the same time, I could give the dwarf something useful and receive his advice in return.","Without a proper master, it would be impossible for my skills to improve by leaps and bounds. However, as I had mentioned earlier, I had plenty of opportunities to practice.","’It’s already evening.’","While I was busy working, the sun had gradually descended, and the sky had begun to darken.","It was about time to prepare dinner and browse the Gallery while I was at it.","The more important of the two was browsing the Gallery.","An important post might have been buried while I was working.","’I wonder if Ludwig still hasn’t entered yet.’","I also considered the possibility that he had taken the sword and run, just as the dwarf feared.","This world was not as kind as I wanted to believe.","There were plenty of good people, but there were also plenty with rotten personalities.","[Apparently, the investigation team has scattered?]","I was browsing the Gallery after dinner and my cultivation session when I noticed that title.","So many new posts had appeared that I was checking mainly the popular ones, and one title immediately caught my attention.","It claimed that the investigation team dispatched by Eldorado had scattered in every direction.","There was no way I could simply pass over a title like that, so I immediately opened it.","Title: Apparently, the investigation team has scattered?","My clergyman friend just got back and told me. Apparently, the investigation team scattered at the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","According to my friend, the leader of the investigation team started a rebellion and escaped, but I don’t know the details. Anyway, it’s true that the investigation team fled.","It’ll be in the newspapers soon enough, but I’m spoiling it early so the Gallery users won’t be too shocked.","└ Hey, you just spoiled some huge news, you bastard.","└ Become a clergyman too if you’re jealous.","I immediately sent the admin a message.","He must have seen the post as well.","Just as I expected, he had already read it and replied immediately.","└ I’d rather be a wealthy unemployed man than a clergyman lol","└ Honestly, I want to be a wealthy unemployed man too. It’s terrifying here T_T","└ Wait, doesn’t that mean all of Grylls’s friends are gone?","└ Oh lololol, you’re right lol","└ What will Grylls do now that he’s all alone...? He even made a signpost.","└ Starting a rebellion is still better than dying.","└ They were practically forced into the forest. I would’ve fought back too lololol","└ Didn’t they also have the sword Grylls gave them?","└ Yeah. I heard it looked like it contained a green galaxy. That description made me wonder if the bastard was lying lol","└ What kind of sword glows green? Lololol","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Just so you know, Mr. Ludwig isn’t the kind of person who would accept someone’s goodwill and run away! He always prays to the Goddess and performs good deeds!]","[Wild Grylls: Forget that. Do you know where he is right now?]","I wanted his location, not a defense of his character.","After seeing that post, his current location was the only thing that mattered.","The contents were deeply unsettling.","The investigation team had scattered in every direction.","My heart sank as I wondered whether the dwarf’s concerns had become reality.","Most users remained skeptical, but I had no choice but to believe the post.","The sword’s description perfectly matched the one I had given Ludwig.","’Th-Then where is Ludwig right now?’","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Well... I’m sorry, but I can’t determine his current location...!]","[Wild Grylls: What is that supposed to mean?;;]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: It’s true! I’m receiving a message saying that he’s somewhere his location cannot be determined!]","[Wild Grylls: Then what about me? That doesn’t make any sense.]","Was the admin lying to me?","The suspicion briefly crossed my mind.","He had been able to determine my location without any trouble before.","He had told me I was at the exact center of the Forest of Four Seasons.","Yet now he claimed he could not locate Ludwig.","It was a complete contradiction.","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: I swear to the Goddess! I can’t determine his location, but I can still send him messages!]","[Wild Grylls: What does that have to do with anything?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: If a registered user dies, I receive a message saying the user no longer exists! Therefore, there’s a high possibility that he entered the Forest of Four Seasons!]","[Wild Grylls: Even so, it’s a little strange that you can’t determine his location.;;]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: You were able to use the Gallery from the very beginning! It’s much more likely that you’re the exceptional case!]","[Wild Grylls: That’s extremely convincing.]","I was not being sarcastic.","It really was.","It was better to treat me as an exception.","How many times had everyone been astonished by the things I had done until now?","It would also be strange to judge my experiences solely by this world’s standards.","’Anyway, there’s a high probability that he entered the Forest of Four Seasons...’","In that case, there was nothing I could do right now.","Since even his location could not be tracked in real time, I had no choice but to wait patiently.","[Wild Grylls: I suppose we have no choice but to wait.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Um...! I know this is a difficult situation, but could you please find Mr. Ludwig?!]","[Wild Grylls: I might be able to guide him toward my location, but I don’t think I can search for him.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: That alone would be enough! I’ll help you as much as I can!]","[Wild Grylls: How?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Hmm...!]","The admin contemplated the matter for a while before cautiously replying.","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Whenever I pray to the Goddess, I could ask her to help you find Mr. Ludwig?]","[Wild Grylls: Does she grant your requests just because you pray?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Yes!]","His confident answer left me speechless.","Did the Goddess really answer his prayers?","If so, that was what you could truly call doing something with a single click.","’I’d be willing to close my eyes and pray if it really worked.’","Of course I would.","Pooooour!","\"Ah, seriously. Again?\"","I just wished she would make this damn rain stop first.","Rain fell frequently in the forest, as one might expect from such a region.","That rain restricted Grylls’s activities.","However, the grasslands were divided into wet and dry seasons, making their climate different from the forest’s.","During the dry season, there were no restrictions on movement, and animals could roam freely.","It was currently the dry season.","The same applied to Ludwig, who had newly entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","He stood motionless, staring at a cave.","Under normal circumstances, he would have entered and explored it. However, his current situation made him hesitate.","The powerful ambient mana had rendered him almost completely incapable of using his own.","Fortunately, given his level of skill, he could still wield a minuscule amount.","Shimmer—","Even that tiny amount was enough to make the sword radiate green light.","Ludwig alternated his gaze between the sword and the cave entrance before nodding.","’It would be best to investigate.’","If he was lucky, the cave might be empty.","With that hope in mind, he entered.","A short while later—","\"Raaaaaargh!\"","Ludwig began fleeing from a three-headed lion."]},{"title":"Chapter 130","paragraphs":["Click (2)","Who was the most confused by the Holy Nation of Eldorado’s decision to dispatch an investigation team?","Kadir, the previous Hero’s close friend?","No.","Ludwig’s family or the families of the other investigators?","Not them either.","It was Asella, the renegade Hero who had ties to Ludwig.","’What in the world is the Holy Nation...?’","Inside a room at an inn where she had barely managed to secure food and lodging, Asella carefully studied a newspaper under the light of a single lamp.","[Shocking! Was the Renegade Hero Created by the Paladins’ Instructor?]","[Corrupt Ideology Inevitably Gives Rise to Misguided Convictions.]","[Eldorado Begins Ideological Inspections: Those Who Do Not Pray to the Goddess Ares Once a Day to Be Considered Subversives.]","It had only been one day.","These articles had poured out just one day after news spread that the investigation team had fled.","Their condemnatory tone made it seem as though they had been prepared in advance.","Asella was bewildered.","What pained her most of all was what they were saying about Ludwig.","[Former Paladin Instructor Ludwig Revealed to Have Insulted Ares.]","[Ludwig, the Blasphemous Paladin—Where Is He Now?]","[Paladins Trained Under Ludwig to Undergo Extensive Investigation...]","Ludwig was an instructor responsible for raising and training paladins.","Asella knew better than anyone how upright and uncompromising he was.","Had she not grown under his teachings before being selected as the Hero?","He had treated Asella so warmly that even she could tell he was especially fond of her.","To Asella, an orphan who had grown up starved of an adult’s affection, Ludwig had practically been a father.","’There must be... some misunderstanding...’","Asella clutched the newspaper tightly.","Eldorado had repeatedly disappointed her of late.","Nevertheless, Eldorado was a nation founded to worship the gods, including Ares.","It was also Eldorado that had taken in an orphan like Asella and raised her into a respectable paladin.","’Is all of this... my fault?’","Asella recalled the moment she had drawn the Holy Sword, Revolution.","The instant she drew it, the Goddess herself delivered an oracle.","Its contents had been difficult to believe.","It was a deeply shocking prophecy declaring that Asella would destroy Eldorado.","At first, she thought it was a misunderstanding, but by the time she came to her senses, she had already become a fugitive.","Eldorado subsequently proclaimed her a renegade on a national scale, leading to the present situation.","’I’m not a renegade...’","Asella knew better than anyone that she had not betrayed her faith.","Therefore, she concluded that the Goddess Ares had misunderstood her.","The notion that a goddess could be mistaken might sound profoundly blasphemous.","However, Asella’s circumstances were more than sufficient to cause such cognitive dissonance.","’Even if I prove that I’m not a renegade... will Teacher be able to restore his honor?’","Ludwig’s reputation had already begun plummeting.","Eldorado completely controlled the press, and this was a considerable incident.","Even the Immortal King incident appeared to be getting quietly swept under the rug, leaving her heart heavy.","Recently, Eldorado had done nothing but disappoint her.","Perhaps this was its true face.","Perhaps it had merely worn the mask of a \"Holy Nation\" and pretended to be righteous all this time.","’The Holy Nation I knew wasn’t like this...’","The Eldorado Asella knew had truly been a beautiful place.","It was a nation where everyone lived happily under the protection of the gods, including the Goddess Ares.","It was a place protected by paladins devoted to service and sacrifice.","A place where even orphaned children could not only realize their dreams but become Heroes.","Yet Eldorado’s recent conduct was the complete opposite.","’It must have lost its way...’","Just as people sometimes lost their way, nations were likely no different.","Eldorado had originally been founded to resist the threat of the Demon King, Mephisto.","However, as culture developed, Mephisto began pursuing conciliatory policies.","He had become so obsessed with ball games that he came to consider violence taboo.","He had even offered a courteous apology, leaving Eldorado without a clear purpose.","’At times like this, you have to keep believing. Abandoning someone when they’re struggling is the worst thing you can do.’","It was one of the life lessons Ludwig had taught her.","Remaining beside those who were suffering was the true virtue of a paladin.","The same should apply even when the one suffering was a nation.","Asella steeled her resolve once more.","She remained completely unaware that she herself was one of the people suffering most in the entire world.","The other was currently working himself to the bone in the Forest of Four Seasons.","’I wonder what Mr. Grylls is doing right now?’","Curious about Grylls’s situation, Asella accessed the Gallery.","Because he had given Ludwig a sword, the investigation team had been able to scatter safely.","Had the newspapers not claimed that Ludwig had wielded an evil \"demonic sword\" to help wicked individuals escape?","Various testimonies had also been circulating throughout the Gallery, so Asella was certain it was Grylls’s gift.","[I Seriously Resent the Heavens.]","\"Huh?!\"","A strange sound escaped Asella as if she had bitten her tongue.","Anyone would have reacted that way after seeing the title of Grylls’s latest post.","Since ancient times, the heavens had been regarded as the domain of the gods.","Whether he meant it figuratively or literally, she could not simply ignore it.","’Has Mr. Grylls committed blasphemy again?’","Since he committed blasphemy at every opportunity, she immediately opened the post.","If that was what he was doing, she intended to give him a stern warning.","Title: I Seriously Resent the Heavens","Wild Grylls","(Video of rain pouring outside the cave)","How long has it even been since the last rainfall? Why the hell is it raining again?","The oven and furnace are fine because I covered them with waterproof tarps, but I think my fish traps are going to get washed away again.","The heavens definitely hate me. This is why I curse them.","└ Heavenly Demon: You resent the heavens...? Does that mean you dislike this lady as well?","└ Wild Grylls: No, no. You’re the exception, Heavenly Demon. Haha. You stand even higher than the heavens.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is also true.","└ Ugh, he’s going to wear his tongue out from all that flattery lololol","└ Just look at how perfectly those two play along with each other lololol","└ Are you two seriously using the Gallery to socialize? Lol","└ Are you going to the Forest of Four Seasons to socialize with them? Lolol","└ We should allow this one. That’s gone beyond ordinary socializing. ;;","└ Lololol, the Forest of Four Seasons should obviously be treated as an exception~","└ SwordMaster: Since you’re in a forest, it seems to rain frequently. Why not devote this opportunity entirely to training?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve been doing that constantly, but my aura just keeps getting bigger.","└ SwordMaster: Wait, what?;; What kind of training are you doing to become absurdly strong like that?","└ Wild Grylls: Nothing special... I eat, practice my cultivation method, consume an inner core, and practice my cultivation method again. That’s all.","└ SwordMaster: You consume inner cores as though they were medicine?","└ Wild Grylls: For now, yes. I’ve set aside enough for Ppareumbo to eat, but I still have extras. Is that strange?","└ SwordMaster: What the fuck? I’ve never met anyone who gobbles down inner cores like medicine. ;;","└ That’s why he’s becoming ridiculously strong lolololol","└ At this rate, won’t his aura eventually reach the heavens?","└ Is he going to shout, \"My aura is the aura that will pierce the heavens!\" someday?","└ Wasn’t that what that absurdly powerful Sword Saint used to shout? Lololol","└ Yeah, lololol. I thought it was so damn cool back then, but now it’s just... lolololol","└ What are you talking about? It’s still cool.","└ Starlight Princess: Don’t resent the heavens too much. I resented them too, but I was fortunate enough to survive.","└ Wild Grylls: That wasn’t the heavens. I was the one who helped you.","└ Starlight Princess: When you put it that way, I don’t really have anything to say. Still, you mustn’t think too negatively! It’s always important to maintain a positive attitude.","└ Wild Grylls: Was that how you lived, Starlight Princess?","└ Starlight Princess: No, haha. I spent every day waiting to die.","└ Wild Grylls: Ma’am...;;","└ Starlight Princess: But just as I met you, Mr. Grylls, you might meet a benefactor someday too!","└ When will that day come?","└ One thing’s for sure—it’ll take months at the very least lolol","└ Apparently, Ludwig entered the Forest of Four Seasons, so they’ll meet someday. In heaven, of course. Lol","└ Youuuuu are seriously horrible lololol","The post had not been expressing resentment toward Ares, but toward the sky itself.","Still, his dislike of the gods was indirectly apparent throughout it.","’A person who hates the gods because he doesn’t want to hate people...’","Asella was troubled.","Would she be able to change Grylls’s mind?","Yet if he could not resent the gods, he would probably begin resenting people instead.","Grylls’s mindset was something she would need to contemplate carefully.","Humans were creatures incapable of living normally without hating something.","There was a reason their emotions were described through joy, anger, sorrow, and pleasure.","’Then I should guide him toward hating them a little less!’","Asella’s characteristic optimism asserted itself.","She left a comment on Grylls’s post, where new replies were still appearing steadily.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: At times like this, you should pray to the heavens! Try praying for the rain to stop!","└ Wild Grylls: Stop trying to sell me snake oil.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Gods don’t sell snake oil!!! Please, just listen to me this once!","└ Wild Grylls: Sigh. Fine. What am I supposed to say?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: \"I beseech Ares, Goddess of War and Wisdom. Please quell the heavens’ wrath and grant me the freedom to go about my activities!\"","└ Wild Grylls: Just wait. I’ll go pray with all my heart.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Very good!","Asella quietly waited for his next comment, praying that something good would happen.","About thirty seconds passed.","Grylls did not leave another comment.","Instead, he created a new post that made Asella’s eyes widen.","[You Fraudulent Admin!!!]","Wondering what had happened, she opened it without hesitation.","Title: You Fraudulent Admin!!!","Wild Grylls","(Video of a torrential downpour outside the cave, as though a hole had opened in the sky)","What? God will listen if I pray?","What a load of crap. The gods definitely hate me too.","Perhaps all her persuasion had borne fruit, because Grylls had replied that he would pray.","In truth, Grylls had only done it because he had nothing better to do, but Asella was simply delighted.","’This should help him let go of at least some of his hatred toward the gods.’","He had prayed, only for the rain to become even heavier.","That was the entire point of his post.","Asella stared blankly at the Gallery for a moment before quietly disconnecting.","’Lady Ares can’t grant every prayer!’","It was an answer befitting the ever-optimistic Asella.","Knock, knock, knock—","\"Excuse me, guest. Are you inside?\"","Someone knocked on the door just as she closed the Gallery.","Asella recognized the voice as the innkeeper’s, but immediately began circulating her mana on instinct.","Once her mana was circulating, she examined not only the presence behind the door but every presence throughout the inn.","’There’s someone... beside the innkeeper.’","It was not merely their presence that was suspicious.","’Are you certain she’s here?’","’Yes. I distinctly saw her orange hair.’","’Then we will enter immediately. You will receive your reward after we capture the renegade alive.’","’Oh, thank you very much.’","They were speaking extremely quietly, but Asella heard every word.","Rather than the sounds directly reaching her ears, it felt as though their presences themselves had taken form.","’They’ve already tracked me down...’","She had not even stayed here for several days, yet her pursuers had already caught up.","Asella bit her lip and hurriedly prepared to leave.","The first thing she did was seize the Holy Sword, Revolution, before heading toward the window.","’I still need more time. Time for this misunderstanding to be resolved.’","Asella opened the window and leaped outside.","Crash!","At the same moment, she heard the door being forced open.","The pursuit squad had smashed it down.","Of course, Asella had already escaped through the window, leaving them with nothing to find.","’Goddess, please grant me the strength to overcome these trials.’","Without losing her faith in the Goddess, Asella fled.","At the same time Asella began running to shake off her pursuers—","\"Aaaaaagh! You bastards! Get lost!! This is my home!\"","\"Kyeeeeng!\"","\"Keeng! Kek!\"","Grylls was struggling against an unexpected wave of beasts.","\"Get out of my house right now!\""]},{"title":"Chapter 131","paragraphs":["Click (3)","I really hate rain. I hated it even before I fell into this godforsaken place.When it rained, I couldn’t see the clear blue sky, and the weather became unbearably humid.","The rainy season was especially awful. It was already hot enough, but the humidity went completely berserk on top of that. It felt like it was going to kill me.","If air conditioners had never been invented, wouldn’t I have melted into a puddle long ago?","Rumble—!!","\"What absolutely fucking shitty weather.\"","I cursed as I watched the torrential rain pouring down so heavily that it nearly blocked my entire field of vision.","I had even prayed for the rain to stop, but what the hell was this?","Instead of answering my prayer, someone had punched a hole in the sky.","This was why I hated gods. I liked religious people, but I hated gods.","’Does that bastard seriously hate me so much that he’s telling me to go fuck myself?’","If so, what a petty bastard. I shook my head.","Anyway, since this was the first rain in almost a week, I had prepared thoroughly.","I put up waterproof covers to keep the oven and furnace from getting wet, and I brought the container holding the fish into the cave.","Unfortunately, I had no choice but to leave the fish traps in the river where they were. It had been raining since morning.","The rain had startled me awake, and I had rushed around taking emergency measures.","\"I’ll have to learn the signs that rain is coming.\"","I had roughly figured out how often it rained. But if I could identify the warning signs, I would be able to prepare much more reliably.","It would be nice if I could rely on common knowledge from my original world, but...","This was the Four Seasons Forest. Ordinary common sense didn’t apply here.","I would have to identify the warning signs unique to the Four Seasons Forest.","’When is this going to stop?’","I gazed outside at the downpour. It showed no sign of letting up.","This storm was on an entirely different level from the last one. The river must have risen tremendously by now.","And as the water rose, all sorts of sea creatures would probably swim upstream.","’What’ll come up this time? Surely it won’t be something like a shark, right?’","It would be best to remain on high alert for a while. I didn’t want to get robbed blind again like last time.","I was blankly watching the endless rain when—","\"Keeeeng!\"","\"Hm?\"","An animal’s cry pierced through the pounding rain.","Wondering what was happening, I looked outside the cave.","\"Keeeeeng!\"","\"Keng! Keng!\"","\"Squeak! Squeak!\"","A whole crowd of small to medium-sized animals had gathered outside the cave.","There were raccoons like the one Fast Sloth had butchered last time, along with rabbits, deer, wild boars, enormous rats, and even animals I had never seen before.","Just as I wondered why these creatures were gathered outside, the raccoon standing at the very front met my gaze.","\"Keng! Keeeng!\"","\"Squeak-squeak?\"","\"Oink?\"","I had a bad feeling about this. I cautiously closed the iron gate.","The moment those animals flooded into the cave, the place would descend into chaos.","Besides, there was no telling what diseases those beasts might be carrying.","\"Kek! Kek-kek!\"","When the raccoon saw me quietly closing the gate, it pointed a finger at me and began protesting.","It seemed to be saying something along the lines of, \"We should all help one another survive! Do you only care about yourself, you selfish bastard?!\"","My answer was extremely simple.","I casually raised my middle finger.","I had no idea whether the animals understood its meaning, but as long as it made me feel better, that was enough.","’You can’t trust these damn beasts.’","Of course, Fast Sloth—the one who lived in symbiosis with the adorable Wonmo—was an exception.","More importantly, these animals were partly to blame. They should have built their homes sooner.","’Not that I’m in any position to say that after stealing this cave from its original owner...’","Anyway, I wasn’t letting anyone into this house. They were welcome to try forcing their way in.","I snorted and firmly barricaded the cave entrance. Apparently, the raccoon had an idea of its own.","\"Keng!\"","\"Oiiink!\"","The raccoon slapped the wild boar on the flank.","The boar immediately began pawing the ground with its hind legs as if preparing to charge.","The moment I saw that, an instinctive sense of unease washed over me.","That bastard was definitely going to charge.","In that case, I had only one option.","Heavy armament.","Those bastards couldn’t get past the iron gate anyway, so I could use it to wage a defensive siege.","\"Oiiiiink—!!!\"","While I was equipping myself, the boar charged at tremendous speed.","Perhaps it was only natural for an animal that inhabited the Four Seasons Forest, but its speed was extraordinary.","The same went for its size. It was as huge as one of the monsters from an old movie.","However, after surviving in the Four Seasons Forest for half a month, I had learned one important lesson.","Shunk—!!","And that was that range was everything.","Whoever had the longer reach was king.","Before the boar could slam into the iron gate, I drove my aura straight through the center of its forehead.","It might have been a little risky if I were still using the Heavenly Demon’s Sword.","But the weapon I was holding now was the Mithricon Sword.","Its physical size had already grown to ridiculous proportions, and the aura blade produced by the Mithricon Sword was even larger.","Thanks to that, I stopped the boar before it could collide with the gate.","Thud!","The boar collapsed with its forehead pierced through.","The impact sent a tremor and a deafening thud through the pounding rain.","Most of the beasts appeared stunned, apparently never imagining that the boar would die so easily.","Keeping my flame-like aura blazing around the sword, I beckoned with the blade.","\"Come at me.\"","\"Come at me, you fucking beasts! Come at me!!\"","\"Keeeeeng!!!\"","And thus began a siege fought across a single iron gate.","Using my overwhelming reach and the gate as a barrier, I fought to keep the animals from getting inside.","Clang—!","I occasionally took some damage from the rabbits and deer, whose kicks were incredibly powerful.","Thank goodness it was an iron gate. If it had been made of wood, it would have shattered long ago.","\"Get the hell out of my house!!!\"","\"Keeeeeng!\"","The siege to defend my home finally ended with the death of their leader—the raccoon.","Once the raccoon died, the other animals scattered in every direction.","Still breathing heavily from the unexpected siege, I eventually collapsed onto the ground.","’Seriously, the craziest things keep happening...’","It hadn’t been like this last time. How strange.","Maybe the torrential rain had destroyed all their homes.","I let out a long sigh and looked beyond the iron gate.","Various animals lay dead outside, including the boar I had killed first.","I would have liked to butcher them, but I didn’t have the time.","’And with all this rain, they’ll rot quickly.’","It was a shame, but I would probably have to throw them away.","I could just dig a pit and bury them—the same place where I had buried the gorillas.","Title: Just Fought a Siege","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the dead animals outside)","(Photo of the iron gate on the verge of breaking)","These beasts suddenly tried to force their way into my house, so I fought a siege against them.","If the homeowner says no, that means no. What kind of animals try to barge in by force? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Could you not have shown them a little mercy? If you behave too heartlessly, you are bound to lose the people’s support.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not living in civilization. I’m in the wilderness ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Ah, right. I had forgotten. It slipped my mind for a moment.","└ Sword Master: A siege against animals... How absurd. You weren’t injured, were you?","└ Wild Grylls: Nope. I just sliced them apart with aura from a distance, and they all died.","└ Sword Master: It seems to have been strangely effective.","└ What did the animals do wrong? They only wanted shelter from the rain...","└ Wild Grylls: Last time, I saw some raccoon steal my fasting pills. That taught me never to trust those damn beasts.","└ Didn’t Fast Sloth tear that one in half?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah, yeah. Still better than letting them make a mess of my house.","└ By the way, has anyone ever fought a siege against ordinary animals rather than monsters?","└ Humanoid monsters like orcs and goblins sometimes raid settlements, but I’ve never heard of animals doing it.","└ It has happened. Wolves are the animals that have fought humans most frequently.","└ Why aren’t there any wolves among those animals? You’d normally expect to see some.","└ They’re territorial animals, so maybe they’re somewhere else?","After watching the users converse among themselves, I closed the Gallery.","When I looked outside again, the rain seemed slightly weaker than before.","It would probably stop in about an hour.","’From now on, I should assume it’ll rain roughly once a week...’","Animals come looking for shelter whenever it rains heavily.","I recorded that in my journal.","Completely unaware that I had just fought a grueling siege, Wonmo was sleeping without a care in the world.","Then again, the siege had been entirely unexpected, so I could understand.","Drip— Drip—","The rain stopped roughly an hour later. I looked outside.","The bright sun greeted me as if it had never rained at all.","Thud! Thud!","Not that it helped me much. I still had to go through the trouble of burying all the animal carcasses.","Praying that no earthworms would appear, I dug into the ground.","Fortunately, no enormous earthworms emerged.","\"Pwah!\"","\"...And what are you supposed to be?\"","Only a strange mole popped out.","The mole stared at me with its bright, round eyes before hurriedly scurrying away.","Apparently, it had been hiding underground when the sudden downpour flooded its home.","After staring after it in disbelief for a moment, I finished burying the animal carcasses.","’The drainage channels are working properly... I guess the only thing left is to head upriver.’","The river would still be greatly swollen, so there was no need to rush.","I had plenty of other things to do anyway, so taking my time was fine.","’If this happens every time it rains, it’s going to be a serious headache.’","Now I had to consider not only the animals inhabiting the Four Seasons Forest, but the weather as well.","I checked the oven and furnace for damage, then armed myself.","Since I had no idea what might emerge from the swollen river, I equipped the Heavenly Demon’s Sword instead of the Mithricon Sword.","Wonmo was still sleeping peacefully, so I left Fast Sloth behind to watch over him.","By the time I reached the river, I came face-to-face with exactly what I had expected.","Roooooar—!!!","\"Goddammit.\"","I cursed as I stared at the swollen river.","It looked like someone had turned a waterfall sideways.","Naturally, the fish traps I had installed had been swept away without a trace.","Fortunately, there was something to salvage around the riverbank. Several fish were flopping around on the ground nearby.","If I took them back with me, they should be enough to last until I obtained new traps.","’But...’","One fish in particular caught my eye.","Last time, it had been an eel. This time, it was a pufferfish.","Yes, a pufferfish—the kind with a round body shaped like Wonmo’s.","A creature that lived in the sea had somehow been swept all the way here.","’Did it rain over the ocean too? Or what?’","Some species of eel lived in freshwater, so I could understand that much. But the pufferfish was even stranger.","It should have been a species that lived exclusively in the sea, so by what mechanism had it been swept all the way here?","Of course, regardless of the answer, I had no intention of eating it.","Pufferfish were poisonous.","Their poison alone was enough to kill a person. And since this was the Four Seasons Forest, the poison would be worse, if anything—certainly not milder.","’I’ve heard they’re incredibly difficult to prepare too.’","You could get away with preparing an ordinary fish rather carelessly, but not a pufferfish.","They were notoriously tricky to handle. Simply \"following along\" with someone else’s instructions wouldn’t cut it.","According to the Gallery, countless people had died after watching videos on how to prepare pufferfish and trying it themselves.","Unless you were a professional, it was best not even to touch one.","’Just to be safe, I should send it back.’","Holding my shield in front of me, I gently nudged the pufferfish toward the river.","Apparently feeling threatened, the pufferfish puffed up its body.","Now that I looked more closely, it wasn’t an ordinary pufferfish. It was a porcupinefish covered in spines.","The instant one of those spines pricked me, I would probably be poisoned.","The medicine the All-Father had given me had granted me resistance to poison, but there was still no harm in being careful.","’I’ll send you back home, so hurry up and go.’","I was gently tapping the pufferfish and rolling it along when—","Grrrrrrumble—!!!","An ominous noise came from its body.","Boom-boom-boom—!!!","Its spines literally exploded in every direction.","Fortunately, I had raised my shield the instant I sensed danger, so I suffered practically no damage.","The problem was that it didn’t end there.","Boom! Bang! Bang! Kaboom!","The ejected spines exploded again, releasing clouds of purple mist.","It puffed up its body once, fired its spines twice, and then made those spines explode for a third layer of defense.","\"...\"","I couldn’t help but marvel at the fact that it possessed three separate self-defense mechanisms.","And even that wasn’t the end.","Sssshhh—","New spines regenerated from its smooth body like a shark replacing its teeth.","The moment I saw that, I freaked out, abandoned my plan to gently push it back, and kicked it as hard as I could.","Splash!","My kick sent the pufferfish sailing directly into the river.","Now it would drift downstream to the lake—or perhaps return to the sea.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Coughing violently, I hurried back home.","’How did this happen when I was being so careful?’","This truly was an astonishing place.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 132","paragraphs":["Click (4)","I had finally come to a realization.","This damned forest was the complete opposite of a children’s fairy tale.","Things that looked obviously dangerous—bears, tigers, and even the Guardian, for example—were actually manageable.","Their appearance instinctively warned you that they were dangerous and that your life would be at risk if you failed to respond.","But that wasn’t true of the little ones.","Things that looked ordinary—or were genuinely tiny—were far more dangerous.","It was the same in martial arts novels.","Beware of children, the elderly, and women.","Small creatures had survived in the Four Seasons Forest despite their diminutive size.","And what did that mean?","It meant they possessed at least two ways of utterly fucking up their opponents.","Why two instead of one?","One was a visible move meant to threaten the enemy.","The other was an unexpected trump card designed to catch the enemy completely off guard.","I had concluded that a creature needed both to survive in the Four Seasons Forest.","Until now, that had been closer to speculation.","But after what the porcupinefish had just done to me, I was certain.","’The saying \"small peppers are the hottest\" fits perfectly.’","Except this pepper wasn’t merely spicy. Eating it would literally melt my body.","At this rate, would a yellow rat that fired lightning appear someday?","Or perhaps a dinosaur that breathed fire would start roaming around.","Why was I suddenly saying all this?","\"Wohmo...\"","\"Squeak?\"","\"Daddy’s bodeh won’t moof.\"","Because the porcupinefish’s poison had left my body half-crippled.","My slurred speech was the least of my problems. My body refused to move the way I wanted it to.","I kept dropping anything I tried to pick up, and I couldn’t even walk without staggering.","Fortunately, I had barely managed to keep my balance and return to the cave. Otherwise, I might have collapsed in the middle of the forest.","Rustle—","Fast Sloth had been silently watching me. Apparently realizing that my condition was serious, it handed me something.","It was an elixir filled with shimmering golden liquid.","I barely managed to take it and gulped it down.","That wasn’t all. I also drank the antidote I had prepared in advance.","Finally, I circulated my internal energy according to my cultivation method.","I did everything I possibly could.","\"Ugh...\"","As time passed, my body gradually returned to normal. Strength began flowing back into my limbs.","I let out a long sigh and reviewed what had just happened.","That had been an incredibly close call.","’If I hadn’t taken the medicine the All-Father gave me, I would’ve collapsed on the spot.’","My resistance to poison was the only reason it had been this mild. Without even that, I probably would have died instantly.","What was the name of pufferfish poison again?","It started with \"tetra\" or something.","Anyway, it was one of the deadliest poisons in the world.","And since the creature inhabited the Four Seasons Forest, its poison would have been even more vicious—certainly not weaker.","’This is a place where the smallest things are the scariest.’","Until now, I had consistently applied insect repellent to avoid being bitten.","What would happen if I were poisoned by some venomous bug or if a wound developed a secondary infection?","I didn’t even want to imagine it.","I carefully examined my body to ensure nothing was wrong and checked whether all my senses had properly returned.","Perhaps thanks to the combination of the elixir and antidote, I couldn’t feel anything particularly wrong.","My internal energy cultivation was proceeding smoothly too, so I appeared to have made a complete recovery.","Every Gallery user had agreed that there was no better way to assess one’s physical condition than by practicing an internal energy cultivation method.","’If I’d been missing even one of the things I had, my life would’ve been in danger. The Gallery really did save my life.’","This was a place where the slightest lapse in vigilance could send you straight to the grave.","You had to remain wary of everything if you wanted to survive.","’Putting that aside, should I build a proper door...?’","I stared at the iron gate blocking the entrance and remembered the siege from earlier that day.","The animals had presumably lost their homes in the torrential rain and attempted to force their way into mine.","Fortunately, I had easily stopped them with the aura I had honed thus far. But there was no telling what might come next time.","If a creature as strong as Fast Sloth threatened me and demanded that I hand over my home...","That would have been a little difficult.","’At the very least, I need to fortify this place whenever it rains.’","I planned to continue using the same tactic—using the iron gate as a shield while attacking through it.","If I installed an actual door, I would lose the ability to counterattack. More importantly, it would probably be smashed apart in no time.","A single charge from that boar could send the door I had worked so hard to build crashing down, just like my hopes and dreams.","’If I’m unlucky, I might have to defend against a monster wave once a week.’","Grumbling inwardly, I got to my feet.","My body had fully recovered, so I didn’t have time to sit around feeling sorry for myself.","Just as the shark giant had previously found its way to my shelter, there was no telling what kind of animal might visit this time.","I would have to remain vigilant and watch the surrounding area for at least a day or two.","Crackle! Pop!","The first thing I did was light a campfire to dry the surroundings, which had become damp from the rain.","After that, I returned to the riverbank to collect the fish flopping on the ground and inspected the drainage channels.","By the time I had finished everything, evening was approaching.","The sky was growing dark.","’Tomorrow will be Day Eighteen, right?’","I thought about it as I marked another line on the cave wall.","Roughly three days had passed since the expedition incident.","If a man named Ludwig had truly entered the Four Seasons Forest, his first day would be coming to an end around now.","Was he still alive and well?","Or was he dead?","Unlike me, he probably didn’t have any elixirs.","’If I’d known this would happen, I would’ve given him a bottle.’","\"...\"","Regret was still regret, no matter how quickly it came.","I prayed that Ludwig would safely reach the place where I was staying.","Honestly, if even this prayer went unanswered, then God would be something far beyond merely petty.","Rumble!","Or so I almost said, but there were some things in human affairs that simply couldn’t be helped.","I glanced outside.","Despite the thunder, no rain fell.","Could the heavens genuinely be listening to me?","’Nah. It must be a coincidence.’","Resolutely dismissing the idea, I accessed the Gallery.","I wondered what everyone had discussed while I had been cleaning up.","Normally, the Gallery would have been filled with all sorts of random shitposts. Recently, however, most of the discussions had revolved around the expedition.","That remained true now.","More than half the posts concerned El Dorado or the expedition.","Most topics quickly lost people’s interest, but this one seemed to have staying power because it was somewhat connected to reality.","’Nothing here particularly interests me.’","The only thing that could really be called a new topic was the Messiah Empire—more specifically, its emperor.","Apparently, the emperor, who had been sick and on the verge of death, had regained his health.","As for what kind of man he was, they said he had led the Messiah Empire to prosperity.","He had given his full support to Ash, who was now renowned as a Sword Master, and had also implemented policies that provided various benefits.","But that was as far as his talents went. His diplomacy was mediocre, so he was best described as an emperor suited strictly for domestic affairs.","Title: What happens to the Crown Prince now that the Emperor’s back on his feet?","Personally, I’d rather the throne still pass to Crown Prince Arnold. I fucking hate the emperor.","└ Why do you hate him?","└ The policies that emperor bastard implemented sent the prices of magic items through the roof.","└ Ah, kekekeke. I know exactly what you mean.","└ Aren’t the side effects still pretty bad?","└ Yeah. This is actually better than it used to be.","└ If he hadn’t pulled that bullshit, public opinion wouldn’t have gone down the drain, kekeke.","└ The current Messiah emperor seriously has no business handling diplomacy, kekeke.","└ AbsoluteSupremeArnoldRules: That was only true at the time. Didn’t things improve afterward? Policies are meant to be judged over the long term.","└ Fuck off. Do you even know how much we’re still paying to import magical goods from the Iris Kingdom?","└ This bastard’s probably a noble. That’s why he has no idea how hard life is for commoners.","└ AbsoluteSupremeArnoldRules: That’s not true. His Majesty was looking far into the future. I’m certain future generations will evaluate him favorably.","└ So what? We’re struggling to put food on the table right now, kekeke.","└ Besides, the average level of martial strength across the continent went up because of the posts Sword Master made, so those policies are fucking meaningless now, kekeke.","└ Can’t you just admit he’s fucking incompetent? Why all the excuses? Kek.","└ AbsoluteSupremeArnoldRules: You uneducated vermin. Do you have any idea who my father is?","└ Why? Did your mother never tell you?","└ Oh, kekekekeke.","└ Terrifying. Absolutely terrifying, kekekeke.","└ What does that mean?","└ He’s indirectly mocking him for growing up alone with his mother and not having a father, kekeke.","└ We really have to explain jokes like that now? Kekeke.","Well, it was the same Gallery as always—a place overflowing with every kind of joke imaginable.","But with nothing except political posts at the moment, it had become far less entertaining.","Judging by the fact that the head moderator wasn’t intervening, he seemed to be absent.","The Heavenly Demon only removed posts that went too far. Nothing more, nothing less.","’There’s a Cheonggu match tomorrow, so that’s a relief.’","Political discourse would obviously be swept away by the dopamine rush of every goal.","I wondered how many people would lose their minds tomorrow.","Would Cheonggu Princess avoid becoming one of them?","I planned to remain at the shelter tomorrow as well, so I could browse the Gallery without worrying.","If I wandered around unnecessarily, some strange creature might show up at my shelter while I was gone.","’I should stick to smoked food until tomorrow.’","There might be another creature like the shark giant that could track me by scent.","Of course, there was no guarantee that something like that would appear again. There was simply no harm in being prepared.","’But why does it feel so cold?’","Maybe it was because the rain had been a torrential downpour rather than an ordinary shower.","As the moisture evaporated, the temperature also dropped enough to make me shiver.","Thank goodness I had a campfire. Without it, I would already have been trembling uncontrollably.","The uniform Cheonggu Princess had given me also helped. Its long sleeves and trousers provided excellent insulation.","’I should use the hide as a blanket.’","I had originally been using the tiger hide as a carpet, but I planned to use it as a blanket tonight.","With the temperature dropping so suddenly, the campfire alone probably wouldn’t be enough.","The human body was fragile. I had to keep it warm by any means necessary.","One mistake, and I might ascend to heaven in my sleep.","Crackle! Pop!","I added more firewood to the campfire, raising the temperature inside the cave.","I could feel the chill gradually fading. The cave was becoming pleasantly warm.","\"Squeak...\"","My cave companions approached the campfire to warm themselves as well.","Wonmo lay down right beside it and even began dozing off.","’Why does he look so fat now?’","I had noticed him growing plumper as time passed, but... now he was completely round.","At this rate, he might soon start rolling across the floor, just like his name suggested.","Still, it was fine because he was cute.","Being round made him even cuter.","Besides, gaining weight in the wilderness meant he had accumulated plenty of energy reserves.","’He’s still young, so eating a lot should be good for him, right?’","Food was already scarce here. The fact that he could gain weight at all was a good thing.","Maybe it was because I practiced an internal energy cultivation method, but instead of gaining fat, I felt as though I was only putting on muscle.","As far as I knew, muscles—especially human muscles—weren’t particularly energy-efficient compared to those of other animals.","’It’s not like I can afford not to build muscle.’","With danger lurking everywhere, muscle was essential. It might not be very efficient, but I had no choice.","I posted in the Gallery that I was calling it a day, then lay down on the floor.","The chilly weather made me instinctively curl into myself.","\"Fast Sloth, you should get under the blanket too. It’s cold.\"","I had already covered Wonmo separately, so I invited Fast Sloth next.","Fast Sloth merely stared at me without doing anything.","I spread open the blanket and invited it again.","\"Come in here.\"","Fast Sloth slowly backed away.","Did it really dislike me that much?","’Wait a minute. Come to think of it, that bastard still hasn’t washed itself, has it?’","Its body was probably crawling with mold and insects. I had completely forgotten.","In the end, Fast Sloth went to sleep a short distance away.","It was near the campfire, so I wasn’t worried.","Before going to sleep, I quietly closed my eyes and circulated the mana within my body.","Rather than practicing a cultivation method, I simply wanted to feel the mana itself.","Even that could serve as a form of training.","’I still have no idea how to create an Aura Blade.’","Would I really be able to control the aura that kept increasing day and night?","I did my best to suppress my anxiety and drifted off to sleep.","The weather continued growing colder, but thanks to the campfire, I was able to endure it.","And so, that eventful day came to an end.","The following morning—","\"B-B-B-Brrr...\"","The biting cold woke me early.","Why was it so damn cold?","I couldn’t believe that a single torrential downpour had turned the weather into this mess.","’C-Campfire... I need to light the campfire first...’","Wrapping both arms around myself, I stepped outside.","And then—","\"...Huh?\"","A completely white forest greeted me.","Forgetting even the cold, I stared around at the snow-white landscape.","Everything was white, no matter where I looked.","White powder had piled atop both the oven and the furnace.","And that white substance was none other than—","\"Don’t tell me it snowed?\"","It was snow.","I muttered in disbelief.","This was why the place was called the Four Seasons Forest.","\"...This is fucking ridiculous.\"","I felt as though I finally understood the reason.","\"...\"","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 133","paragraphs":["Winter (1)","I had assumed the name Four Seasons Forest was purely metaphorical.","A demonic realm overflowing with every imaginable environmental feature, where a variety of seasons seemed to live and breathe.","That interpretation wasn’t exactly wrong. Even across the river, numerous different terrains stretched out before me.","Of those, I had thought the volcanic region was truly beyond salvation.","But the volcanic region wasn’t the only hopeless place.","This place was just as hopeless.","Title: It snowed, haha","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the snow-covered forest)","(Photo of the ground blanketed in white snow)","(Photo of the tools covered in snow)","It was fucking freezing this morning, and I couldn’t figure out why. Turns out it snowed overnight?","Yesterday, it was pouring like the middle of the rainy season, and now this happens out of nowhere. What a headache, haha.","How the fuck am I supposed to clear away all this shitty white garbage?","└ Heavenly Demon: How beautiful. But how could the season change overnight?","└ Sword Master: It must be because this is the Four Seasons Forest. As expected, that place is completely divorced from common sense.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Just as the Heavenly Demon said, it’s pretty. It looks like somewhere from a fairy tale.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. How unusual for you to say something sensible.","└ Cheonggu Princess: I feel like I’ll get banned if I keep going, so I’m not doing it anymore, haha.","└ Can something like that really happen overnight? That’s fucking incredible.","└ That’s why it’s called the Four Seasons Forest.","└ How are you supposed to prepare when the seasons change without warning? Humans seriously can’t live there, kekeke.","└ Most people die within a day anyway. Grylls would’ve been killed by Mad Dog if he hadn’t had the Gallery.","└ Starlight Princess: It’s strange that the season suddenly changed to winter. Weren’t there any warning signs?","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of Wonmo after growing so fat that he became round) This guy did gain weight extremely quickly.","└ Starlight Princess: Oh my. He’s absolutely adorable. The name Wonmo suits him perfectly.","└ Hey, pick him up and roll him. I want to know whether he really rolls.","└ Kekekekeke. What if he actually rolls really well?","└ Wonmo! Roll out!","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly awful.","└ PraiseTheSun: Wow. It almost never snows in our country, but it must snow over there whenever it gets the chance.","└ Does it even snow in Setan? Isn’t it a desert?","└ It does, but only once in a blue moon. The problem is that any rain or snow over there is practically a natural disaster, so we’re screwed whenever it happens.","└ Why? Doesn’t the sand absorb all the water anyway?","└ If the packed sand collapses, we’re fucked. Besides, most houses in Setan are built from mud, so they’re extremely vulnerable to rain.","└ Passing Dwarf: Aren’t you cold? I heard those clothes are pretty thin.","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. I’m fuuuuucking freezing. Can you give me a set of clothes?","└ Passing Dwarf: I’ll give you whatever I have left over. But I’ll have to ask my friend if you want something custom-made.","└ Wild Grylls: Ask him for now. If that isn’t enough, tell him I’ll give him another fully grown mandrake.","└ Passing Dwarf: Okay, wait a bit. It might take some time to find winter clothes that fit you.","The sudden arrival of winter was already a problem, but the most serious issue was the sharp drop in temperature.","Perhaps because of their fur, Wonmo and Fast Sloth seemed capable of enduring it.","I wasn’t.","The cold felt as though it were slicing into my flesh. Even wrapping myself in the hide I had been using as a carpet did little to help.","’I miss central heating.’","How wonderful would it be if I could simply turn on the heat?","Shivering violently, I looked around the area near the cave.","\"...\"","Fortunately, nothing particularly noteworthy stood out except the thick blanket of snow.","But that alone wasn’t enough to put me at ease. I still had to investigate the other areas.","’I wonder if winter came to the gorillas’ territory too.’","It was likely, but I couldn’t be certain.","That area was a tropical rainforest.","I had never heard of winter coming to a tropical rainforest.","Then again, this was the Four Seasons Forest, so it wasn’t entirely impossible.","I barely managed to warm myself beside the campfire as I waited for a message from the dwarf.","To distract myself from the cold, I also searched the Gallery for information.","└ Wild Grylls: It’s freezing. Can’t I do something with my internal energy cultivation method?","└ Heavenly Demon: Circulating your cultivation method should raise your body temperature somewhat. However, you will have to maintain it continuously.","└ Sword Master: The Heavenly Demon is right. Think of it as roughly similar to generating heat.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’ll start immediately.","└ All-Father: Truly... That forest has gone beyond fascinating and entered the realm of the mystical. To think it transitioned into winter overnight. Were there no traces of autumn?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not sure. It came so suddenly that I didn’t notice anything.","└ All-Father: I see. Still, the existence of winter means you are fortunate, Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: What do you mean by that?","└ All-Father: Winter is a period during which energy consumption increases drastically because of the cold. Creatures that inhabit regions where only winter exists are usually large, but those living in places with all four seasons tend to be smaller on average. This is especially true of insects.","└ Ah, I’ve heard of that. Places that are comfortable for humans are also comfortable for animals.","└ Isn’t Wyd like that? The insects there are fucking enormous, kekekeke.","└ Wyd is a country where fairies genuinely exist. It’s a terrifying place.","└ Suspiciously: That’s also why most of us beastfolk are so large... Still, it warms my heart whenever we have a bountiful harvest, kek. You people can’t grow corn, can you?","└ Fuck, I’m from the Central Plains, and all I can do is sigh. Why is all our land such garbage?","└ Garbage, my ass, kekeke. You’re the ones refusing to develop it because you claim to live in harmony with nature. Even the elves develop their land these days.","└ Didn’t elves have a nature-friendly image in the past?","└ Yeah, but once the Elven Queen took the throne, she started developing the country like crazy. That’s when their potential exploded.","└ The Elven Queen is genuinely insane. She can seize control of public opinion with a single speech and steer everyone in the direction she wants, kekeke.","└ Yeah. She knows exactly what the elves want. That makes her even scarier.","└ Even the Council of Elders united because they thought, \"That bitch is seriously fucking crazy,\" kekekeke.","Amid all the useless chatter about rumors and current affairs, the All-Father’s information particularly caught my attention.","Animals in regions that experienced winter tended to be smaller on average.","In other words, the region where I lived was inhabited by animals that were \"comparatively\" small.","’What the fuck? This is what a place with comparatively small animals looks like?’","Wonmo’s mother alone had been as enormous as a house.","The saber-toothed tiger had genuinely been about the size of a house.","If those counted as comparatively small, how enormous were the creatures elsewhere?","I couldn’t even imagine it.","A sense of futility washed over me. I wished I hadn’t asked.","’But there’s an even more serious problem...’","Food.","Still shivering, I headed outside.","There was something I hadn’t managed to check because of the extreme cold—the fish.","Worried that something might have happened to them, I looked inside the iron container.","\"Oh, great. I’m screwed.\"","Not only had the water in the container frozen solid, but so had the fish.","Natural frozen storage.","I could only sigh.","Title: Do I have to throw this away?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the fish frozen solid)","They froze completely in that short amount of time. Do I have to throw them away, or should I just extract their inner cores?","└ Heavenly Demon: There is no need to worry. If they possess inner cores, they will not freeze to death.","└ Wild Grylls: Is that even possible?","└ Heavenly Demon: They are called inner cores for a reason. You may trust me.","└ Sword Master: Do you really expect him to believe you when you blindly demand his trust? You should offer a more scientific explanation.","└ Wild Grylls: Can you provide one?","└ Sword Master: No. I’m a muscle-brained idiot who only ever studied martial arts, haha.","└ Wild Grylls: ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: As I recall, even your martial arts were rather unimpressive.","└ Sword Master: You fucking bi—","└ Heavenly Demon: What did you just say?","└ Sword Master: Head Moderator, the assistant moderator is abusing her authority. ;;","└ DontThrowAwayTheHero: Swearing was wrong too! But Heavenly Demon, please don’t do that again!","└ All-Father: As the Heavenly Demon said, if they possess inner cores, they should still be alive. They are likely not even hibernating, but simply continuing to live normally.","└ Wild Grylls: Can you explain that scientifically?","└ All-Father: Yes. Most fish that possess inner cores contain a substance called ardorotoxin, which... (omitted) ...and that is how it works.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh. I see.","└ Hmm. I understand perfectly.","└ I was actually just about to explain it myself.","└ The harvest of bullshit is plentiful this year, kekeke.","└ Says the bastards who couldn’t even get into the Academy, kekeke.","Without winter clothing, outdoor activity was almost impossible.","I was wearing both the uniform Cheonggu Princess had given me and the one I had received from King Leor, yet I was still cold.","If I hadn’t possessed even these, wouldn’t I have frozen to death already?","’Isn’t there some magical item that can warm up the inside of a room?’","The thought suddenly occurred to me, so I made another post in the Gallery.","I needed to warm the cave first before deciding whether I could venture outside.","Even then, food remained a concern.","For the moment, I couldn’t obtain any myself.","I would have to visit it to know for certain, but in weather this cold, the river had probably frozen solid too.","I still had smoked tiger meat, but I had no idea how long winter would last.","’Did those animals come to my cave yesterday because they were preparing for winter?’","It wasn’t entirely implausible.","Shivering, I added more wood to the campfire.","Title: Is there a magic item that can warm an entire room?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the campfire)","It’s still too cold with just a campfire. Isn’t there some kind of item that can warm an entire room?","└ Heavenly Demon: My bedchamber is always warm. I shall ask one of my aides and return.","└ Sword Master: Such items exist, but they usually only warm the sleeping area. We use fireplaces to heat entire houses.","└ Wild Grylls: Would it be difficult to heat the whole room with something like a crystal orb?","└ Passing Dwarf: You’d probably have to tear out the entire floor to do that. But there’s mithril beneath the floor of your cave, isn’t there?","└ Cheonggu Princess: The dwarf is right. If you’re going to use a crystal orb, it would be more efficient to renovate the house instead.","└ Wild Grylls: Then what would be the best option?","└ Passing Dwarf: You’d be better off building a fireplace. It’s easier to punch through the ceiling than the floor.","└ Wild Grylls: But that sounds hard...","└ Passing Dwarf: Then freeze to death, kek.","└ Wild Grylls: Sigh.","└ Passing Dwarf: I’ll upload some basic construction instructions. Follow those. It’s easy as long as you have bricks.","So I would have to punch a hole somewhere after all.","I let out a hollow laugh.","With winter attacking without warning, renovations had become essential.","’The ceiling is still the better option.’","If only because of the mithril, I couldn’t tear out the entire floor.","I thought about the materials I would need and began preparing.","[ Wild Grylls: Well, it’s better than nothing.]","[ Passing Dwarf: I’ll send you this and upload the post immediately, so keep an eye out.]","Before that, I received winter clothes from the dwarf.","They were only meant to serve as a temporary measure.","The clothes were made from fur and leather that looked warm at a glance.","The hat in particular was so large that \"voluminous\" seemed like the only appropriate word.","It resembled the kind of winter clothing a rifle-carrying hunter might wear.","\"Whew.\"","Once I put everything on, the cold became somewhat bearable.","There was nothing I could do about my freezing feet, though.","I would just have to wear a pair of thick socks. As luck would have it, the Gallery had a suitable pair available.","Now that I had winter clothing, the only remaining task was to install a fireplace in the cave.","The dwarf had said he would upload the post immediately, so I just needed to follow his instructions.","[ Passing Dwarf: Here are the winter clothes. I couldn’t give you shoes because I didn’t have any in your size.]","Title: Here are the fireplace plans. Take a look.","Passing Dwarf","(Photo of a fireplace cross-section diagram)","(Photo of a fireplace)","This should be enough, right? The principle itself is simple, so you should be able to build it quickly.","└ Wild Grylls: Thanks. But if I light a fire in it, I’ll need to seal the cave entrance too, right?","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah, obviously. Don’t bother trying to install a door. Just cover the entrance with thick cloth or leather. That’ll work better.","└ Wild Grylls: Okay.","The cross-section allowed me to understand the structure, aided by the dwarf’s explanation.","The construction itself wasn’t difficult.","The chimney was the problem.","I would have to seal the gaps between the bricks so that smoke couldn’t leak out.","I had used mud to seal the gaps in the bricks when constructing both the oven and the furnace.","And what did that mean?","Clang! Clang!","\"Argh! This is driving me insane!\"","It meant I had to suffer through the backbreaking task of digging into ground that had frozen solid.","Rain had fallen yesterday, followed by snow today, so the ground was practically ice rather than soil.","For a moment, I considered pouring hot water over it.","I quickly abandoned the idea.","I would only be creating more work for myself. Pouring water onto the ground in winter was sheer madness.","’I’ll have to dig it up with a pickaxe.’","In the end, I had no choice but to \"mine\" the soil with a pickaxe.","Why the hell was I being put through this?","After gathering all the soil I needed, I purchased a ladder from the auction house.","I needed it to climb above the cave’s ceiling and look for a suitable location.","The ladder I had previously bought for butchering was a folding ladder, so it wasn’t long enough.","The ladder I purchased this time was tall enough to reach high places.","’Somewhere around here...’","I was examining different parts of the ceiling in search of a suitable spot when a tiny white object gently landed on the back of my hand.","I couldn’t feel it because I was wearing gloves, but that didn’t matter.","Tap— Tap—","It wasn’t just one.","More white objects drifted down one after another.","I raised my head toward the sky.","Dark clouds had gathered without my noticing, completely obscuring the sun.","\"Wow...\"","Garbage was falling from the sky.","What a truly godforsaken place.","Perhaps the weather had read my mind.","Whoooooosh—!!!","\"Aaaaaaargh!!!\"","In the span of thirty seconds, the snow evolved into a full-blown blizzard.","’What the fuck did I do to deserve this?!’","It was so unfair I could die.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 134","paragraphs":["Winter (2)","I had thought this many times before, but God definitely hated me.","Otherwise, He wouldn’t have sent a blizzard specifically to stop me from renovating my home.","’But didn’t I hate Him first?’","I had spent my entire life blaming God because I didn’t want to hate people.","Had that snowball finally rolled all the way back to me?","Lost in this mixture of armchair philosophy and nonsense, I waited for the blizzard to stop.","The situation outside the cave was nothing short of a natural disaster. The entire landscape was buried in snow.","I had never experienced a blizzard even on Earth, so encountering one after coming here was absurd.","Title: Save me","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the blizzard raging outside the cave)","Now there’s a blizzard too. Somebody save me.","└ Heavenly Demon: What utter chaos. The weather does whatever it pleases.","└ Sword Master: The animals living there are fascinating too. How do they survive in such an environment?","└ Wild Grylls: I think they instinctively know what’s coming. Wonmo gaining weight proves it.","└ Heavenly Demon: Wonmo aside, did Fast Sloth show no changes?","└ Wild Grylls: Nope. Nothing in particular. It still has the same stupid expression.","└ Those creatures survived because they’ve adapted, kek.","└ I wonder what the gorillas are doing.","└ Eating bananas, probably.","└ What if yellow dust blows in during spring too? Kekeke.","└ Where would the sand come from?","└ The terrain across the river changes all the time. If it turns into a desert during the spring season, the dust could blow over from there.","└ That makes enough sense to be terrifying, kekekeke.","└ If yellow dust really comes, it’ll be legendary, kekeke.","A blizzard was already bad enough, but yellow dust in spring?","That would drive me completely insane.","The problem was that the possibility wasn’t merely nonzero—it was actually rather high.","This damned forest was a place where miracles manifested and the impossible became possible.","Even the sea and river had overturned common sense. There was no reason the weather would be any different.","’At least the blizzard has stopped.’","The blizzard that had descended as though determined to sweep everything away had completely vanished.","All it left behind was an even thicker layer of white garbage.","Thank goodness this wasn’t the military.","When garbage fell from the sky there, clearing it was a never-ending task.","’And I don’t know when another blizzard might come.’","I should hurry.","I grabbed my pickaxe and climbed onto the part of the ceiling I had previously selected.","I wasn’t going to break through the entire ceiling immediately. That would only create more work and waste time.","Clang! Clang! Crunch!","I opened only a small hole.","Then I stuck my face through it and looked down into the cave.","Fast Sloth was staring up at me with its usual vacant expression.","Now I simply had to use this hole as a starting point and gradually build the brickwork upward.","Before that, I should boil some water to thaw the soil—","’Ah. Right.’","I realized something belatedly.","I opened the valve connected to the hose to check whether water would come out.","Just as I had feared, nothing emerged despite the open valve.","The river had probably frozen.","Even if it hadn’t, the water inside the hose itself might have frozen solid.","’I’ll have to make water from snow.’","Fortunately, the recent blizzard meant I could use snow instead.","So much had accumulated in that short time that it squeaked beneath my feet.","While waiting for the water to boil, I decided to prepare the foundation for the fireplace.","The structure itself wasn’t difficult, but since it was my first time building one, I had every reason to proceed carefully.","’Before stacking the bricks, I need to start with the floor...’","I repaired the floor before laying any bricks.","I designed it so that the ashes wouldn’t pile up inside but would collect underneath, while fresh air could flow in smoothly from outside.","There were so many features to consider that I had to move repeatedly between the inside and outside of the cave.","However, temperature control was directly tied to my survival.","As long as it kept me from freezing to death, the effort was worthwhile.","People from warm regions might not understand, but winter was mercilessly harsh in most parts of the world.","You had to prepare for every threat while the weather was still warm.","Otherwise, you could die from hypothermia, starvation, or any number of other causes.","Since ancient times, Koreans had made such preparations during kimchi-making season.","There was even a saying:","’Every season is merely preparation for winter.’","As I began preparing for the cold, I also started worrying about various illnesses—especially the common cold.","’Why don’t humans have fur? Is it because fur catches fire easily?’","While wondering why humans lacked fur and were therefore so susceptible to colds, I decided to ask the All-Father about it later.","Anyway, I had finished digging the ground. All that remained was to stack the bricks.","Since I planned to apply mud between them like cement, I prepared hot water first.","I was boiling it outside so that I could also use it to thaw the surrounding ground.","\"Hm?\"","\"Kiyuuung...\"","But then I noticed a strange animal near the campfire.","At first, I thought it was a raccoon dog, but a closer look revealed that it wasn’t.","It was an animal often mistaken for a raccoon dog—an actual raccoon.","The raccoon was holding both hands toward the campfire to warm them.","It hadn’t entered the cave and was still outside, so I didn’t mind.","However, I planned to chase it away if it stayed too long.","’Or Fast Sloth will teach it a lesson.’","Just as I thought that and picked up the container of hot water, the raccoon glanced at me.","Then it stuck its hands into the campfire.","Literally into the fire.","I couldn’t help but jump in surprise.","That wouldn’t merely burn its hands. Its entire body could catch fire.","But what kind of place was this?","It was the Four Seasons Forest, where small creatures weren’t merely dangerous—they were downright horrifying.","Fwoosh!","The raccoon stared at its hands as they caught fire and began blazing.","Then it put them straight into its mouth.","It looked as though it were eating the flames.","By the time I had become too dumbfounded to speak, the raccoon proudly returned to the forest.","I couldn’t even begin to understand what I had just witnessed.","Did the fire inside its body act as some kind of heater?","’Right. Trying to understand would only hurt me.’","I had more than enough problems of my own.","I began constructing the fireplace as planned.","Lay down one row, apply mud.","Lay down another row, apply more mud.","The dwarf had warned me to make sure everything was firmly secured, so I inspected the brickwork meticulously.","I had originally intended to smear the mud on with my hands, but the weather was too cold, so I bought a tool instead.","After rummaging through the auction house, I found a trowel used for applying cement.","Once I tried it, I wondered how I could possibly have managed without it.","’Now all that’s left is the chimney...’","The chimney was the most difficult part.","It had to narrow as it extended upward.","Mud alone wouldn’t secure it properly as I built higher, so I needed another solution.","’I’ll need a frame.’","Since I was using mud instead of cement, the framework was important.","After considering my options, I purchased a suitably sized iron container from the auction house.","I then stepped outside to do the hammering. I didn’t want to wake Wonmo.","Slice! Slice! Slice!","First, I cut the iron container into flat panels.","A sword infused with aura was more than sufficient.","I then cut away the middle, leaving only the outer edges intact.","With that, the frame was complete.","It was shaped like a squared arch and made from thick iron, so it was sturdy.","’The size should be about right too.’","It would be fine as long as the smoke could escape properly.","If it collapsed...","Well, I would just have to build it more carefully next time.","This was the best I could do.","I continued stacking the bricks one by one until the chimney reached the hole in the ceiling.","The work inside the cave was finished, so I had to head outside again.","I needed to bring wet mud, bricks, a pickaxe, and finally, a hammer.","Crunch! Crack!","I widened the hole with the pickaxe and carefully refined its edges with the hammer.","Since I couldn’t work with perfect precision, the hole ended up wider than the chimney, but that was fine.","I had brought the mud specifically to seal the gaps.","Thanks to my spatial bag, I had been able to carry everything at once.","\"Good. Finished!\"","After neatly completing the chimney, my makeshift fireplace was finished.","A chimney sticking out of the top of a cave looked somewhat peculiar.","But the job wasn’t truly complete yet.","The most important thing was its performance.","I needed to test whether the fireplace worked properly.","\"Whew.\"","Had the weather grown even colder while I was working?","My breath emerged in a thicker white cloud than before.","I cleared all the stone fragments out of the fireplace and placed firewood inside.","Crackle! Pop! Crackle!","A fire sprang to life, creating a rather picturesque scene.","The sight alone warmed my heart, but I still wasn’t finished.","Cold air continued seeping in through the cave entrance.","I had to block that first.","’The dwarf said to cover it with some well-insulated cloth or leather, right?’","The tiger hide wasn’t nearly large enough.","For now, I would cover the entrance with several layers of large cloth.","This was the perfect opportunity since there was no blizzard.","If I secured them firmly with nails, they should block most of the wind.","Whenever a blizzard struck, I planned to weigh down the cloth hanging along the ground with rocks.","’It’s getting warmer now that the entrance is covered.’","This was why I had built the chimney.","I needed to close the entrance.","When I used an open campfire, leaving the entrance uncovered was the only relatively safe option. A fireplace was different.","I felt comfortable as the cave’s interior gradually grew warmer.","At some point, Fast Sloth had also approached the fireplace and begun warming itself.","\"Nice, isn’t it?\"","It nodded in response.","For some reason, that made me feel proud.","This was the perfect time to make a Gallery post.","I photographed the fireplace and uploaded the pictures.","Only then did I realize that building it had taken a full two hours.","I had been so focused on the construction that I hadn’t noticed the time passing.","Title: Finished building the fireplace","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the fire burning inside the fireplace)","(Photo of Fast Sloth staring blankly into the flames)","(Photo of Wonmo sleeping beside the fire after wandering over at some point)","This is the makeshift fireplace I spent two hours building. I think I’ll be able to get through winter without too much trouble, haha.","└ Heavenly Demon: I think this every time, but you are remarkably skilled with your hands. To think you could even construct a fireplace.","└ Sword Master: I agree. Were you always good at making things?","└ Wild Grylls: I used to be amazing at folding colored paper.","└ Does that really count as being good with your hands? ;;","└ Of course it does. I can know exactly how to fold something and still fail, kekeke.","└ Some people really are naturally gifted or hopeless with their hands.","└ Passing Dwarf: You did a pretty decent job. Did you apply mud between the bricks?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. I also cut and made the frame myself.","└ Passing Dwarf: Oh, nice. Did you check whether smoke is coming out of the chimney?","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t, but I’m sure it’s fine.","└ Passing Dwarf: Check immediately unless you want them to find your mysterious corpse tomorrow.","└ Wild Grylls: Sounds like a pain.","└ Passing Dwarf: Then die, kek.","It was annoying, but I checked and confirmed that smoke was escaping through the chimney.","Going outside also allowed me to feel just how drastic the temperature difference was.","The fireplace genuinely performed well. The inside of the cave was remarkably warm.","’I should rest for a while.’","Perhaps because I had poured all my concentration into building the fireplace, my body felt heavy with fatigue.","I should eat lunch before resting.","Naturally, I was having smoked meat.","All I had to do was warm it over the fireplace, making it extremely convenient.","’I’ll give the inner core to Fast Sloth. As for Wonmo... I guess I don’t need to give him any?’","Perhaps Wonmo had entered hibernation, because all he did was sleep.","Even while I worked, he remained curled into a ball, sleeping soundly.","I decided not to wake him.","He would get up when he was hungry.","After eating, I browsed the Gallery while waiting for my food to digest.","[ Chae-U vs. Beger: Kone scores the opening gooooooal!!! ]","’Oh. There was a match today?’","Coincidentally, Cheonggu Princess had uploaded a post about it.","I had been so busy lately that I had forgotten about today’s match.","Cheonggu Princess would probably feel a little disappointed.","I should at least leave a comment now.","I opened the post.","This is what an attacking line looks like! This is Chae-U! This is how you build an attack!! Do you understand now, you filthy Leor vermin?!","└ King Leor: Kekekeke, look how excited you are. You bastards can’t even qualify for the Champions League.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Yeah, well, you’re still going trophyless this season too~","└ King Leor: And have you lot lifted a trophy in the past ten years?","└ Cheonggu Princess: We’re winning the Devil Cup this time. Unlike a certain trophyless team, kek.","└ King Leor: You’ll still crash and burn next season. Enjoy this while you can.","└ Cheonggu Princess: (Video of Leor conceding the opening goal six minutes into the first half) Oh? What’s this? That goal positively reeks!","└ King Leor: When the fuck did Svi concede again? This is fucking bullshit.","Title: Chae-U vs. Beger: Kone scores the opening gooooooal!!!","Cheonggu Princess","(Video of a goal being scored five minutes into the first half)","└ Cheonggu Princess is seriously vicious, kekekeke.","└ Chae-U supporters have always been like that, kekeke.","└ Wild Grylls: There was a match today? I’ve been so busy that I didn’t know. Sorry. Let’s go, Chae-U!","└ Cheonggu Princess: Excellent! Now that the Saint has appeared, we’ll win again today! What score do you predict?","└ Wild Grylls: They often attack like that and then concede. Their defense is weak, so I’m predicting 4–2. Chae-U scores the four, by the way.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Four whole goals! Thank you!","└ King Leor: What score do you predict for us?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t watch Leor’s matches much, so I’m not sure, but I think you’ll lose. You threw away your lead in the last match too.","└ King Leor: Come on. You said something nice about Chae-U, so why us...?","└ Wild Grylls: You can clearly see their lack of concentration in the goal they just conceded.","└ Cheonggu Princess: How dare you doubt the Saint! How rude!","└ King Leor: Sigh. Svi’s stamina really has declined, so it’s hard to argue with that.","Cheonggu Princess and King Leor fought whenever there was a match.","Opposites attracted, as the saying went.","They supported different teams, but their personalities were remarkably similar.","Whoooooosh—!!!","Had another blizzard started outside while I was browsing the Gallery?","The cloth covering the entrance repeatedly swelled outward before settling down again.","The razor-sharp wind was an added bonus.","With the weather fluctuating so wildly, I should probably avoid outdoor activity for a while.","Rain was irritating enough, but a blizzard was an even greater disaster.","’I should practice my cultivation method.’","I spent an hour circulating my internal energy and another thirty minutes practicing swordsmanship.","By then, the matches should have been ending, so I checked the Gallery.","[ Chae-U vs. Beger: Final score 4–2! Chae-U wins despite showing defensive instability, exactly as the Saint predicted! ]","[ Leor vs. Balrog: Final score 0–2. Leor suffers a shocking defeat after showing signs of declining stamina. ]","Everything had unfolded exactly as I had predicted.","Naturally, countless users flocked to my comment to make their pilgrimages to the \"holy site.\"","I felt somewhat uneasy, but I dismissed it as a coincidence.","’More importantly...’","I looked at Fast Sloth, which was still staring blankly into the flames.","It hadn’t behaved like this when I used an ordinary campfire.","Why was it acting that way now?","\"Hey. You’ll ruin your eyes. Move back.\"","\"...\"","\"Come on. I said move back.\"","I felt as though I finally understood how my mother had felt when she tried to drag me away from the computer.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 135","paragraphs":["Winter (3)","Around the time Grylls’s activities became restricted by the untimely onset of winter, the world outside the Forest of Four Seasons was bustling for various reasons.","The Holy Kingdom and El Dorado were in an uproar over the investigation team and the Immortal King incident.","In Mephisto, the hooligans refused to accept the outcome of the match and were burning everything in sight.","Even the relatively peaceful nations remained active, each for its own reasons.","\"Are you the one who presented Us with a fully matured mandrake?\"","The man wore an expression that radiated weariness with everything in the world. Yet even that could not conceal his dignity.","His golden hair still shone without having lost its color, and his beard was immaculately groomed.","The very picture of a handsome middle-aged man spoke in an indifferent voice.","Though every conceivable trace of annoyance showed on his face, his solemn bearing was impossible to hide.","\"Y-yes! That is correct, Your Majesty.\"","Count Gorgon, standing opposite him, bowed deeply as he answered.","A short distance away from Count Gorgon stood Arnold, a handsome young man with golden hair, watching the exchange.","\"Raise your head. You are practically Our savior.\"","\"I-I am deeply honored, Your Majesty.\"","\"There is no need for that. So, what is it that you desire?\"","The middle-aged man who discarded the preamble and went straight to the point was named Robert.","Robert Louis Messiah II, Emperor of the Messiah Empire.","Despite the curious reputation of being an \"emperor suited only for domestic affairs,\" he wielded immense authority.","In truth, being suited for domestic affairs meant possessing outstanding administrative ability—something impossible without tremendous power.","It was precisely because he held such fearsome authority that he had been able to steadily strengthen the foundations of the Messiah Empire.","\"Th-this humble servant desires nothing. I am satisfied simply knowing that Your Majesty has recovered your health.\"","\"Is that so? Very well. We shall consider a reward appropriate for you. You may withdraw.\"","\"May Your Majesty enjoy a long and healthy life.\"","Count Gorgon bowed deeply once more before departing.","His tactful wish for the emperor’s longevity was an added touch, rather than a conventional farewell.","Even at those considerate words, Robert maintained his impassive expression.","Soon, only Robert and Arnold remained in the emperor’s bedchamber.","Robert remained silent for some time, while Arnold stood still and waited for his father to speak.","\"...My son.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","\"You have truly done something unnecessary.\"","Robert finally spoke amid the heavy silence, his words tinged with reproach.","Arnold flinched and stole a glance at him.","Perhaps lost in thought, Robert merely stared up at the ceiling.","\"Thanks to you, my plan has fallen apart.\"","\"What plan... do you mean?\"","\"...\"","Robert did not answer. His attitude made it clear that he did not want to explain.","He then looked at the bewildered Arnold and quietly spoke.","\"You said this item came from the Gallery?\"","\"Yes. That is... correct.\"","\"The Gallery truly has all manner of things. And to think this came from the Forest of Four Seasons...\"","Robert stroked his beard as though pondering something deeply, then continued.","\"What did you say his name was? Count Golla?\"","\"Count Gorgon.\"","\"Right, of course. Leave this matter entirely to him. I have something else I must do.\"","\"And what would that be...?\"","\"I must prepare your succession ceremony.\"","\"...\"","Arnold’s eyes widened.","Robert had spoken calmly, but the content of his words was anything but calm.","A succession ceremony meant that the throne would be passed down.","It meant Arnold would soon ascend as emperor.","Arnold was briefly exhilarated that the moment he had long desired was finally approaching, but he soon brought his excitement under control.","His experiences thus far had taught him that excitement could ruin everything.","\"I shall have the succession ceremony prepared within a month. Things will become quite busy.\"","\"Father, I am not yet—\"","\"Even after consuming the mature mandrake, my health is not what it once was. It is becoming difficult for me to endure.\"","Robert cut Arnold off before he could finish.","Arnold inwardly cheered, but patiently waited for Robert to continue.","\"So you must prepare yourself thoroughly as well. Recent developments in the Holy Kingdom are concerning, and Alvenheim’s movements are equally suspicious.\"","\"I will remain vigilant.\"","\"If you overcome these difficulties, you may become an even greater emperor than I.\"","\"That is not true. You have strengthened the very foundations of the empire, Father.\"","\"That was all thanks to Ash.\"","\"Pardon?\"","Arnold’s eyes widened, wondering if he had misheard.","\"Cough! Cough! Cough!\"","Of course, when Robert broke into a violent coughing fit, Arnold’s doubts immediately turned to concern.","Startled, Arnold turned to summon the imperial physician.","Before he could, however, Robert raised a hand to stop him.","\"Cough. It is nothing. A minor cough is unavoidable at my age.\"","\"Father...\"","\"In any event, the empire has no shortage of talented people, so there is no need to worry about internal affairs. If necessary, you can write a letter to the former captain of the Imperial Guard.\"","There was only one person he could mean by the former captain of the Imperial Guard.","Ash Menethil, the strongest sword in the empire and a warrior who possessed Swordmaster as an official title.","Though he had currently entered a state of partial seclusion, he was someone who would gladly heed Robert’s request.","The emperor had been Ash’s patron and had supported him wholeheartedly, while Ash had repaid that kindness in full.","Someone had flooded the Gallery with invaluable tips, causing the continent’s average combat strength to rise, but that was no cause for concern.","Ash’s reputation alone ensured that no one would dare treat the empire lightly.","\"So you need only focus on external affairs. The situation appears to be growing increasingly serious.\"","\"Yes, I understand.\"","\"Then withdraw. I wish to be alone.\"","\"The imperial physician...\"","\"I shall summon him myself.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","Arnold bowed and left the bedchamber, leaving Robert alone.","Robert blinked in silence for a while before eventually releasing a sigh.","Then, with a wistful look unlike any he had shown before, he muttered softly,","\"I didn’t want to work...\"","It was the grumbling of an office worker exhausted by his job.","And that was not all.","\"Why did something like a mature mandrake have to exist...? I was planning to enjoy a comfortable retirement...\"","Robert muttered in a voice filled with irritation and weariness toward everything in the world.","Had his health truly deteriorated?","To some extent, yes.","But he was not bedridden to the point that he could barely attend to his duties.","It was closer to malingering—though his act did involve actual poison.","He had consumed a poison that caused symptoms resembling a cold but had no lasting effect on his health.","He had also informed the imperial physician beforehand, allowing them to make his condition appear far more serious than it truly was.","The reason he had gone to such lengths was simple.","He did not want to work.","The position of emperor—or king, for that matter—inevitably came with overwork.","Robert had been unable to escape it either, and in the end, he had resorted to this.","One might say he lacked a sense of responsibility as emperor, but it was not truly a problem.","He had already transferred the entirety of state affairs to his son, Arnold.","Only the succession ceremony remained, yet he had been unable to endure even that long and had taken to his bed.","I only hope El Dorado and Alvenheim don’t start any trouble during the next month.","With several troublesome factions already causing chaos, Robert wanted the succession ceremony completed as quickly as possible.","He would have to work again for that to happen. The mere thought was horrifying.","After briefly growing distressed over all the work awaiting him, Robert looked into the air.","As he did, a window floated into view.","It was the Gallery, which his son Arnold had also recently begun enjoying.","Those were good times.","What had Robert been doing while pretending to be ill—though technically not entirely pretending?","He had been amusing himself on the Gallery.","Even a dignified emperor could not resist a secret indulgence.","In fact, after working so diligently all those years, he had become absorbed in the Gallery as a way of rewarding himself.","I want to live like that too.","Why did he have to be the emperor?","He did not mind the nickname \"emperor suited only for domestic affairs,\" but why did he have to be emperor in the first place?","Why had his father only sired one son?","All sorts of thoughts crossed his mind.","While browsing the Gallery, Robert found a post by someone who had recently gained considerable fame.","Title: The fast sloth is zoning out by the fire","Wild Grylls","(The fast sloth staring into the fire)","This little bastard was zoning out in front of the fire, so I tried to pull him away, but he wouldn’t budge.","Even when I forcibly dragged him away, he went straight back. Some of his fur has already been singed, but he’s still doing this. LOL","└ Heavenly Demon: Strangely adorable. It seems to understand how precious warmth is.","└ SwordMaster: The fast sloth has an unexpectedly cute side to it.","└ Starlight Princess: Is Wonmo there too? I want to see him.","└ Wild Grylls: (Wonmo sleeping curled into a ball) Here he is.","└ He’s seriously adorable every time I see him. LOL","└ Isn’t he waking up? Is he actually hibernating?","Wild Grylls was said to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","His daily records had recently become Robert’s favorite reading material.","Robert wanted nothing from Grylls. As emperor, he already possessed everything a man could have.","I’m strangely envious.","He was simply envious of the life Grylls was currently living.","It was not entirely raw survival, since he received bits of support here and there, but he was still living in the wilderness.","Robert wanted to live that way too.","He wanted to build an oven, hunt, and catch fish.","He finally understood why people wanted to take up farming as they grew older. After living such a busy life, they began to yearn for freedom.","Not absolute freedom, but freedom earned through one’s own efforts—a life where every action produced a direct result.","Now that Robert had entered middle age, reading Grylls’s posts only intensified that desire.","It would be nice if my safety could be guaranteed...","Of course, Grylls’s objective was survival and escape, not simply enjoying life in the wilderness.","Robert, on the other hand, wanted the wilderness lifestyle without any of the danger.","Whenever Grylls found himself in peril, Robert nearly had a heart attack.","I suppose I’ll have to settle for living vicariously through him.","For that to happen, Grylls could not die.","The Gallery was perfect for filling the loneliness of his life.","And so Robert made his decision.","In another month, he would be free from the burden of being emperor.","Until then, he would provide Grylls with whatever support he could.","First, I need to create a registered username...","A short while later, Robert came up with:","[AbsolutezZoneRobertIsAwesome]","\"Heh-heh.\"","It was a username that perfectly demonstrated that the apple did not fall far from the tree.","His son already used the same name, which only made it better.","Chuckling to himself, Robert tried to register it.","[This username has already been registered.]","Robert was momentarily speechless.","Someone is actually using an idiotic fucking username like this?","His son was.","****","The fast sloth had caused me plenty of trouble by staring into the fire all day, but I had decided to let it go.","No matter how much I struggled with him, I was the only one who suffered.","It was better to leave him alone.","Surely the fast sloth would move away from the campfire eventually.","That was what I told myself.","Whoooooosh!!!","Regardless, the blizzard was still raging outside.","Part of me wanted to pull aside the flapping cloth and take a look, but I restrained myself.","If I did that and the cloth tore free from its fastenings, it would be a disaster.","In the end, I had no choice but to remain inside the cave all day.","Considering that it had rained yesterday, I had effectively spent nearly two days trapped inside.","What would I have done if I hadn’t smoked the meat?","I ate smoked meat for dinner, while the fast sloth ate one of the inner cores I had stored away.","Weather this goddamned awful might continue, so I would probably have to go hunting again soon.","If that proved impossible, I would have to rely on fish.","Whatever I caught, smoking it would be essential.","If the blizzard stops tomorrow, I’m going to have a rough time.","Just how much snow would accumulate?","I was a little worried.","To bring the day to a close, I added more firewood to the campfire.","Ordinarily, one person would have to remain awake to keep it burning, but that was difficult in my current situation.","All I could do was pile on as much firewood as possible.","Isn’t there some kind of device that can automatically feed firewood into a fire?","Something like that would be perfect.","I went to sleep and brought the day to an end.","And then the next morning arrived.","\"...You still haven’t slept?\"","The campfire was still blazing.","And, of course, the fast sloth was still sitting in front of it.","Had this little guy actually been adding firewood throughout the night?","I was dumbfounded.","Still, thanks to him, I stayed warm.","The cloth was no longer flapping, so it seemed the blizzard had stopped sometime during the night.","I pushed against the curtain to check the situation outside.","It stopped dead.","\"Huh?\"","Something was wrong.","Why would the curtain not move?","I had even removed the stones holding it in place, yet something was clearly amiss.","For a moment, I wondered if the curtain itself had frozen solid, but that was not it.","When I pulled it backward instead of pushing it out, it came away without resistance.","\"...What the hell is this?\"","Behind the curtain was a pure white wall.","At first, I had no idea what I was looking at, but it did not take long for me to realize the truth.","\"Oh.\"","It was all snow.","Snow that had been compressed into a solid mass.","Just how much snow had fallen for it to block the entire cave entrance?","I was utterly bewildered.","But there was an even greater problem—one directly related to my survival.","How am I supposed to clear all of this?","As though having garbage fall from the sky were not bad enough—","Bam! Bang!","\"Aaaaaaargh!!!\"","—it also taught me just how precious time was.","I furiously \"mined\" through the snow with my pickaxe as I shouted,","\"Someone’s in here!!!\"","I was beginning to hate winter.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 136","paragraphs":["Disaster (1)","Title: I’m fucked.","(A photo of the cave entrance completely blocked by snow)","It appears that I’m fucked.","That is the conclusion I reached after careful consideration.","I’m fucked.","└ Heavenly Demon: Is all of that snow?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It’s hardened from the cold, so I’m digging through it with a pickaxe.","└ Heavenly Demon: Would it not be easy to excavate with sword energy?","└ Wild Grylls: I can, but no matter how much I dig, more snow keeps falling from above. I have no idea how much has accumulated.","└ SwordMaster: Isn’t that dangerous? What if you run out of oxygen?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m surviving thanks to the chimney I opened yesterday. It looks like the fast sloth kept adding firewood, so all the snow around it melted.","└ SwordMaster: It feels like the fast sloth has saved your life several times now.","└ Why do those sentences sound so literary?","└ Just three sentences perfectly convey how fucked he is. LOL","└ There’s profanity in it, but it somehow doesn’t even feel like swearing. LOL","└ Can snow really pile up that high? Is this another effect of the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ No. Places with heavy snowfall are often like that. Apparently, the snow frequently piles up as high as the doors.","└ Just look at northern Messiah. I heard the people there shovel snow every day. LOL","└ I’m from the north, and clearing snow is more irritating than subjugating monsters. It really is garbage falling from the sky.","└ All-Father: Even so, that is an abnormal amount of snowfall. It should be difficult for that much to accumulate overnight.","└ Wild Grylls: No matter how much I dig, more snow keeps pouring down from above.","└ All-Father: A word of advice: why not spend the time you are using on the Gallery digging through the snow instead? This appears dangerous.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m still digging while posting.","Though \"mining\" with a pickaxe would be more accurate than digging with a shovel, I was working hard.","The problem was that I had no idea how much snow had accumulated above me. Every time I dug some out, more came cascading down to fill the space again.","If the fast sloth had not added firewood throughout the night, the chimney would have become blocked too.","If the chimney—my only source of oxygen—had been buried as well...","I did not even want to imagine it.","The fast sloth was an enormous help not only in combat, but in everyday life as well.","But if it snows this much, can the other animals even survive?","And not just the animals.","I had to wonder whether the plants could survive either.","Nothing should have been able to grow properly beneath this much snow.","Yet countless trees stood tall enough to form an entire forest.","Either they possessed enough vitality to withstand the snow, or there was some other explanation.","If winter in the forest is already this awful, how fucked up must the other environments be?","The forest supposedly had a relatively \"ordinary\" climate, yet it had become like this.","The snowy mountains and desert could only be worse.","The rainforest where the gorillas lived was probably no different.","It made no sense for only my territory to be this extreme.","I’ll never finish if I just keep digging blindly.","I briefly considered climbing out through the chimney, but quickly abandoned the idea.","The chimney was not especially wide. If I became wedged inside, it would be a disaster.","I was better off seeing this through and excavating the snow blocking the entrance.","I have to clear the entrance before it snows again.","If another snowfall came now, I might be trapped inside this cave for the rest of my life.","Even the chimney was no guarantee of safety.","Actually, forget the chimney. I was worried about the cave itself.","Once snow accumulated, its weight became tremendous.","Could this cave withstand the weight of all that snow?","Especially after I had slightly modified it to install the chimney?","I could not simply sit around doing nothing.","\"Fortunately, I have plenty of firewood.\"","I removed the curtain that had covered the entrance and lit another campfire.","The snow had frozen solid, so I decided to melt it with fire.","Of course, I was not going to sit around and wait. Once the snow had melted to a certain point, I would resume digging.","Crack! Thud!","As time passed, the snow softened and became easier to excavate.","I remained cautious, since melting snow could flow down and extinguish the campfire.","Who knew how much time had passed?","Eventually, the cavity no longer refilled whenever I removed more snow.","At last, the end was in sight.","\"Whew!\"","After all that labor with the pickaxe and shovel, I could finally see the result.","I had somehow managed to remove all the snow filling the cave entrance.","But that only applied to the entrance itself.","The surrounding area was another matter entirely.","Even directly outside the cave, the snow stood far above my head. Elsewhere, it had accumulated even higher.","People in Russia and Canada live in places like this?","How did they manage?","I was genuinely curious.","As I stared at the space I had cleared around the cave entrance, I suddenly remembered my time in the military.","I remembered shoveling whenever it snowed and scattering calcium chloride to prevent the ground from freezing.","Does this world even have a term for calcium chloride?","This world used alchemy rather than chemistry.","Historically, chemistry had developed from alchemy.","But considering how effective elixirs were, alchemy here was probably every bit as advanced as chemistry.","Wouldn’t producing calcium chloride be relatively simple?","If that isn’t possible, I can always use salt.","I had once heard that ordinary salt could be scattered in place of calcium chloride.","Something about it being more beneficial despite concerns over environmental damage.","I’ll ask about it after I finish working. For now, let’s spread some salt.","Salt was available through the auction house.","It was expensive, but it was an essential survival resource with plenty of demand, so it was never out of stock.","I proceeded section by section, scattering salt over the ground exposed by my shovel before clearing the next area.","Fortunately, it did not begin snowing again, allowing me to set up additional campfires along the way.","Still, I had to figure out how to keep this path clear and secure enough space to move around.","At this rate, I’ll need to build an emergency exit, not just a chimney.","It seemed I would soon need to borrow the wisdom of people who lived in cold regions.","I did not know how long this winter would last, but it did not seem likely to end anytime soon.","It was nearly lunchtime by the time I finished clearing the area around my shelter.","This isn’t a barren snowy mountain. There are definitely plants here...","I pondered the mystery while removing the snow covering the oven and furnace.","As I had already noted, animals and plants should not have been able to survive under this much snow.","The place should have been as barren as a snowy mountain.","There was no way these conditions would remain unchanged forever.","Perhaps everything would return to normal as early as tomorrow.","I had not been here long, and so many dramatic things had happened that I could not help forming all sorts of theories.","If the season could abruptly change to winter, perhaps it could just as suddenly become summer.","Imagining this immense amount of snow melting away offered me some comfort.","But imagination was imagination, and reality was reality.","It might snow again, so I should move everything I can into the cave.","The iron drum filled with frozen fish, the bellows, and all my assorted tools—everything that could be moved.","I could not relocate the makeshift oven or furnace, so I had no choice but to leave them outside.","They were unlikely to collapse under the snow, and even if they did, I could always rebuild them.","Or so I reassured myself.","With that, my winter preparations and precautions against isolation were nearly complete.","I had finally found a moment to rest and was about to open the Gallery when—","Ruuuuumble—","An ominous sound reached my ears, and the ground trembled faintly.","The moment I felt the noise and vibration, I rushed into the cave without hesitation.","Then, keeping my composure, I picked up my sword and shield.","My objective was not to take shelter, but to prepare myself. It was a lesson I had learned during my time here.","It was better to prepare like this than sit around waiting for whatever fate had in store for me.","Rustle—","Just before I left, the fast sloth reached out to me.","Did he want to come along?","But the fast sloth had to watch over the hibernating Wonmo.","I deliberately ignored his outstretched hand and stepped outside the cave.","Ruuuuumble!","The noise and vibrations had grown even stronger.","What in the world was coming?","Judging from its momentum, it had to be moving quickly.","That made me even more tense. I had no idea what might suddenly appear.","Just in case, I began circulating my mana and even manifested my aura.","After concentrating on the noise and vibrations for some time, I finally realized where they were coming from.","Behind... the cave?","It was coming from the exact opposite direction of the entrance.","The instant I realized that, I whipped my head around.","It was strange that the disturbance was coming from behind the cave rather than the forest, but this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","Nothing that appeared here could truly be considered strange.","Even if it was—","Rrrrrumble!","—not a living creature, but a natural disaster.","\"Oh, fu—\"","At the sight of the avalanche surging from behind the cave like a tidal wave, I experienced the illusion that time had slowed.","In that brief moment, I glanced down and saw the fast sloth looking up at me from inside the cave.","His expression seemed to say, This is why you should have listened to me instead of going out alone, you idiot.","When he had reached out earlier, he had not been asking to come with me.","He had been trying to stop me.","Roooooar!!","\"Gah! Urgh! Uwaaagh!\"","No matter how powerful an animal might be, it was helpless before the forces of nature.","The same applied to me.","I hurriedly drove my sword into the ground, but it was useless.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword was simply too effective.","Rather than anchoring me, it sliced straight through the ground as the avalanche swept me away.","Its effectiveness had backfired at the worst possible moment.","W-wasn’t I being swept toward the river?","Even amid the confusion of being carried away by the avalanche, I forced myself to remember the direction.","This avalanche was heading toward the river.","And the space beyond the river changed constantly.","This was dangerous.","One wrong move, and I might never be able to return to my shelter.","Not the sword—the shield...!","I flailed with my shield instead of the Heavenly Demon’s sword, hoping it would catch on a branch or anything else.","With most of my body already buried beneath the snow, it was closer to a desperate struggle than a calculated maneuver.","Still, I had to do something.","When it came to survival, you had to try whatever you could.","Jerk!","The result of my desperate effort came quickly.","I did not know which tree I had caught on, but I could clearly feel my clothes snagging against something.","I had been prepared to abandon the Heavenly Demon’s sword if necessary, but fortunately, I stopped at just the right moment.","\"Mmmphhh!!\"","Of course, that did not change the fact that the avalanche continued battering my entire body.","I endured and endured, waiting for it to end.","\"Pwah!\"","After what felt like an eternity, the avalanche finally passed.","Ordinarily, an avalanche would leave snow piled everywhere, but strangely, this one had swept all of it away.","Thanks to that, I was not buried beneath a snowdrift and could breathe normally.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","I coughed and looked around.","The avalanche seemed to have carried away all the accumulated snow, exposing the bare earth beneath it.","Before anything else, I needed to figure out where I was.","If I had crossed the river, it would be the worst possible outcome.","I’m not across the river.","Apparently, I had snagged on a tree near the river.","I could see the frozen river from where I was, confirming it.","On the other side was terrain utterly different from this place—a pure white, snow-covered mountain.","An immense amount of snow covered the mountain as well.","The avalanche that had just passed had clearly gone in that direction.","Had the snow moved on its own?","Or had the forest expelled it?","I could not tell.","Was the terrain around here even capable of producing an avalanche in the first place?","Was there a mountain nearby?","This was confusing.","Perhaps the forest was literally alive and had cleansed itself.","With weather this awful, no plants would remain if the forest could not purify itself somehow.","It would have become just like the snowy mountain across the river.","It was a highly plausible theory.","If even the forest is like this, what the hell is happening in the other regions?","I was becoming increasingly frightened.","I quickly gathered myself and returned to the cave.","\"...Ah.\"","There, I was greeted by the devastated remains of my shelter’s yard.","Not only had the barricade been swept away, but so had the makeshift furnace and oven.","I could rebuild the furnace and oven, but the barricade was a serious problem.","So this is why there’s no civilization here.","Civilization could never develop when everything was regularly swept away.","While Grylls was filming a disaster movie all by himself—","Whoooooosh!!","—another disaster was unfolding in the grasslands of the Forest of Four Seasons.","The region naturally had distinct wet and dry seasons, so heavy rain during the wet season was to be expected.","But what would happen if far too much rain fell?","It was still a grassland, so wouldn’t the earth absorb it all?","\"Blub! Blub!\"","\"Groooan! Grooan!\"","It did not.","An actual flood had struck the grasslands, harming countless animals.","Those who suffered the most were the animals unable to find shelter—particularly the young.","Still small and weak, they were simply swept away.","\"Hmm.\"","There was someone observing the scene in real time.","It was Ludwig.","He was still wearing his heavy armor to preserve his defenses.","\"So that is why this animal has such long legs.\"","\"...\"","He was currently sitting atop a giraffe, using it to escape the disaster.","Giraffes were ordinarily known for having foul tempers, but this one did not attack Ludwig.","The bumps on its head had given it enough intelligence to judge him harmless.","I would have been in serious trouble without this animal.","Sitting on the giraffe’s back, Ludwig looked up at its face.","The giraffe stood calmly even amid the flooded grasslands.","It had merely moved beneath a massive tree to escape the rain for a while, remaining steadfast and composed.","Boom! Thud! Thud!","Then a thunderous noise reached Ludwig’s ears, accompanied by vibrations that shook the ground.","When he turned toward the source, he witnessed a sight that was difficult to believe.","Thud! Boom! Thud!","It was a turtle.","Not a sea turtle, but a tortoise.","Instead of an ordinary shell, it carried an enormous mountain upon its back.","Naturally, a creature capable of carrying a mountain was itself terrifyingly immense.","As the rain poured down heavily enough to flood the grasslands, animals climbed onto the tortoise’s back.","Had Grylls seen it, he would have called it a living Noah’s Ark.","\"...\"","Ludwig silently watched the tortoise lumber onward before turning his head away.","People can actually survive in a place like this?","Ludwig was becoming increasingly curious about Grylls.","The irony was that Grylls’s entire yard had just been swept away.","I should find shelter on higher ground. I have an excellent steed, so it should be manageable.","It was a giraffe, not a horse.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]}]);
